docs/rtl-gap-assessment.md:98:| A4 Auto-format | W-3 (verible-verilog-format, svformat) | — (vendors ship style checkers, not formatters) | **ABSENT** | Deterministic formatting makes diffs reviewable and idempotent re-runs stable. |
docs/rtl-gap-assessment.md:99:| A5 Templates/style knowledge | W-7 (snippets, TerosHDL templates; style guides in W-1) | — | **ABSENT** | Skill-level knowledge raises first-pass quality of FIFO/FSM/ALU boilerplate. |
docs/rtl-gap-assessment.md:100:| B1 Simulation run gate | W-9 (Verilator, Icarus) | W-10 (VCS, Xcelium, Questa) | **ABSENT** | Loop step 3. No pass/fail capture means generated RTL is never executed. Blocking. |
docs/rtl-gap-assessment.md:102:| B3 Coverage evidence | W-13/W-15 (verilator_coverage, covergroups) | W-14 (VCS `urg`, IMC, vcover) | **ABSENT** | Coverage-gap feedback ("which states never exercised") drives testbench improvement. |
docs/rtl-gap-assessment.md:103:| B4 Assertions (SVA) execution | W-16 (Verilator `--assert`, SymbiYosys formal) | full SVA/PSL + assertion debug | **PARTIAL** (write-only) | Assertions are only worth what a run gate checks; today they are dead text. |
docs/rtl-gap-assessment.md:104:| B5 UVM execution | W-17 (uvm-core, uvm-verilator, pyuvm) | full UVM + VIP | **PARTIAL** (write-only) | Verification-assistant mode needs `+UVM_TESTNAME` runs + report (HTML/XML) parsing, not just codegen. |
docs/rtl-gap-assessment.md:105:| B6 Python TB (cocotb) | W-18 (cocotb; strongest OS automation surface) | — | **ABSENT** | cocotb+pytest is the cheapest high-value path to automated, agent-friendly TB loops. |
docs/rtl-gap-assessment.md:106:| B7 Regression automation | W-19/W-20 (SVUnit, VUnit, rtl_buddy) | vManager, Questa verify | **PARTIAL** | Generic orchestration exists; what is missing is the RTL-aware runner (test lists → logs → JUnit/coverage). |
docs/rtl-gap-assessment.md:107:| B8 Formal verification | W-21 (SymbiYosys `sby`, yosys `equiv_*`) | W-22 (JasperGold, VC Formal, Conformal/Formality) | **ABSENT** | `sby` proves small properties end-to-end with counterexample VCD — a later-stage amplifier. |
docs/rtl-gap-assessment.md:108:| C1 Synthesis | W-23 (Yosys + ABC, slang frontend) | W-24 (DC, Genus, Vivado/Quartus) | **ABSENT** | Closes the RTL→netlist leg; enables `equiv_*` LEC and "does it synthesize" gating. |
docs/rtl-gap-assessment.md:109:| C2 SDC + STA | W-25/W-26 (OpenSTA, OpenTimer) | PrimeTime, (DC/Genus STA) | **ABSENT** | Timing feedback (slack reports) turns synthesis runs into actionable fixes. |
docs/rtl-gap-assessment.md:110:| C3 CDC verification | — (no mature open CDC lint; W-28) | W-28 (SpyGlass CDC, Questa CDC, JasperGold CDC) | **ABSENT** | Cross-clock bugs are the highest-value lint class for SoC work; open track cannot close this — commercial, user-env only. |
docs/rtl-gap-assessment.md:114:| D2 CI/regression gates | W-32 (GH Actions/GitLab CI + open tools) | Jenkins + vManager/Questa verify | **PARTIAL** | dsh-qa proves the evidence discipline; it just has no RTL case to gate on yet. |
docs/rtl-gap-assessment.md:116:| D4 Version control | W-34 (Git/LFS, SVN, pre-commit lint) | SOS bridges | **PRESENT** | git-master + svn-master skills cover both common EDA VCS backends. |
docs/rtl-gap-assessment.md:117:| D5 Agent orchestration of the whole flow | W-36 (MCP wrappers, pyvcd/vcdvcd, pyverilog) | — | **PARTIAL** | This is the exact integration surface my-power-dsh consumes; substrate present, RTL gates absent. |
