evidence/agent-teams/scheduler-wakeup-fix/2026-09-10T10-16-23Z/captain-session-f333e946.jsonl:411:{"type":"assistant/chunk","seq":9697,"time":1789026768285,"data":{"turn":1,"step":6,"chunk":{"type":"block-end","index":0,"block":{"type":"reasoning","text":"The momus spawn failed because the read-only deny filter names tools that don't exist in this harness (\"str_replace_editor\", \"apply_patch\"). This is an interesting finding — a real defect in the mpd-roles plugin's read-only discipline for this harness! Worth noting as a discovered defect (relevant to \"遍历工程，了解工程详细信息\" — understanding the project deeply). It means `mpd_role_spawn` for read-only roles is currently BROKEN in this harness.\n\nSimilarly, `mpd_workmate_spawn` READONLY_DENY includes \"write\", \"edit\", \"str_replace_editor\", \"apply_patch\", \"mpd_hashline_edit\" — for a readonly base, toolFilter deny would fail in the same way if the harness rejects unknown names. That's important for the workmate task! Actually that's a bug that affects the workmate spawn path too (readonly workmates can't spawn). Let me verify how toolFilter is applied — but mpd-workmate READONLY_DENY also contains str_replace_editor/apply_patch which are not known tools here. So mpd_workmate_spawn for a readonly workmate would fail identically. This is a genuine defect discovered during traversal — very relevant to the user's \"遍历工程，了解工程详细信息\" and to the optimization work.\n\nLet me quickly verify by grepping the workmate test for readonly spawn, and check the roles plugin file that defines the deny list.\n\nMeanwhile, fall back for the requirements conference: use a non-readonly specialist? Or use `subagent` (plain) to get the adversarial questions. Simpler: use the `subagent` tool with a Plan-Reviewer-style prompt (it has no deny filter issue). Let me do that in background while I verify the deny-list defect.\n\nActually — the conference questions matter for the user Q&A. Let me fire the subagent (background) and in parallel verify the deny-list defect.\n\nNote the plan: I should also consider adding a repair task for this deny-list defect into the DAG (it's directly related: readonly workmate spawn is broken → and the workmate system optimization). But is it in scope of the user's ask? The user asked to optimize the workmate system: rename + delete. Fixing the readonly deny list is a genuine defect adjacent to it (mpd_workmate_spawn with a readonly base). I'll surface it to the user as a question/option in the requirements batch: include the fix or not.\n\nLet me now:\n1. Fire subagent for adversarial requirements questions (background).\n2. Verify the deny-list/toolFilter defect concretely: grep for READONLY_DENY in roles plugin + check dsh tools.restrict behavior + whether mpd_workmate_spawn readonly is covered by existing tests.\n\nLet me check the test file — does it test readonly spawn? Let me look at lines 134-160."}}}}
