evidence/agent-teams/scheduler-wakeup-fix/2026-09-10T10-16-23Z/captain-session-f333e946.jsonl:650:{"type":"user/message","seq":14735,"time":1789026874016,"data":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Background subagent 8fdfdfd4-308b-4ab3-b12f-21bf5997f1ae finished and will do no further work unless you send it more."},{"type":"text","text":"Its closing message:"},{"type":"text","text":"## (1) USER QUESTIONS — only the human can decide\n\n**Q1 AUTHORITY / SURFACE.** Rename + delete as agent-callable tools (`mpd_workmate_rename`/`_delete`), GUI-only human actions, or both?\n- Why: the library is the agent's own durable cross-project memory; an agent tool lets any captain/teammate autonomously destroy months of evolved persona+memory.\n- Candidates: (a) both, destructive call requires explicit `confirm:\"<name>\"`; (b) both, unguarded; (c) GUI-only, no agent tools; (d) tools only, no GUI change.\n\n**Q2 DELETE REVERSIBILITY.** Hard `rm -rf` or recoverable?\n- Why: memory.md is accumulated evidence that cannot be regenerated from the base template; one mis-click loses it permanently.\n- Candidates: (a) hard delete; (b) move to `~/.mpd/workmate/.trash/<name>-<ISO>/` (restorable, hidden from list); (c) tombstone rename, dir kept, hidden; (d) hard delete behind typed-name confirmation.\n\n**Q3 RENAME SEMANTIC SCOPE.** What exactly moves, and does the workmate's own text follow?\n- Why: the name is embedded in artifacts — `autoNote()` writes `<baseName>-based workmate \"<name>\".` into note.md, and persona/memory may quote the old name.\n- Candidates: (a) dir + meta.name + index key only (stale note text accepted); (b) also rewrite the auto-note self-reference; (c) also append a `## Renamed <old> → <new>` memory entry and/or a `renamedFrom` field; (d) grep-replace the old name through persona/memory. Sub-question: does rename bump `updatedAt` (it re-sorts the list)? (Does not bump `uses`.)\n\n**Q4 LIVE TEAM-MEMBER BINDING.** What happens when the mutated workmate's name equals a member of a live/archived team?\n- Why: binding is name-equality only — `members.js#workmateBacking` hashes the member name to the dir, and the team file persists that member name. Rename/delete silently strips the backing; that member's later `mpd_workmate_reflect` then FAILS (`ensureInstance` throws). Worst case: a workmate named a roster normal name (`senior-engineer`, `deep-worker`) is auto-bound to every such member of every `mpd`-profile team.\n- Candidates: (a) silent; (b) pre-check `.mpd/team/*/team.json` and REFUSE while a live team has such a member; (c) warn and proceed; (d) cascade — rewrite team member names (rename only). Sub-decision: does the member follow the rename automatically (alias)?\n\n**Q5 OLD NAME AFTER RENAME (REUSE / IDENTITY SWAP).** Is the old name freed immediately?\n- Why: if freed, a later `init` can create a *different* workmate under the old name and every existing member named that way silently re-binds to a different persona/memory.\n- Candidates: (a) free immediately; (b) reserve/tombstone with alias resolution (binding follows the alias); (c) free but `init` warns \"previously used by X\".\n\n**Q6 NAME INPUT CONTRACT.** Strict-reject or silent-normalize, and are non-ASCII names supported?\n- Why: `sanitizeName()` strips everything outside `[a-z0-9_-]` — a Chinese name such as 助理 sanitizes to `\"\"`, and `wmDir(\"\")` is the LIBRARY ROOT. Since the requester writes Chinese, CJK naming may be expected — supporting it means changing the key scheme in BOTH plugins (`members.js#workmateKey` must stay byte-identical).\n- Candidates: (a) strict reject (invalid/empty/no-op/collision), CJK unsupported and documented; (b) silent sanitize, error only on empty/collision; (c) allow Unicode dir names (new key scheme, cross-plugin change); (d) sanitize + `base-N` auto-suffix like init. Also: no-op rename = error or 200? Collision = refuse or merge?\n\n**Q7 GUI BEHAVIOR.** Where do controls live and how is delete confirmed?\n- Why: this is the human-facing half of the request; the tab is sidebar-only, `single: true`, with zh+en dictionaries (zh is the key-set source of truth) and a rebuilt `client.js` or nothing ships.\n- Candidates: (a) detail view only; (b) inline per-row controls; (c) native confirm / typed-name / two-step arm-then-confirm; plus: after rename does the open detail follow the new name or return to the list? Undo/toast or none?\n\n**Q8 SCOPE OF THE TRAVERSAL-DISCOVERED DEFECT.** The deny lists in mpd-workmate-plugin (line 30) AND mpd-roles-plugin (lines 23–27) name tools this harness lacks (`str_replace_editor`, `apply_patch`), and the harness rejects the whole restriction call — read-only workmate spawn and `mpd_role_spawn` fail today. In scope?\n- My recommendation for the user to rule on: OUT (separate `fix/` branch per AGENTS.md §5 — different package, different failure, §2.6 minimal diffs). Caveat arguing IN: a readonly workmate cannot be spawned at all, so end-to-end evidence for rename/delete on readonly instances is unreachable.\n- Candidates: (a) separate defect branch (recommended); (b) same change, both plugins; (c) same change, workmate plugin only.\n\n## (2) EDGE CASES THE IMPLEMENTATION MUST HANDLE\n\n- **EMPTY SANITIZED NAME**: `sanitizeName(x) === \"\"` (CJK, punctuation-only, whitespace) must be rejected BEFORE any fs call — `wmDir(\"\")` is `~/.mpd/workmate` itself, so delete would target the library root and rename would move it.\n- Path containment: the resolved target must be a strict child of the library root, never `index.json` or any non-directory entry.\n- Unknown name → explicit error, zero side effects; delete must not silently \"succeed\"; a second delete must error.\n- Half-created instance: a dir with no meta.json (crash between `mkdirSync` and the meta write at init) — `listInstances` skips it; rename/delete must decide error vs orphan cleanup.\n- Rename collision: target name exists (as dir or file) → refuse, mirroring init's `already exists`.\n- Sanitization collision: distinct inputs mapping to the same key (\"Alice Cooper\" / \"alice-cooper\" / \"Alice  Cooper\").\n- Case-only rename (\"Alice\" → \"alice\") on a case-insensitive filesystem must be a defined outcome, not a rename-to-itself ENOENT.\n- index.json consistency: it has NO reader today (grep: only `indexPath()`/`writeIndexEntry`) — rename must drop the old key and add the new, delete must drop the key, else it goes permanently stale; decide whether it is authoritative at all.\n- Partial failure: meta.name + index write can fail after the dir moved → no dir whose name and meta.name disagree; delete must not leave a half-removed instance.\n- Symlinks: a symlinked workmate dir must not let delete/rename escape the library root.\n- Race with in-flight work: `spawn` reads persona/memory, the subagent reflects LATER; `reflect` does readMeta → mutate → `writeFileSync(join(wmDir(meta.name)...))` — a reflect racing a rename resurrects the OLD dir; reflect after delete throws. Must be defined.\n- Service immediacy: `mpdWorkmate.get(old)` → null, `.get(new)`/`.read(new)` full detail, `list` updated on the very next call (no caching).\n- Cross-module: member backing resolves by dir existence alone; keys equal to roster normal names (`senior-engineer`) affect every matching member in every team.\n- Readonly instances: rename/delete are library-admin ops; a readonly workmate must not be able to mutate the library via the agent-tool path.\n- Web routes: method guard (405), 400 on invalid JSON, 404 on unknown name (mirror `/get`), `cache-control: no-store`, and a deliberate decision on leaking the absolute `$HOME` path (`initWorkmate` already returns `path`).\n- Lifecycle: routes register lazily behind `webRegistered` only when `webServer`/`httpServer` exists — headless must work tool-only.\n- GUI: stale selection/polling after mutation (no 404 loop); no second tab (`single: true`); new zh AND en keys mandatory; `node scripts/build-mpd-client.mjs` must be re-run.\n- Names colliding with roster ids/normal names or existing auto-names (`hephaestus-1`) must not overwrite.\n- Reflect/init side effects must not be able to recreate or mutate a deleted instance.\n- Sync surfaces (gates, not optional): package README.md + README.zh-CN.md, docs/user-guide.md + .zh-CN, AGENTS.md (tool list, glossary, troubleshooting), `presets/mpd/agent.cordis.yml` + the `mpd` roster profile protocol string in `packages/mpd-bundle/cordis.patch.yml`, `skills/dsh-qa/scripts/workmate-library.mjs` (asserts the list/roster/get route literals), `web-client-adapt.mjs`, `packages/mpd-bundle-plugin/test/sidebar-tab.test.mjs`.\n\n## (3) INVARIANTS ACCEPTANCE MUST PIN\n\n**I1 — NAME↔DIR↔INDEX BIJECTION AND ROOT SAFETY.** At all times: `sanitizeName(meta.name)` === dir basename === index.json key; after a rename the old dir and old key are gone; no operation may resolve to, move, or recursively remove the library root — an empty/invalid sanitized name is rejected with zero side effects. Holds identically in both plugins via the byte-identical `sanitizeName`/`workmateKey` algorithm.\n\n**I2 — RENAME IS IDENTITY-PRESERVING, NEVER A RE-INSTANTIATION.** The same instance moves: persona.md / memory.md / note.md content and caps, `uses`, `lastTask`, `createdAt` preserved (only the explicitly-decided self-references/`renamedFrom` change); no base re-copy, no memory reset, no `uses` bump.\n\n**I3 — DELETE IS COMPLETE AND ALL-OR-NOTHING.** After success: dir gone, index entry gone, `mpdWorkmate.get`/`read` null, absent from `list`, and no other workmate's bytes changed; unknown/empty/invalid name fails with a clear error and zero side effects; a failed delete never leaves a partially removed instance.\n\n**I4 — CROSS-MODULE BINDING OUTCOME IS DETERMINISTIC AND TEST-PINNED.** Whatever Q4/Q5 decide (silent / refuse / alias / cascade), the observable result for a team member whose name equals a mutated workmate, and for the `mpdWorkmate` service plus `mpd_workmate_list`/`_match`, must equal that decision at all times — no state where dir, index.json, service view and member backing disagree — pinned by the offline lifecycle test plus a QA self-test/real-boot row, with the real `$HOME` untouched (sandbox HOME).\n\nGates for acceptance: `bun test`, `bun run typecheck`, `bun run test:qa`, `node scripts/verify-vendor.mjs`, `dsh --profile headless --dump-config` in an isolated `DSH_HOME`, evidence under `evidence/<domain>/<slug>/<timestamp>/`, bilingual docs in the same commit. Full deliverable sent to the captain (`session-f333e946-e284-414f-b043-65a349cbe480`)."}],"source":{"kind":"subagent-settled","form":"notice","summary":"Background subagent 8fdfdfd4-308b-4ab3-b12f-21bf5997f1ae finished and will do no further work unless you send it more.","senderSessionId":"8fdfdfd4-308b-4ab3-b12f-21bf5997f1ae"},"role":"user","id":"2dcbc545-e6a2-4f6e-b9c3-53d43075f72f"},"surfaceOp":"append"}
