evidence/agent-teams/scheduler-wakeup-fix/2026-09-10T10-16-23Z/captain-session-f333e946.jsonl:922:{"type":"assistant/message","seq":22589,"time":1789026916489,"data":{"turn":1,"step":11,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"reasoning","text":"Now I have everything. Key facts confirmed:\n- agent-teams exposes NO cordis service (no `provide(` found for team state) — only tools `agent_teams_*`. So a cross-plugin cascade of team member names has no sanctioned API from within the workmate plugin. That's a critical constraint for \"改了以后全改\".\n- index.json has no reader — confirmed.\n\nSo how do I honor \"agent在跑的时候不让改，改了以后全改\" safely?\n\nInterpretation & design:\n- **Liveness gate (不让改 while running)**: refuse rename/delete while the workmate is in use:\n  (a) in-flight `mpd_workmate_spawn` in this process (track a live set of names with running spawns) — in-plugin, exact.\n  (b) a live team member bound by name: needs team state. The agent-teams state lives in `.mpd/team` (stateDir override). There's no service. Reading team state files directly is a coupling. BUT the honest way: the workmate plugin may READ (never write) the team state dir to detect live teams on the same session? Hmm — the captain protocol forbids *me* (the agent) from inspecting .agent-teams state to revise plans; that's a captain rule, not a plugin rule. Still, coupling a plugin to another plugin's file format is fragile.\n\nAlternative, cleaner and sanctioned: the **GUI/tool surface** can ask the agent-teams plugin via its **tools** — i.e. the workmate plugin calls `dsh.hasTool(\"agent_teams_status\")` / `dsh.executeTool({name:\"agent_teams_status\"})` to get live team members, and refuses when a member name matches. That IS the sanctioned path exposed by the adapted API (§6: internal tool calls via the adapter). It's read-only and uses the public tool surface. That's elegant and reviewable.\n\nHmm, does `agent_teams_status` return all teams of all sessions and their members? The captain