e offline test able to know the harness's known tool names? The roles plugin source could import the roster/harness? There's `dsh.hasTool(name)`. An offline unit test could assert the deny list is a subset of the harness's known tools by importing something... The adapter has `hasTool`. In a unit test with a fake ctx, hasTool is stubbed. Hmm. A live harness check (`dsh --dump-config`?) wouldn't list global tools. Honestly the cleanest proof: run the real harness's restrict with the list (live) → the QA case.\n    \nSo let me REASSIGN: T5 (Deep Worker) = fix both deny lists + live-harness QA case + offline test. T7 (Lead) = docs + existing QA script route assertions + AGENTS.md, explicitly NOT touching T5's new files. Conflict only if both edit SKILL.md concurrently; I'll add to T7's description \"T5 owns the roles-run readonly row and its script; append your rows without touching theirs\" and since T7 runs after T3/T4, T5 is likely done. Acceptable with explicit path ownership: T7 inScope includes skills/dsh-qa/SKILL.md, T5 inScope includes skills/dsh-qa/scripts/roles-readonly-spawn.mjs (new file) and its SKILL.md row... \n\nI'll just say: T5 owns `skills/dsh-qa/scripts/*` (new case) + packages/mpd-roles-plugin/**; T7 owns packages/*/README*, AGENTS.md, docs/**, and `skills/dsh-qa/scripts/workmate-library.mjs` + `web-client-adapt.mjs` + SKILL.md rows EXCEPT the readonly row. Fine — describe precisely.\n\nActually, cleaner: make T7 (docs) depend on T5 as well, so it runs after T5 finishes → no concurrent SKILL.md edit. T7 depends T3, T4, T5. Good — that's a genuine ordering (docs describe the shipped surface, including the readonly fix). I'll do that.\n\nThen:\n- T8 [integration] → **Lead**: depends T6 (verification), RV1, RV2, RV3, T7. Deliverable: integrated evidence + final gate sweep + a delivery report + confirm nothing contradicts (docs vs code). Hmm, Lead owning both T7 and T8: fine, sequential.\n\nBut wait: Lead having T7 and T8 — a member can own only ONE un