k` kind task.\n\nTask kinds: use quality kinds where they fit (requirements, implementation, verification, review, integration) with contracts. For the dossier and docs tasks, use `work` (legacy, no gate) or `implementation`? Docs is an implementation-ish deliverable; but implementation/repair require inScope + verify. Docs changes: inScope = docs paths; verify = the bilingual link check? There's no doc gate script... maybe a simple grep-based check. I could use kind=work for docs to avoid a fake verify command. Hmm, the protocol says quality kinds need contracts; docs as `work` is acceptable and honest. But \"The user explicitly requests full quality-mode planning\" — they didn't. The slash command says derive the smallest useful DAG. I'll use:\n- T1 requirements (contract)\n- T2 work (dossier)\n- T3 implementation (verify cmds)\n- T4 implementation (verify cmds)\n- T5 implementation (verify cmds)\n- T6 verification (acceptance)\n- RV1/RV2/RV3 review (reviewedTaskId)\n- T7 work (docs/sync) — with a verify command (e.g. `bun run test:qa` after script updates + grep link check) → could be implementation kind with inScope+verify. I'll make it implementation? Docs \"implementation\" is a stretch but the verification commands (test:qa self-tests, bilingual file pair existence) are real. Let me use kind=work with explicit acceptance listed in description to avoid gate semantics that need inScope/verify... Actually implementation kind REQUIRES inScope + verify — I can supply both truthfully: verify: [\"bun run test:qa\", \"node skills/dsh-qa/scripts/web-client-adapt.mjs --self-test\"]. inScope: packages/mpd-workmate-plugin/README.md, ...README.zh-CN.md, AGENTS.md, docs/user-guide.md, docs/user-guide.zh-CN.md, skills/dsh-qa/**. That's fine and gives a real gate. Use kind=implementation for T7. Hmm, but then a review of T7? The quality gate would want a review of each implementation. Not mandatory (the system doesn't force it); but reviewers exist... I'll not add a 4th review (docs review by Plan Reviewer could be folded into RV3? RV3 is T5.) Keep RV1/RV2/RV3 only; the integration task (Lead) verifies doc/code consistency, and I verify at the end.\n\nLet me finalize ids after creation (task ids come from the tool).\n\nAlso the \"escalated/halted\" semantics: not relevant at staging.\n\nOne more: acceptance criteria must be concrete and verifiable by a reviewer.\n\nAlso inScope paths must be workspace-relative POSIX. Fine.\n\nNow, the second user question (CJK names). Let me ask it as a single question, receive the answer, then create the tasks (so the plan encodes it). Actually — with ask_user_question returning inline, I can then create tasks in the same turn. Let me do that.\n\nHmm, but is asking again worth the interruption? The momus flagged it as a genuine product decision with a safety angle (CJK → empty sanitized key → root hazard). The safety part I handle regardless (reject). The product part (support CJK names) materially changes scope. Given the user writes Chinese, I'd say ask. One focused question, with the tradeoff. Yes.\n\nLet me write it concisely in Chinese."},{"type":"text","text":"Consult landed with a full edge-case/invariant set. One genuinely scope-changing decision remains (the specialist flagged a real hazard: `sanitizeName()` strips non-ASCII, so a Chinese name like `助理` sanitizes to `\"\"` — and `wmDir(\"\")` is the library root itself):"},{"type":"tool-call","id":"call_00_emXd4Xm8Njv0iB8YsBhw6639","name":"ask_user_question","arguments":"{\"questions\": [{\"header\": \"workmate 命名\", \"id\": \"cjk_names\", \"options\": [{\"description\": \"名字限定 [a-z0-9_-]；中文/空/非法名在碰文件系统之前就被拒绝并给出清楚错误（绝不触发 wmDir(\\\"\\\")=库根 的危险）。改动最小、不动跨插件绑定算法。\", \"label\": \"本次保持 ASCII 命名（推荐）\"}, {\"description\": \"改 sanitizeName 键方案（目录名允许 Unicode），但 mpd-workmate-plugin 与 mpd-agent-teams-plugin/members.js#workmateKey 必须逐字节一致地同步改，并补跨插件一致性用例；工作量变大。\", \"label\": \"支持中文名（跨插件改键方案）\"}], \"question\": \"workmate 名即目录名，也是 team 成员绑定 key（两插件间必须逐字节一致