end on review round 1.\" ✓.\n\nAlso, per §9 full-quality-mode: requirements → implementation → verification → review → integration. We have that.\n\nDo I need \"T2 dossier\" as kind=work? Yes, fine.\n\nLet me also consider: T3 and T5 both might touch `skills/dsh-qa`? T3's QA route assertions are in workmate-library.mjs / web-client-adapt.mjs — I assigned those to T7. So T3's inScope: packages/mpd-workmate-plugin/** + evidence/workmate/rename-delete/**. Wait, T3 must produce evidence too (AGENTS.md: evidence without evidence is incomplete; each gate needs on-disk evidence). Let me give each impl task an evidence path in its inScope: evidence/workmate/<slug>/**.\n\nCareful: multiple tasks writing into the same evidence dir → conflicts. Use distinct slugs:\n- T3: evidence/workmate/rename-delete-core/<ts>/\n- T4: evidence/workmate/rename-delete-gui/<ts>/\n- T5: evidence/workmate/roles-readonly/<ts>/\n- T6: evidence/workmate/rename-delete-verify/<ts>/\n- T7: evidence/workmate/rename-delete-docs/<ts>/\n- T8: evidence/workmate/rename-delete-integration/<ts>/\n\nGood.\n\nNow let me verify a few facts before writing tasks: do packages/mpd-roles-plugin and others have test dirs (for verify commands)? Let me check quickly. Also check the build command convention (package.json scripts).\n\nLet me run one command to check test dirs + package scripts.\n\nThen create the tasks (multiple agent_teams_create_task calls — can be parallel within one block? They're independent calls; the tool says tasks can depend on ids... I need ids from earlier calls for dependencies. So: first create T1, T2, T3, T4, T5 (independent of each other mostly: T3/T4/T5 depend on T1 → T3/T4 need T1's id). So sequence: create T1 & T2 in parallel → then T3,T4 (dep T1) & T5 (no dep) in parallel → then T6 (dep T3,T4,T5), RV1 (dep T3), RV2 (dep T4), RV3 (dep T5) → then T7 (dep T3,T4,T5) → T8 (dep T6,RV1,RV2,RV3,T7,T2).\n\nThat's 4 rounds of calls. Fine.\n\nLet me check facts first."},{"type":"text","text":"All d