 RV3, T7, T2]:\nsubject: \"Integrate and report: rename/delete feature, defect fix, docs and evidence as one coherent change\"\nobjective: \"Integrate the verified, reviewed work into one coherent change on disk and report it honestly: reconcile docs against the shipped code and the T2 dossier, persist the T1 contract and T2 dossier into the evidence tree, re-run the final gate sweep on the integrated tree, and summarize what changed, what was verified, and what remains open.\"\nacceptance:\n- \"The T1 requirements contract and the T2 project-traversal dossier are persisted on disk under evidence/workmate/rename-delete-integration/<timestamp>/ (read-only members delivered them as text).\"\n- \"A code↔docs consistency pass confirms every tool name, route, flag, status code and refusal semantic documented in AGENTS.md/READMEs/user guide matches the shipped sources; any drift is fixed or reported as an open finding.\"\n- \"The final integrated tree passes the gate sweep (bun test packages, bun run typecheck, bun run test:qa, node scripts/verify-vendor.mjs) with the real output recorded.\"\n- \"The delivery report states: changed files, the exact user decisions implemented (archive-first delete, in-use refusal + full library-owned cascade, readonly defect fixed, tools+GUI surface, ASCII-only naming), what is explicitly NOT rewritten (archived team records), verification evidence paths, and any residual risk or follow-up.\"\n- \"No quality gate is left failed and no review finding from RV1/RV2/RV3 is left unresolved at integration time.\"\ninScope: [\"evidence/workmate/rename-delete-integration/\"]\nHmm, integration may need to fix docs drift → outOfScope packages. Let me give it inScope: docs paths too: [\"AGENTS.md\", \"docs/\", \"packages/mpd-workmate-plugin/README.md\", \"packages/mpd-workmate-plugin/README.zh-CN.md\", \"evidence/workmate/rename-delete-integration/\"]. Good.\n\nThat's 11 tasks: T1..T8 + RV1..RV3 = 11. Reasonable for a \"small-to-medium\" task with quality mode. Hmm, \"smallest useful task graph\" — 11 tasks with 11 members. It's proportional to a 3-surface implementation with bilingual docs + a defect fix. OK.\n\nLet me now create tasks. Round 1: T1, T2.\n\nNote: assignee names must match member names: \"Planner\", \"Explorer\", \"Senior Engineer\", \"Junior Engineer\", \"Deep Worker\", \"Reviewer\", \"Architect\", \"Plan Reviewer\", \"Lead\".\n\nLet me write the calls. I'll do T1 and T2 in one block."}}}}
evidence/agent-teams/scheduler-wakeup-fix/2026-09-10T10-16-23Z/captain-session-f333e946.jsonl:1253:{"type":"assistant/message","seq":32692,"time":1789027101515,"data":{"turn":1,"step":13,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"reasoning","text":"All gates exist. Now let me stage the DAG.\n\nRound 1: create T1 (requirements, Planner) and T2 (work dossier, Explorer).\n\nLet me write substantial, precise descriptions.\n\nT1:\nsubject: \"Requirements contract + pinned wire protocol for workmate rename/delete\"\nkind: requirements, round 1\nassignee: Planner\nobjective: \"Turn the user-approved decisions into a binding, implementation-ready contract for workmate rename + delete: exact tool surface, exact HTTP wire protocol, refusal semantics, cascade list, archive layout, and error taxonomy — covering every edge case surfaced by the adversarial interrogation.\"\nacceptance:\n- \"Contract fixes the exact names/signatures of the new agent tools: mpd_workmate_rename and mpd_workmate_delete, their required/optional args (incl. the delete archive-vs-purge switch and the confirmation arg), return fields, and error messages.\"\n- \"Contract fixes the exact HTTP wire protocol: path + method + request JSON + success/error body + status codes (405 wrong verb, 400 invalid JSON, 404 unknown name, 409/400 collision, cache-control: no-store) for every new route, byte-matching what the GUI task will call.\"\n- \"Contract pins the usage/liveness gate semantics: mutation is REFUSED while the workmate is in use (an in-flight spawn in this process, or a member of a live/non-archived team bound by name), naming the exact detection mechanism the implementation must use in this harness and its documented fallback.\"\n- \"Contract enumerates the complete cascade for rename: directory key, meta.name, index.json key, note.md self-reference, continuity metadata (renamedFrom/previousNames), updatedAt handling, and explicitly states which references are NOT rewritten (archived team records are historical and stay untouched).\"\n- \"Contract pins delete semantics: default archive to ~/.mpd/workmate/.archive/<name>-<ISO>/ (hidden from list/match, restorable), purge for real removal, and the exact refusal when the instance is in use.\"\n- \"Contract pins name-safety invariants: ASCII-only key scheme ([a-z0-9_-]); any name whose sanitized form is empty/invalid is rejected BEFORE any filesystem call; no operation may ever resolve to, move, or recursively remove the library root; collisions (dir, file, or live workmate) are refused.\"\n- \"Contract carries the edge-case matrix with a decided outcome for each item (empty/invalid name, unknown name, double delete, half-created instance without meta.json, case-only rename, sanitization collision, symlinks, partial-failure atomicity, spawn/reflect race, service immediacy, readonly instances, headless profile without web routes).\"\n- \"Verdict=pass with the contract text in the task output.\"\ndeliverables: [\"requirements contract (task output text)\", \"edge-case matrix with decided outcomes (task output text)\"]\nnonGoals: [\"Designing the implementation\", \"Editing any file (read-only role)\"]\ncoverageOf: [\"1. 可以给workmate改名\", \"2. 可以删除workmate\"]\n\nAlso description with the user decisions verbatim.\n\nT2:\nsubject: \"Project traversal dossier: workmate system in the full bundle context\"\nkind: work\nassignee: Explorer\ndescription: the whole-repo traversal; deliverables: dossier text (task output).\nNo contract needed for kind=work, but let me still include deliverables/acceptance? For kind=work only subject required. I'll add description + deliverables.\n\nLet me write these now. Keep descriptions detailed but not bloated.\n\nRound 2: T3 (Senior Engineer, implementation, dep T1), T4 (Junior Engineer, implementation, dep T1), T5 (Deep Worker, implementation, no dep).\n\nT3 details:\nsubject: \"Implement workmate rename + delete in mpd-workmate-plugin (tools, service, routes, safety, tests)\"\nkind: implementation, round 1\nassignee: Senior Engineer\ndependencies: [T1]\nobjective: \"Implement the rename and delete operations in packages/mpd-workmate-plugin exactly as the T1 contract pins them: new mpd_workmate_rename / mpd_workmate_delete tools, matching mpdWorkmate service methods, the new web routes, the usage/liveness refusal gate, the archive-first delete, full rename cascade, root-safety guards, and the workmate-side readonly deny-list correction — with unit tests and a rebuilt dist.\"\ninScope: [\"packages/mpd-workmate-plugin/\", \"evidence/workmate/rename-delete-core/\"]\noutOfScope: [\"packages/mpd-roles-plugin/\", \"packages/mpd-bundle-plugin/\", \"packages/mpd-agent-teams-plugin/\", \"AGENTS.md\", \"docs/\"]\nacceptance: (list ~7)\n - \"mpd_workmate_rename and mpd_workmate_delete are registered tools with the exact contract args/returns; the mpdWorkmate service exposes the matching methods and list/get/read reflect the mutation on the very next call (no caching).\"\n - \"After rename: old dir and old index key are gone; new dir basename === sanitizeName(meta.name) === the new index key; persona.md/memory.md/note.md content and caps, uses, lastTask and createdAt are preserved; note self-reference and continuity metadata updated; no re-instantiation and no uses bump.\"\n - \"After delete (default archive): the instance is moved under ~/.mpd/workmate/.archive/<name>-<ISO>/ and disappears from list/match/service; with purge it is removed; the index key is dropped in both paths; no other workmate's bytes change.\"\n - \"Usage/liveness gate: rename and delete are refused with a clear, actionable error while the workmate is in use (in-flight spawn in this process; a member bound by name in a live/non-archived team) using the mechanism T1 pinned; the refusal has zero side effects.\"\n - \"Name safety: any invalid/empty-sanitized name is rejected before any filesystem call; a rename collision (existing dir/file/workmate) is refused; a rename to the same sanitized key is a defined no-op error; no operation can ever resolve to, move, or remove ~/.mpd/workmate itself (root-safety test present).\"\n - \"Web routes are registered per the T1 wire contract with the pinned verbs/status codes/cache-control, and the plugin still works tool-only in a headless profile with no web server service.\"\n - \"The workmate-side READONLY_DENY no longer names tools this harness lacks (fix the readonly workmate spawn failure), pinned by a test.\"\n - \"bun test packages/mpd-workmate-plugin/test/workmate.test.ts and bun run typecheck pass; dist/index.js is rebuilt; evidence written under evidence/workmate/rename-delete-core/<timestamp>/ with command output.\"\nverify: \n - \"bun test packages/mpd-workmate-plugin/test/workmate.test.ts\"\n - \"bun run typecheck\"\n - \"cd packages/mpd-workmate-plugin && bun build src/index.ts --target node --format esm --outfile dist/index.js\"\nnonGoals: [\"GUI/client changes (T4)\", \"roles-plugin deny list (T5)\", \"docs (T7)\"]\n\nHmm: \"The workmate-side READONLY_DENY no longer names tools this harness lacks\" — good, and T5 does roles side.\n\nWait — is it safe/correct to just remove names? What ARE the correct tool names in this harness? Known: write, edit, mpd_hashline_edit, apply_patch? The harness has `write`, `edit`, `mpd_hashline_edit`. So deny should be [\"write\",\"edit\",\"mpd_hashline_edit\"] (+ maybe \"mpd_comment_check\"? no). The fix: drop the two unknown names. And also assert against the harness's known set — there's `dsh.hasTool(name)` at runtime; the plugin could filter the list dynamically by hasTool! That's a robust fix: `READONLY_DENY.filter(t => dsh.hasTool(t))`. Nice — I'll suggest that in the task as the preferred approach (filter at execute time so the list never goes stale). Good engineering. I'll mention it as a recommendation but let the implementer decide with the harness reality.\n\nT4: GUI\nsubject: \"Workmates sidebar tab: rename + delete controls (zh/en) and rebuilt client.js\"\nkind: implementation\nassignee: Junior Engineer\ndependencies: [T1]\nobjective: \"Give the Workmates DSH-better-sidebar tab the human-facing half of the feature: rename and delete controls wired to the T1 wire contract, bilingual (zh/en) dictionary keys, safe confirmation for the destructive path, stale-selection handling, and a rebuilt packages/mpd-bundle-plugin/client.js.\"\ninScope: [\"packages/mpd-bundle-plugin/src/web-client.js\", \"packages/mpd-bundle-plugin/test/\", \"packages/mpd-bundle-plugin/client.js\", \"evidence/workmate/rename-delete-gui/\"]\noutOfScope: [\"packages/mpd-workmate-plugin/\", \"packages/mpd-bundle-plugin/src/team-page.js\", \"AGENTS.md\", \"docs/\"]\nacceptance:\n- \"The workmate tab exposes rename (prefilled input) and delete (two-step arm-then-confirm, matching the archive-first semantics) for the selected workmate; both call ONLY the T1-pinned routes/methods/payloads.\"\n- \"Every new user-visible string exists in BOTH the zh and en dictionaries with identical key sets (zh remains the key-set source of truth).\"\n- \"After a successful rename the view follows to the new name (or returns to the refreshed list) and after delete it returns to the list; no stale detail polling, no 404 loop, no second tab.\"\n- \"An in-use refusal from the host (liveness gate) surfaces as a readable message instead of an unhandled failure.\"\n- \"The tab remains sidebar-only (no floating fallback / footer toggle reintroduced) and the sidebar seam policy (ctx.inject(['betterSidebar'])) is unchanged.\"\n- \"node scripts/build-mpd-client.mjs succeeds and the committed client.js contains the new routes/markers; bun test packages/mpd-bundle-plugin/test/sidebar-tab.test.mjs (and the workmate tab assertions) pass; evidence under evidence/workmate/rename-delete-gui/<timestamp>/.\"\nverify: [\"node scripts/build-mpd-client.mjs\", \"bun test packages/mpd-bundle-plugin/test/sidebar-tab.test.mjs\", \"bun run typecheck\"]\n\nHmm — `bun run typecheck` covers package