al output recorded: bun test packages, bun run typecheck, bun run test:qa, node scripts/verify-vendor.mjs, and a dsh --profile headless --dump-config boot in an isolated DSH_HOME.\"\n- \"A real sandbox-HOME exercise demonstrates: rename keeps persona/memory/note/uses/createdAt byte-identical and frees the old key; delete archives by default (restorable under .archive/) and purges on demand; list/match/service views agree with the filesystem immediately after each mutation.\"\n- \"Negative cases demonstrably pass: empty/CJK/punctuation-only name rejected before any filesystem call (library root untouched), unknown name errors with zero side effects, double delete errors, rename collision refused, rename/delete refused while the workmate is in use.\"\n- \"The web routes answer per the T1 contract (real boot: correct status codes for success/invalid/unknown/wrong-verb), and the readonly spawn fix is demonstrated against the real harness.\"\n- \"Every command result is recorded in commandsRun with exit codes and evidence; results.json/output.log written under evidence/workmate/rename-delete-verify/<timestamp>/; the real HOME and real ~/.dsh are never touched (sandbox asserted).\"\nverify: [\"bun test packages\", \"bun run typecheck\", \"bun run test:qa\", \"node scripts/verify-vendor.mjs\"]\ninScope: [\"evidence/workmate/rename-delete-verify/\"]\nHmm — a verification task's inScope: only evidence. Fine.\noutOfScope: [\"packages/** (verification must not fix; failures go back as findings)\"]\nnonGoals: [\"Fixing anything yourself\", \"Approving the implementation\"]\n\nRV1 review of T3 → Architect:\nsubject: \"Review: core rename/delete implementation (safety, identity, atomicity, races)\"\nkind: review, round 1, reviewedTaskId T3\nassignee: Architect\nobjective: \"Adversarially review the T3 implementation against the T1 contract on the points where a bug is expensive: root-safety, name sanitization, identity preservation, atomicity/partial failure, index consistency, spawn/reflect races, service immediacy, and the readonly deny correction — judging the LATEST implementation state, not the implementer's summary.\"\nacceptance:\n- \"Each T1 acceptance criterion is checked against the code and evidence with pass/fail and a concrete citation (file/line or command output).\"\n- \"The review explicitly attempts to falsify the invariants: I1 (name↔dir↔index bijection + root safety), I2 (rename is identity-preserving, never a re-instantiation), I3 (delete complete and all-or-nothing), I4 (deterministic cross-module binding outcome) — reporting any counterexample found.\"\n- \"Race/failure analysis covers: reflect after rename (old-dir resurrection), reflect/delete ordering, partial failure between the directory move and the metadata write, and the in-flight spawn liveness gate.\"\n- \"Verdict is pass only with zero unresolved blocker/high findings; otherwise fail with structured findings (id/severity/problem/requiredFix) that name the exact file and the required fix.\"\ninScope: [] hmm, review tasks don't need inScope. Only implementation/repair require inScope. Right: \"implementation/repair also need inScope and verify\". So reviews need objective + acceptance only.\n\nRV2 review of T4 → Plan Reviewer:\nsubject: \"Review: Workmates tab rename/delete UI, locale keys and rebuilt client\"\nkind: review, round 1, reviewedTaskId T4\nobjective: \"Review the T4 GUI work as a UI/UX and contract-conformance reviewer: does the tab actually let a human rename and safely delete a workmate, does every string exist in both zh and en with identical key sets, do the calls match the T1 wire contract exactly, and are the destructive path, refusal messaging and stale-selection handling sound?\"\nacceptance:\n- \"Wire-contract conformance is verified call-by-call (path/method/payload/response handling) against T1 — any drift is a finding.\"\n- \"Every new visible string is present in both dictionaries with identical key sets; a missing zh or en key is at least a high finding.\"\n- \"The destructive flow is human-safe: explicit confirmation, archive-first wording that matches the host semantics, no single-click irreversible action, and a readable message on an in-use refusal.\"\n- \"The sidebar design constraints hold: sidebar-only tab (no floating fallback / footer toggle), single:true, no stale detail polling or 404 loop after a mutation, and client.js is rebuilt so the shipped bundle contains the new UI.\"\n- \"Verdict is pass only with zero unresolved blocker/high findings; otherwise fail with structured findings naming the file and the required fix.\"\n\nRV3 review of T5 → Senior Engineer:\nsubject: \"Review: read-only deny-list defect fix and its real-harness proof\"\nkind: review, round 1, reviewedTaskId T5\nobjective: \"Review the T5 fix on correctness of the diagnosis and strength of the proof: does the deny list now name only tools this harness registers, is the mechanism robust rather than a one-off literal patch, does the regression actually exercise the real harness (not a stub), and did the fix avoid widening read-only authority?\"\nacceptance:\n- \"The root cause is confirmed against the harness's real tool registry and the fix is shown to remove it (before/after evidence cited).\"\n- \"The regression/QA case is evaluated for real-harness fidelity: it must fail on the pre-fix code or on the original deny list, and pass after — a stub-only assertion is a finding.\"\n- \"Read-only authority is verified not to have widened: the roles remain unable to write (no write/edit/apply_patch-style tool becomes available).\"\n- \"Verdict is pass only with zero unresolved blocker/high findings; otherwise fail with structured findings naming the file and the required fix.\"\n\nRound 4:\nT7 docs/sync → Lead, kind implementation, deps [T3, T4, T5]:\nsubject: \"Bilingual docs + QA surface sync for workmate rename/delete\"\nobjective: \"Sync every human-facing and agent-facing surface with the shipped feature: the package README pair, the user guide pair, AGENTS.md (workmate tool list, glossary, troubleshooting), and the QA scripts that assert the workmate route literals — both language versions in the same change, and the QA assertions extended to the new routes.\"\ninScope: [\"packages/mpd-workmate-plugin/README.md\", \"packages/mpd-workmate-plugin/README.zh-CN.md\", \"AGENTS.md\", \"docs/user-guide.md\", \"docs/user-guide.zh-CN.md\", \"skills/dsh-qa/scripts/workmate-library.mjs\", \"skills/dsh-qa/scripts/web-client-adapt.mjs\", \"skills/dsh-qa/SKILL.md\", \"evidence/workmate/rename-delete-docs/\"]\noutOfScope: [\"packages/mpd-workmate-plugin/src/\", \"packages/mpd-bundle-plugin/src/\", \"packages/mpd-roles-plugin/\", \"the readonly-spawn QA case and its SKILL.md row (T5)\"]\nacceptance:\n- \"packages/mpd-workmate-plugin/README.md and README.zh-CN.md both document the new tools/routes/semantics (archive-first delete, in-use refusal, ASCII naming) with the language switch link directly under each title; neither version is left stale.\"\n- \"docs/user-guide.md and docs/user-guide.zh-CN.md are updated in the same change wherever the workmate workflow is described, keeping the switch links intact.\"\n- \"AGENTS.md carries the new tool names in the workmate tool list, updates the workmate glossary entry, and adds troubleshooting rows for the rename/delete failure modes (in-use refusal, archived instance restore, invalid/CJK name rejection).\"\n- \"The QA scripts assert the new routes/routes-list so the shipped surface is pinned by test:qa (workmate-library.mjs and web-client-adapt.mjs updated, their --self-test still passes, and SKILL.md's case table matches reality).\"\n- \"Docs claim nothing the code does not do: every documented tool name, route, flag and status code is verified against the shipped sources.\"\nverify: [\"bun run test:qa\", \"bun test packages/mpd-bundle-plugin/test\", \"bun run typecheck\"]\n\nT8 integration → Lead, kind integration, round 1, deps [T6, RV1, RV2, RV3, T7, T2]:\nsubject: \"Integrate and report: rename/delete feature, defect fix, docs and evidence as one coherent change\"\nobjective: \"Integrate the verified, reviewed work into one coherent change on disk and report it honestly: reconcile docs against the shipped code and the T2 dossier, persist the T1 contract and T2 dossier into the evidence tree, re-run the final gate sweep on the integrated tree, and summarize what changed, what was verified, and what remains open.\"\nacceptance:\n- \"The T1 requirements contract and the T2 project-traversal dossier are persisted on disk under evidence/workmate/rename-delete-integration/<timestamp>/ (read-only members delivered them as text).\"\n- \"A code↔docs consistency pass confirms every tool name, route, flag, status code and refusal semantic documented in AGENTS.md/READMEs/user guide matches the shipped sources; any drift is fixed or reported as an open finding.\"\n- \"The final integrated tree passes the gate sweep (bun test packages, bun run typecheck, bun run test:qa, node scripts/verify-vendor.mjs) with the real output recorded.\"\n- \"The delivery report states: changed files, the exact user decisions implemented (archive-first delete, in-use refusal + full library-owned cascade, readonly defect fixed, tools+GUI surface, ASCII-only naming), what is explicitly NOT rewritten (archived team records), verification evidence paths, and any residual risk or follow-up.\"\n- \"No quality gate is left failed and no review finding from RV1/RV2/RV3 is left unresolved at integration time.\"\ninScope: [\"evidence/workmate/rename-delete-integration/\"]\nHmm, integration may need to fix docs drift → outOfScope packages. Let me give it inScope: docs paths too: [\"AGENTS.md\", \"docs/\", \"packages/mpd-workmate-plugin/README.md\", \"packages/mpd-workmate-plugin/README.zh-CN.md\", \"evidence/workmate/rename-delete-integration/\"]. Good.\n\nThat's 11 tasks: T1..T8 + RV1..RV3 = 11. Reasonable for a \"small-to-medium\" task with quality mode. Hmm, \"smallest useful task graph\" — 11 tasks with 11 members. It's proportional to a 3-surface implementation with bilingual docs + a defect fix. OK.\n\nLet me now create tasks. Round 1: T1, T2.\n\nNote: assignee names must match member names: \"Planner\", \"Explorer\", \"Senior Engineer\", \"Junior Engineer\", \"Deep Worker\", \"Reviewer\", \"Architect\", \"Plan Reviewer\", \"Lead\".\n\nLet me write the calls. I'll do T1 and T2 in one block."},{"type":"text","text":"Now I'll stage the task DAG on the already-staged `MPD Default` team (profile `mpd`), encoding your five decisions."},{"type":"tool-call","id":"call_00_hU6VeOa76cUa49ozcy2s4354","name":"agent_teams_create_task","arguments":"{\"subject\": \"Requirements contract + pinned wire protocol for workmate rename/delete\", \"kind\": \"requirements\", \"round\": 1, \"assignee\": \"Planner\", \"coverageOf\": [\"1. 可以给workmate改名\", \"2. 可以删除workmate\", \"遍历工程，了解工程详细信息\"], \"objective\": \"Turn the user-approved decisions into a binding, implementation-ready contract for workmate rename + delete: exact agent-tool surface, exact HTTP wire protocol, in-use refusal semantics, complete rename cascade, archive-first delete layout, and an error taxonomy — with a decided outcome for every edge case raised by the adversarial interrogation. This contract is what the two implementation tasks build against in parallel, so it must be precise enough that no implementation choice is left open.\", \"description\": \"Ground the contract in the real sources: packages/mpd-workmate-plugin/src/index.ts (the whole feature, ~439 lines: sanitizeName, wmDir, readMeta/writeJson, readIndex/writeIndexEntry — note index.json currently has NO reader — listInstances, initWorkmate, autoNote, appendMemory, mergePersona, the mpdWorkmate service, the 5 tools, the 4 lazily-registered web routes), packages/mpd-agent-teams-plugin/lib/members.js (workmateKey/workmateBacking: a team member is bound to a workmate by NAME EQUALITY against a sanitized key; there is NO provided cordis service for team state — only agent_teams_* tools), packages/mpd-bundle-plugin/src/web-client.js (the Workmates sidebar tab, SIDEBAR_TAB_ID=\\\"mpd-workmate\\\", zh+en dictionaries with zh as key-set source of truth) and the existing tests.\\n\\nUSER DECISIONS ALREADY AGREED (binding input — do not reopen):\\nD1 Delete = archive-first. Default moves the instance to ~/.mpd/workmate/.archive/<name>-<ISO>/ (hidden from list/match, restorable); real removal only with an explicit purge switch. Destructive path gets an explicit confirmation in the GUI.\\nD2 In-use gate + full cascade. Mutating a workmate is REFUSED while an agent is actually using it (an in-flight mpd_workmate_spawn in this process, or a member bound by name in a live/non-archived team). Once a mutation is allowed, ALL library-owned name references are updated (dir key, meta.name, index.json key, note.md self-reference, continuity metadata). Archived team records are historical and are NOT rewritten — state that boundary explicitly.\\nD3 The read-only deny-list defect is IN SCOPE for this change (roles plugin = separate task T5; the workmate-side line belongs to the core implementation task T3).\\nD4 Surface = agent tools + web routes + the Workmates sidebar GUI (zh/en).\\nD5 ASCII-only key scheme for now: names are limited to [a-z0-9_-]; CJK/empty/invalid names are rejected with a clear error BEFORE any filesystem call. (sanitizeName(\\\"\\\") returns \\\"\\\" and wmDir(\\\"\\\") IS the library root — this is a real hazard the contract must close.)\\n\\nDeliverables are TEXT in your task output (you are a read-only role): the contract plus the edge-case matrix with a decided outcome for each item. Do not edit files.\", \"acceptance\": [\"Contract fixes the exact names, arguments, return fields and error text of the new agent tools mpd_workmate_rename and mpd_workmate_delete, including the delete archive-vs-purge switch, the confirmation argument, and the intended mpdWorkmate service method additions.\", \"Contract fixes the exact HTTP wire protocol for every new route (path + method + request JSON + success body + error body + status codes for wrong verb / invalid JSON / unknown name / refused-in-use / name collision, and cache-control: no-store), precise enough that the GUI task can call it without guessing.\", \"Contract pins the in-use refusal semantics: the exact conditions that refuse a mutation, the detection mechanism that actually works in THIS harness (including what is permitted to be read and what must never be written across plugins), the refusal error shape, and the documented fallback when the signal is unavailable.\", \"Contract enumerates the COMPLETE rename cascade and its deliberate exclusions: directory key, meta.name, index.json key, note.md self-reference, continuity metadata (renamedFrom/previousNames), updatedAt handling, no uses bump, no base re-copy, and an explicit statement that archived team records are not rewritten.\", \"Contract pins delete semantics end to end: archive layout and naming, hidden-from-list/match behaviour, restore expectation, purge behaviour, index-key removal in both paths, and the exact refusal when the instance is in use.\", \"Contract pins name-safety invariants: ASCII key scheme; invalid/empty-sanitized names rejected before any filesystem call; every resolved path a strict child of the library root; collisions (existing dir, existing file, live workmate) refused; no operation may ever resolve to, move, or remove the library root itself.\", \"Contract carries an edge-case matrix with a decided outcome per item: empty/invalid name, unknown name, repeated delete, half-created instance without meta.json, case-only rename, sanitization collision, symlink escaping the root, partial failure between directory move and metadata write, spawn/reflect race (old-dir resurrection), service/list immediacy, readonly instances, and a headless profile with no web server.\", \"Verdict=pass with the full contract and matrix present in the task output.\"], \"deliverables\": [\"requirements contract (task output text)\", \"edge-case matrix with decided outcomes (task output text)\", \"exact wire-protocol table for the new routes (task output text)\"], \"nonGoals\": [\"Writing implementation code or editing any file (read-only role)\", \"Designing the GUI layout (T4 owns it)\", \"Reopening the five user decisions already agreed\"]}"},{"type":"tool-call","id":"call_01_Xz7813drvUc2kTToJUkA4982","name":"agent_teams_create_task","arguments":"{\"subject\": \"Project traversal dossier: the workmate system in full bundle context\", \"kind\": \"work\", \"assignee\": \"Explorer\", \"description\": \"Deliver a grounded traversal dossier of this repository, with the workmate system located inside it. Read the real sources — do not summarize AGENTS.md back to the reader. Cover, at minimum:\\n\\n1. Repository shape: every package under packages/ and what it actually does (source of truth = its src/index.ts + README, not its name), plus presets/, skills/, scripts/, tests/, evidence/ and the .mpd state roots.\\n2. The workmate system end to end: packages/mpd-workmate-plugin (library root at $HOME/.mpd/workmate, per-instance meta.json/persona.md/memory.md/note.md, the root index.json and the fact that nothing reads it, the size caps, sanitizeName, the 5 tools, the mpdWorkmate service, the 4 lazily-registered web routes) — and every OTHER surface that references it: the agent-teams member binding by name equality (packages/mpd-agent-teams-plugin/lib/members.js), the Workmates sidebar tab and its zh/en dictionaries (packages/mpd-bundle-plugin/src/web-client.js), the bundle patch rows, the presets, the QA scripts that assert workmate route literals, and every doc that mentions it.\\n3. Execution and gates: how the bundle is installed (one-command `dsh plugin add .`, the packed release path), how QA boots an isolated DSH_HOME/HOME, what each gate command in AGENTS.md §4 really does, and the evidence-on-disk convention.\\n4. Coupling map and hazards: where a workmate name is load-bearing (directory key, index key, team-member binding, note self-reference), which cross-plugin assumptions are byte-identical by contract (sanitizeName vs members.js#workmateKey), and which surfaces go stale if a workmate is renamed or deleted.\\n\\nDeliver the dossier as TEXT in your task output (you are a read-only role — do not edit files). Prefer concrete file paths and line-anchored facts over prose, and call out anything that contradicts AGENTS.md. The captain and the integration task will persist your dossier into the evidence tree.\", \"deliverables\": [\"project traversal dossier (task output text)\", \"workmate coupling map + stale-surface list (task output text)\", \"contradictions found between docs and the real code (task output text)\"], \"nonGoals\": [\"Editing any file\", \"Proposing the rename/delete design (T1 owns the contract)\"]}"}],"source":{"kind":"model","provider":"deepseek-official","model":"deepseek-v4-flash"},"id":"37463c8f-a2bf-4c23-bb7f-92804b070566"},"usage":{"inputTokens":768,"outputTokens":7707,"totalTokens":104603,"cacheReadTokens":96128,"reasoningTokens":5649}},"sourceEventSeqs":[[25154,32691]],"surfaceOp":"append"}
