de READONLY_DENY no longer names tools this harness does not register, so a readonly workmate can actually be spawned; pinned by a test.\", \"bun test packages/mpd-workmate-plugin/test/workmate.test.ts, bun run typecheck and the dist rebuild all pass, with evidence written under evidence/workmate/rename-delete-core/<timestamp>/.\"], \"assignee\": \"Senior Engineer\", \"dependencies\": [\"t1\"], \"description\": \"Implement exactly what the T1 contract pins — read its output first and treat it as binding; if you find a contract gap or a genuine impossibility in this harness, report it in your task output instead of silently improvising a different design.\\n\\nThe work is centred on packages/mpd-workmate-plugin/src/index.ts: the 5 existing tools (list/init/spawn/reflect/match), the mpdWorkmate service, the index.json writer (no reader today), and the 4 lazily registered web routes. Correctness constraints that matter most: sanitizeName() is the single key algorithm and wmDir(\\\"\\\") resolves to the library root itself, so every name must be validated before any fs call; the rename must preserve the evolved identity (persona/memory/note/uses/createdAt) and must never be a re-instantiation; delete must be all-or-nothing; and a mutation racing an in-flight spawn/reflect must have a defined outcome (the liveness gate from D2 is how you close that race).\\n\\nKeep the house rules: all harness seams go through the mpd-dsh-adapter (packages/mpd-dsh-adapter-plugin) — never call ctx.tools/ctx.subagents directly; keep the state under ~/.mpd/workmate (the one sanctioned HOME exception); English-only code comments and docstrings; minimal diff, no speculative refactors. Rebuild the package dist when done (bun build src/index.ts --target node --format esm --outfile dist/index.js) — a checkout install reads dist directly.\\n\\nScope boundary: the roles-plugin deny list is T5's, the GUI is T4's, all documentation is T7's. Do not touch them.\", \"inScope\": [\"packages/mpd-workmate-plugin/\", \"evidence/workmate/rename-delete-core/\"], \"nonGoals\": [\"The roles-plugin READONLY_DENY (T5 owns it)\", \"The Workmates sidebar GUI and client.js (T4 owns it)\", \"Docs, AGENTS.md and QA scripts (T7 owns them)\", \"Changing the library root, the size caps, or the matching algorithm\"], \"outOfScope\": [\"packages/mpd-roles-plugin/\", \"packages/mpd-bundle-plugin/\", \"packages/mpd-agent-teams-plugin/\", \"AGENTS.md\", \"docs/\", \"skills/\"], \"objective\": \"Implement rename and delete for the workmate library in packages/mpd-workmate-plugin exactly as the T1 contract pins them: the two new agent tools, their mpdWorkmate service methods, the new web routes, the in-use refusal gate, archive-first delete, the complete rename cascade, root-safety and name-safety guards, the workmate-side read-only deny correction, plus tests, a rebuilt dist and evidence on disk.\", \"round\": 1, \"subject\": \"Implement workmate rename + delete core: tools, service, routes, safety, tests\", \"verify\": [\"bun test packages/mpd-workmate-plugin/test/workmate.test.ts\", \"bun run typecheck\", \"cd packages/mpd-workmate-plugin && bun build src/index.ts --target node --format esm --outfile dist/index.js\"]}"}}}}
