bject\": \"Workmates sidebar tab: rename + delete controls (zh/en) and rebuilt client\", \"verify\": [\"node scripts/build-mpd-client.mjs\", \"bun test packages/mpd-bundle-plugin/test\", \"bun run typecheck\"]}"}}}}
evidence/agent-teams/scheduler-wakeup-fix/2026-09-10T10-16-23Z/captain-session-f333e946.jsonl:1330:{"type":"assistant/message","seq":34793,"time":1789027111867,"data":{"turn":1,"step":14,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"reasoning","text":"Round 2: T3 (dep t1), T4 (dep t1), T5 (no deps)."},{"type":"tool-call","id":"call_00_trJ8bjsnMbH9dnegCHBP8009","name":"agent_teams_create_task","arguments":"{\"acceptance\": [\"mpd_workmate_rename and mpd_workmate_delete are registered with the exact contract arguments and returns, and the mpdWorkmate service exposes matching methods; list/get/read reflect the mutation on the very next call with no caching.\", \"After rename: the old directory and the old index key are gone; the new directory basename === sanitizeName(meta.name) === the new index key; persona.md/memory.md/note.md content and caps, uses, lastTask and createdAt are preserved byte-for-byte; the note self-reference and continuity metadata are updated; no re-instantiation, no uses bump.\", \"After delete (default): the instance is moved under ~/.mpd/workmate/.archive/<name>-<ISO>/ and disappears from list/match/service immediately; with purge it is really removed; the index key is dropped in both paths; no other workmate's bytes change.\", \"In-use gate: rename and delete are refused with a clear actionable error while the workmate is in use (in-flight spawn in this process; a member bound by name in a live/non-archived team) via the mechanism T1 pinned, with zero side effects on refusal; archived team records are never rewritten.\", \"Root-safety and name safety: invalid/empty-sanitized names are rejected before any filesystem call; rename collisions (existing dir/file/workmate) are refused; renaming to the same sanitized key is a defined outcome; a test proves no operation can resolve to, move, or remove ~/.mpd/workmate itself.\", \"Web routes match the T1 wire contract (verbs, payloads, status codes, cache-control) and the plugin still works tool-only when no web server service exists (headless profile).\", \"The workmate-side READONLY_DENY no longer names tools this harness does not register, so a readonly workmate can actually be spawned; pinned by a test.\", \"bun test packages/mpd-workmate-plugin/test/workmate.test.ts, bun run typecheck and the dist rebuild all pass, with evidence written under evidence/workmate/rename-delete-core/<timestamp>/.\"], \"assignee\": \"Senior Engineer\", \"dependencies\": [\"t1\"], \"description\": \"Implement exactly what the T1 contract pins — read its output first and treat it as binding; if you find a contract gap or a genuine impossibility in this harness, report it in your task output instead of silently improvising a different design.\\n\\nThe work is centred on packages/mpd-workmate-plugin/src/index.ts: the 5 existing tools (list/init/spawn/reflect/match), the mpdWorkmate service, the index.json writer (no reader today), and the 4 lazily registered web routes. Correctness constraints that matter most: sanitizeName() is the single key algorithm and wmDir(\\\"\\\") resolves to the library root itself, so every name must be validated before any fs call; the rename must preserve the evolved identity (persona/memory/note/uses/createdAt) and must never be a re-instantiation; delete must be all-or-nothing; and a mutation racing an in-flight spawn/reflect must have a defined outcome (the liveness gate from D2 is how you close that race).\\n\\nKeep the house rules: all harness seams go through the mpd-dsh-adapter (packages/mpd-dsh-adapter-plugin) — never call ctx.tools/ctx.subagents directly; keep the state under ~/.mpd/workmate (the one sanctioned HOME exception); English-only code comments and docstrings; minimal diff, no speculative refactors. Rebuild the package dist when done (bun build src/index.ts --target node --format esm --outfile dist/index.js) — a checkout install reads dist directly.\\n\\nScope boundary: the roles-plugin deny list is T5's, the GUI is T4's, all documentation is T7's. Do not touch them.\", \"inScope\": [\"packages/mpd-workmate-plugin/\", \"evidence/workmate/rename-delete-core/\"], \"nonGoals\": [\"The roles-plugin READONLY_DENY (T5 owns it)\", \"The Workmates sidebar GUI and client.js (T4 owns it)\", \"Docs, AGENTS.md and QA scripts (T7 owns them)\", \"Changing the library root, the size caps, or the matching algorithm\"], \"outOfScope\": [\"packages/mpd-roles-plugin/\", \"packages/mpd-bundle-plugin/\", \"packages/mpd-agent-teams-plugin/\", \"AGENTS.md\", \"docs/\", \"skills/\"], \"objective\": \"Implement rename and delete for the workmate library in packages/mpd-workmate-plugin exactly as the T1 contract pins them: the two new agent tools, their mpdWorkmate service methods, the new web routes, the in-use refusal gate, archive-first delete, the complete rename cascade, root-safety and name-safety guards, the workmate-side read-only deny correction, plus tests, a rebuilt dist and evidence on disk.\", \"round\": 1, \"subject\": \"Implement workmate rename + delete core: tools, service, routes, safety, tests\", \"verify\": [\"bun test packages/mpd-workmate-plugin/test/workmate.test.ts\", \"bun run typecheck\", \"cd packages/mpd-workmate-plugin && bun build src/index.ts --target node --format esm --outfile dist/index.js\"]}"},{"type":"tool-call","id":"call_01_zoJtafOE7luDtInOHDvf4276","name":"agent_teams_create_task","arguments":"{\"acceptance\": [\"The Workmates tab offers rename (input prefilled with the current name) and delete (explicit two-step confirmation that matches the archive-first semantics) for the selected workmate, calling ONLY the T1-pinned routes, methods and payloads.\", \"Every user-visible string added exists in BOTH the zh and en dictionaries with identical key sets (zh remains the key-set source of truth).\", \"After a rename the view follows to the new name or returns to the refreshed list; after a delete it returns to the list; no stale detail polling, no 404 loop, no second tab.\", \"An in-use refusal returned by the host surfaces as a readable, actionable message (naming why the mutation was refused), never as an unhandled failure or a silent no-op.\", \"The tab stays sidebar-only (no floating fallback, no footer toggle reintroduced) and the sidebar seam policy (ctx.inject(['betterSidebar']), probe-never-throw for optional seams) is unchanged.\", \"node scripts/build-mpd-client.mjs succeeds, the committed packages/mpd-bundle-plugin/client.js contains the new UI markers, and bun test packages/mpd-bundle-plugin/test passes.\", \"Evidence written under evidence/workmate/rename-delete-gui/<timestamp>/ (build output plus the test run).\"], \"assignee\": \"Junior Engineer\", \"dependencies\": [\"t1\"], \"description\": \"Deliver the human-facing half of the feature in the existing Workmates DSH-better-sidebar tab. Read the T1 wire contract first and treat it as binding — call exactly those routes and payloads; if the contract is missing something the UI needs, report it in your task output rather than inventing a route.\\n\\nSource of truth is packages/mpd-bundle-plugin/src/web-client.js: the WorkmateLibraryView component, its list/detail/init form, the request() helper, the WORKMATE_LOCALE_NAMESPACE zh+en dictionaries, SIDEBAR_TAB_ID=\\\"mpd-workmate\\\" and registerWorkmateSidebarTab. The tab is sidebar-only BY DESIGN (the old overlay floater and footer toggle were deliberately removed and the build fails if they come back), it is single: true, and it must never reintroduce an unguarded service declaration: optional seams are probed through ctx.get behind a helper that never throws (see the AGENTS.md troubleshooting rows and packages/mpd-bundle-plugin/test/sidebar-tab.test.mjs, which pins this seam policy).\\n\\nAfter editing the source you MUST rebuild the shipped client with `node scripts/build-mpd-client.mjs`, otherwise the bundle shows nothing new.\\n\\nScope boundary: the host tools and web routes are T3's; documentation and QA scripts are T7's. Do not touch them.\", \"inScope\": [\"packages/mpd-bundle-plugin/src/web-client.js\", \"packages/mpd-bundle-plugin/test/\", \"packages/mpd-bundle-plugin/client.js\", \"evidence/workmate/rename-delete-gui/\"], \"nonGoals\": [\"Adding or changing the host-side routes and tools (T3 owns them)\", \"The AgentTeams page (src/team-page.js) except where a test requires keeping its assertions intact\", \"Documentation and QA scripts (T7 owns them)\"], \"outOfScope\": [\"packages/mpd-workmate-plugin/\", \"packages/mpd-roles-plugin/\", \"packages/mpd-bundle-plugin/src/team-page.js\", \"AGENTS.md\", \"docs/\"], \"objective\": \"Give the Workmates sidebar tab a real rename and delete flow wired to the T1 wire contract: rename with a prefilled input, delete behind an explicit confirmation that matches archive-first semantics, bilingual (zh/en) strings with identical key sets, correct stale-selection handling after a mutation, a readable surface for an in-use refusal, and a rebuilt packages/mpd-bundle-plugin/client.js so the change actually ships.\", \"round\": 1, \"subject\": \"Workmates sidebar tab: rename + delete controls (zh/en) and rebuilt client\", \"verify\": [\"node scripts/build-mpd-client.mjs\", \"bun test packages/mpd-bundle-plugin/test\", \"bun run typecheck\"]}"}],"source":{"kind":"model","provider":"deepseek-official","model":"deepseek-v4-flash"},"id":"e46baa60-a946-4989-94cb-44de6590fb54"},"usage":{"inputTokens":229,"outputTokens":2324,"totalTokens":107001,"cacheReadTokens":104448,"reasoningTokens":25}},"sourceEventSeqs":[[32699,34792]],"surfaceOp":"append"}
