evidence/agent-teams/scheduler-wakeup-fix/2026-09-10T10-16-23Z/captain-session-f333e946.jsonl:1374:{"type":"assistant/chunk","seq":35837,"time":1789027118643,"data":{"turn":1,"step":15,"chunk":{"type":"block-end","index":1,"block":{"type":"tool-call","id":"call_00_hAeYSKS3JJ7o9cLkKzrm0338","name":"agent_teams_create_task","arguments":"{\"acceptance\": [\"packages/mpd-roles-plugin no longer passes any global tool name this harness does not register into a restriction call; the mechanism is robust (corrected or filtered against the live tool registry) rather than a one-off literal patch that can go stale again.\", \"The root cause is demonstrated against the REAL harness registry: evidence shows the original failure ('names unknown global tools') and the fixed behaviour, not merely a constructed deny array.\", \"A regression test fails on the pre-fix code (or on the original name list) and passes after the fix; a stub-only assertion that never exercises the real registry is insufficient.\", \"A dsh-qa case exists (script + --self-test + SKILL.md case-table row) that boots the real dsh in an ISOLATED DSH_HOME and HOME and demonstrates the read-only spawn path succeeding end to end; it never touches the real ~/.dsh, the real HOME, or real credentials.\", \"bun run test:qa and bun run typecheck pass with the new case included.\", \"Read-only authority is NOT widened: a read-only role still cannot write (no write/edit/apply_patch-class tool becomes available to it).\", \"Evidence written under evidence/workmate/roles-readonly/<timestamp>/ with the before/after command output.\"], \"assignee\": \"Deep Worker\", \"description\": \"This is a real, reproducible defect found while traversing the project, not a hypothesis. Reproduction the captain already confirmed:\\n\\n  mpd_role_spawn(role=...) for every READ-ONLY roster role fails immediately with:\\n  Error: tools.restrict() names unknown global tools \\\"str_replace_editor\\\", \\\"apply_patch\\\";\\n  known global tools: agent_teams_add_member, agent_teams_approve, ... (the harness's full list).\\n\\nThe deny lists live at packages/mpd-roles-plugin/src/index.ts (READONLY_DENY, ~line 23-27, used at ~line 123 as `toolFilter: { deny: READONLY_DENY }` when spec.readonly) and at packages/mpd-workmate-plugin/src/index.ts line 30 (the readonly workmate spawn path — that one belongs to task T3, NOT to you). Two of the denied names are from a different agent harness and do not exist here, and this harness rejects the WHOLE restriction call when any name is unknown, so the read-only discipline silently became 'no spawn at all'. The existing unit tests only assert the deny array's construction against a stub adapter, so they never caught it.\\n\\nNote the likely-honoured trap: the roster's read-only guarantee is a security-ish property (read-only specialists must not be able to write files). Fix the mechanism, verify the authority is unchanged, and do not 'fix' it by simply deleting the restriction.\\n\\nScope boundary: keep the workmate-side line out of your diff (T3 changes it) and do not touch the bundle client or the docs. The QA skill at skills/dsh-qa is yours for the new case; follow its discipline (SKILL.md case table, --self-test on every script, evidence under evidence/, isolated DSH_HOME with HOME=<sandbox>, credentials copied once into the sandbox, stdio to files rather than pipes for long-lived MCP children).\", \"inScope\": [\"packages/mpd-roles-plugin/\", \"skills/dsh-qa/scripts/\", \"evidence/workmate/roles-readonly/\"], \"nonGoals\": [\"The workmate-side READONLY_DENY line (T3 owns it)\", \"Changing the roster, its personas or its model routes\", \"Widening or removing the read-only restriction itself\", \"The Workmates GUI and documentation (T4/T7 own them)\"], \"outOfScope\": [\"packages/mpd-workmate-plugin/\", \"packages/mpd-bundle-plugin/\", \"AGENTS.md\", \"docs/\"], \"objective\": \"Fix the live defect that makes read-only specialist spawn (mpd_role_spawn) and read-only workmate spawn fail on this harness: the tool deny lists name global tools this harness does not register (str_replace_editor, apply_patch), and the harness rejects the entire restriction call, so no read-only spawn can be created at all. Prove the fix against the REAL dsh tool registry, keep read-only authority intact, and leave a regression that would catch the next stale name.\", \"round\": 1, \"subject\": \"Fix read-only deny lists so read-only spawn works on the real harness\", \"verify\": [\"bun test packages/mpd-roles-plugin/test\", \"bun run test:qa\", \"bun run typecheck\"]}"}}}}
