ict() names unknown global tools \\\"str_replace_editor\\\", \\\"apply_patch\\\";\\n  known global tools: agent_teams_add_member, agent_teams_approve, ... (the harness's full list).\\n\\nThe deny lists live at packages/mpd-roles-plugin/src/index.ts (READONLY_DENY, ~line 23-27, used at ~line 123 as `toolFilter: { deny: READONLY_DENY }` when spec.readonly) and at packages/mpd-workmate-plugin/src/index.ts line 30 (the readonly workmate spawn path — that one belongs to task T3, NOT to you). Two of the denied names are from a different agent harness and do not exist here, and this harness rejects the WHOLE restriction call when any name is unknown, so the read-only discipline silently became 'no spawn at all'. The existing unit tests only assert the deny array's construction against a stub adapter, so they never caught it.\\n\\nNote the likely-honoured trap: the roster's read-only guarantee is a security-ish property (read-only specialists must not be able to write files). Fix the mechanism, verify the authority is unchanged, and do not 'fix' it by simply deleting the restriction.\\n\\nScope boundary: keep the workmate-side line out of your diff (T3 changes it) and do not touch the bundle client or the docs. The QA skill at skills/dsh-qa is yours for the new case; follow its discipline (SKILL.md case table, --self-test on every script, evidence under evidence/, isolated DSH_HOME with HOME=<sandbox>, credentials copied once into the sandbox, stdio to files rather than pipes for long-lived MCP children).\", \"inScope\": [\"packages/mpd-roles-plugin/\", \"skills/dsh-qa/scripts/\", \"evidence/workmate/roles-readonly/\"], \"nonGoals\": [\"The workmate-side READONLY_DENY line (T3 owns it)\", \"Changing the roster, its personas or its model routes\", \"Widening or removing the read-only restriction itself\", \"The Workmates GUI and documentation (T4/T7 own them)\"], \"outOfScope\": [\"packages/mpd-workmate-plugin/\", \"packages/mpd-bundle-plugin/\", \"AGENTS.md\", \"docs/\"], \"objective\": \"Fix the live defect that makes read-only specialist spawn (mpd_role_spawn) and read-only workmate spawn fail on this harness: the tool deny lists name global tools this harness does not register (str_replace_editor, apply_patch), and the harness rejects the entire restriction call, so no read-only spawn can be created at all. Prove the fix against the REAL dsh tool registry, keep read-only authority intact, and leave a regression that would catch the next stale name.\", \"round\": 1, \"subject\": \"Fix read-only deny lists so read-only spawn works on the real harness\", \"verify\": [\"bun test packages/mpd-roles-plugin/test\", \"bun run test:qa\", \"bun run typecheck\"]}"}],"source":{"kind":"model","provider":"deepseek-official","model":"deepseek-v4-flash"},"id":"53e199ef-3599-49d1-9ed9-881003573162"},"usage":{"inputTokens":206,"outputTokens":1149,"totalTokens":108235,"cacheReadTokens":106880,"reasoningTokens":32}},"sourceEventSeqs":[[34800,35839]],"surfaceOp":"append"}
