evidence/agent-teams/scheduler-wakeup-fix/2026-09-10T10-16-23Z/captain-session-f333e946.jsonl:1507:{"type":"assistant/chunk","seq":39378,"time":1789027138726,"data":{"turn":1,"step":17,"chunk":{"type":"block-end","index":0,"block":{"type":"reasoning","text":"Interesting — RV1 became t7 (id), not \"RV1\". Task ids are t1..tN. So my planned T7 (docs) will become t8 and T8 (integration) t9. Let me keep track:\n\n- t1 requirements (Planner)\n- t2 dossier (Explorer)\n- t3 core impl (Senior Engineer)\n- t4 GUI impl (Junior Engineer)\n- t5 readonly fix (Deep Worker)\n- t6 verification (Reviewer)\n- t7 review of t3 (Architect)\n- t8 review of t4 (Plan Reviewer) — to create\n- t9 review of t5 (Senior Engineer) — to create\n- t10 docs/sync (Lead) — to create\n- t11 integration (Lead) — to create\n\nLet me create t8 and t9 now."}}}}
evidence/agent-teams/scheduler-wakeup-fix/2026-09-10T10-16-23Z/captain-session-f333e946.jsonl:1508:{"type":"assistant/chunk","seq":39379,"time":1789027138726,"data":{"turn":1,"step":17,"chunk":{"type":"block-end","index":1,"block":{"type":"tool-call","id":"call_00_SOnsh5zjeO2IezM4qEfS9579","name":"agent_teams_create_task","arguments":"{\"acceptance\": [\"Wire-contract conformance is verified call by call against T1 (path, method, request payload, response handling, error handling); any drift is a finding.\", \"Every string the change adds is present in both the zh and en dictionaries with identical key sets; a missing key in either language is at least a high finding.\", \"The destructive flow is human-safe: an explicit confirmation step, wording that matches the archive-first semantics (so the user is not misled into thinking data is destroyed when it is archived, or vice versa), no single click that irreversibly destroys a workmate, and a readable actionable message when the host refuses a mutation because the workmate is in use.\", \"The sidebar design constraints hold in the shipped artifact: still sidebar-only with no floating fallback or footer toggle, single: true, no stale detail polling or 404 loop after a mutation, unguarded service declarations not reintroduced, and the rebuilt client.js actually contains the new UI.\", \"The UI is judged against the LATEST state of the code, including any repair that already ran.\", \"Verdict is pass only with zero unresolved blocker/high findings; otherwise the task fails with structured findings (id, severity, problem, requiredFix) naming the exact file and the required correction.\"], \"assignee\": \"Plan Reviewer\", \"dependencies\": [\"t4\"], \"description\": \"Review the GUI half (task t4) as both a contract-conformance reviewer and a UI/UX critic. Read the T1 wire contract, then the real sources: packages/mpd-bundle-plugin/src/web-client.js (the WorkmateLibraryView component, the request() helper, the WORKMATE_LOCALE_NAMESPACE zh+en dictionaries, registerWorkmateSidebarTab) and the rebuilt packages/mpd-bundle-plugin/client.js. The tests to cross-check are packages/mpd-bundle-plugin/test/sidebar-tab.test.mjs, test/client-harness.mjs and test/team-page.test.mjs.\\n\\nAttack in particular:\\n- does the flow actually let a human rename a workmate and delete one, with the archive-first semantics clearly communicated rather than hidden behind a destructive-looking button?\\n- what happens to the view when a mutation succeeds, when it is refused because the workmate is in use, when the host returns an error, and when the selected workmate disappears underneath the detail view?\\n- are the zh and en key sets genuinely identical, and is the Chinese wording natural and accurate (not a literal translation of a wrong English string)?\\n- is the shipped bundle actually rebuilt and does it still respect the sidebar-only decision (the build script fails the build if the removed floater/toggle come back) and the seam policy that a declared-but-unregistered service takes the whole page down?\\n\\nYou are a read-only role: report findings, do not edit files. A 'pass' verdict with an unverified criterion is worse than a 'needs_revision' with a real finding.\", \"nonGoals\": [\"Editing any file\", \"Reviewing the core library implementation (t3) or the roles fix (t5)\", \"Re-litigating decisions the user already made\"], \"objective\": \"Review the Workmates tab rename/delete UI as a UI/UX and contract-conformance critic: does it let a human rename and safely delete a workmate, does it match the T1 wire contract exactly, are all zh/en strings complete and accurate, and are the destructive path, refusal messaging, stale-selection handling and sidebar-only constraints sound in the shipped client bundle?\", \"reviewedTaskId\": \"t4\", \"round\": 1, \"subject\": \"Review: Workmates tab rename/delete UI, zh/en strings, rebuilt client\"}"}}}}
evidence/agent-teams/scheduler-wakeup-fix/2026-09-10T10-16-23Z/captain-session-f333e946.jsonl:1509:{"type":"assistant/chunk","seq":39380,"time":1789027138727,"data":{"turn":1,"step":17,"chunk":{"type":"block-end","index":2,"block":{"type":"tool-call","id":"call_01_YURB6Kp9Vo6E2kkVprEs3263","name":"agent_teams_create_task","arguments":"{\"acceptance\": [\"The root cause is confirmed against the harness's real tool registry and the fix is shown to remove it, with before/after evidence cited (not merely asserted).\", \"The proof is evaluated for real-harness fidelity: the regression or QA case must have been able to fail on the pre-fix state and must pass after it; an assertion that only exercises a stub or a constructed array is a finding.\", \"Read-only authority is verified not to have widened — after the fix, a read-only role still cannot write files (no write/edit/apply_patch-class tool becomes available), and the mechanism cannot silently degrade to 'no restriction' in a future harness.\", \"The QA case follows the repo's discipline: isolated DSH_HOME and HOME, sandbox path asserted, no real credentials or real home touched, stdio handled safely, self-test present and passing, and a matching SKILL.md case-table row.\", \"The fix is judged against the LATEST state of the code, including any repair that already ran.\", \"Verdict is pass only with zero unresolved blocker/high findings; otherwise the task fails with structured findings (id, severity, problem, requiredFix) naming the exact file and the required correction.\"], \"assignee\": \"Senior Engineer\", \"dependencies\": [\"t5\"], \"description\": \"Review the read-only deny-list fix (task t5), which unblocked a defect that made every read-only spawn fail on this harness. You did not implement t5, so this is an independent review.\\n\\nAttack in particular:\\n- was the diagnosis correct and complete? The harness rejects the ENTIRE restriction call when any name is unknown, so the original symptom was 'read-only role cannot be spawned at all' — confirm the fix removes that, and check whether the same class of staleness exists anywhere else in the tree (other toolFilter/deny lists), reporting it as a finding rather than fixing it.\\n- is the mechanism robust (derived from or validated against the live registry) or a one-off literal patch that will rot again when the harness renames a tool?\\n- does the verification actually exercise the real dsh (isolated home, real boot, real spawn path) rather than a stub adapter? Cross-check the evidence under evidence/workmate/roles-readonly/.\\n- did the read-only guarantee survive: the point of the list is that read-only specialists must not write, so a fix that weakens or voids the restriction is a blocker, not a pass.\\n- does the new QA case follow skills/dsh-qa discipline (SKILL.md case table, --self-test, evidence path, isolated homes, credentials handling)?\\n\\nYou are a worker role, so you may inspect anything and run commands, but do not change t5's files: report findings instead.\", \"nonGoals\": [\"Editing the files under review\", \"Reviewing t3 (Architect) or t4 (Plan Reviewer)\", \"Changing the roster or the read-only policy itself\"], \"objective\": \"Review the read-only deny-list defect fix on diagnosis correctness and proof strength: does the deny list now name only tools this harness registers, is the mechanism robust rather than a literal patch, does the regression genuinely exercise the real harness and fail pre-fix, and did the fix preserve read-only authority?\", \"reviewedTaskId\": \"t5\", \"round\": 1, \"subject\": \"Review: read-only deny-list fix and its real-harness proof\"}"}}}}
