nd t11."},{"type":"tool-call","id":"call_00_jBb1oz0jH5g4ZyGxrd0S8930","name":"agent_teams_create_task","arguments":"{\"acceptance\": [\"packages/mpd-workmate-plugin/README.md and README.zh-CN.md are both updated to document the new tools, routes and semantics (archive-first delete, in-use refusal, ASCII-only naming, rename cascade) with the language switch link directly under each title; neither version is left stale.\", \"Every other human-facing doc that enumerates workmate capability is synced in BOTH languages in the same change (README pair at the root, docs/user-guide pair, docs/index pair, packages/mpd-bundle and packages/mpd-bundle-plugin README pairs) — the repo's binding bilingual rule means a change to one language version without the other is an unfinished change.\", \"AGENTS.md carries the new tool names in the workmate tool surface, an updated workmate glossary entry, and troubleshooting rows for the new failure modes (refused because the workmate is in use, restoring an archived instance, rejected invalid/CJK name), all in English.\", \"Any preset or bundle-patch text that enumerates the workmate tools is synced, and the QA scripts that pin the workmate route literals (skills/dsh-qa/scripts/workmate-library.mjs, skills/dsh-qa/scripts/web-client-adapt.mjs) assert the new routes, with SKILL.md's case table matching reality and all self-tests passing.\", \"Docs claim nothing the shipped code does not do: every documented tool name, argument, route, status code and refusal semantic is checked against the shipped sources and the verification evidence rather than copied from the contract draft.\"], \"assignee\": \"Lead\", \"dependencies\": [\"t3\", \"t4\", \"t5\", \"t6\"], \"description\": \"Sync every documentation and QA-assertion surface with what actually shipped, in both languages, in one coherent pass. Start from the verification evidence (t6) and the contract (t1) so the docs describe verified behaviour rather than intentions.\\n\\nThe repo's binding rules you must honour: agent-facing content (AGENTS.md, code comments, QA scripts) is English-only; every human-facing doc ships BOTH an English file and a 简体中文 *.zh-CN.md translation kept in sync in the same change, each carrying the language switch link directly under its title; process artifacts (docs/plan-*.md, docs/decisions.md, prior-phase reports) and internal QA/golden reference docs are exempt from the bilingual rule. Check which docs genuinely enumerate workmate capability and update only those — do not mass-rewrite docs that merely mention the word.\\n\\nAlso worth fixing while you are here: anything the traversal dossier (t2) flagged as a doc-vs-code contradiction, if it touches the workmate surface.\\n\\nScope boundary: do not change implementation code (t3/t4/t5 own it) and do not touch the read-only-spawn QA case or its SKILL.md row (t5 owns them) — append your rows without disturbing theirs.\", \"inScope\": [\"AGENTS.md\", \"README.md\", \"README.zh-CN.md\", \"docs/\", \"packages/mpd-workmate-plugin/README.md\", \"packages/mpd-workmate-plugin/README.zh-CN.md\", \"packages/mpd-bundle/README.md\", \"packages/mpd-bundle/README.zh-CN.md\", \"packages/mpd-bundle-plugin/README.md\", \"packages/mpd-bundle-plugin/README.zh-CN.md\", \"packages/mpd-bundle/cordis.patch.yml\", \"presets/\", \"skills/dsh-qa/scripts/workmate-library.mjs\", \"skills/dsh-qa/scripts/web-client-adapt.mjs\", \"skills/dsh-qa/SKILL.md\", \"evidence/workmate/rename-delete-docs/\"], \"nonGoals\": [\"Changing implementation code\", \"The read-only-spawn QA case and its SKILL.md row (t5 owns them)\", \"Mass-rewriting docs that only mention the word workmate in passing\", \"Translating internal process artifacts that are exempt from the bilingual rule\"], \"outOfScope\": [\"packages/mpd-workmate-plugin/src/\", \"packages/mpd-bundle-plugin/src/\", \"packages/mpd-social-plugin/\", \"packages/mpd-roles-plugin/src/\"], \"objective\": \"Bring every human-facing document (bilingual EN + zh-CN), the agent-facing manual, the preset/bundle texts and the QA assertions in line with the shipped rename/delete feature and the read-only deny fix — so no surface still describes the old tool set, and every documented statement matches what the verification actually proved.\", \"round\": 1, \"subject\": \"Bilingual docs + QA assertion sync for workmate rename/delete\", \"verify\": [\"bun run test:qa\", \"bun test packages/mpd-bundle-plugin/test\", \"bun run typecheck\"]}"}],"source":{"kind":"model","provider":"deepseek-official","model":"deepseek-v4-flash"},"id":"d05ec4b1-f3d2-406a-aac2-af4fc3b2d162"},"usage":{"inputTokens":240,"outputTokens":2740,"totalTokens":115108,"cacheReadTokens":112128,"reasoningTokens":1569}},"sourceEventSeqs":[[39390,42010]],"surfaceOp":"append"}
