evidence/agent-teams/scheduler-wakeup-fix/2026-09-10T10-16-23Z/captain-session-f333e946.jsonl:1766:{"type":"assistant/chunk","seq":46102,"time":1789027178651,"data":{"turn":1,"step":22,"chunk":{"type":"block-end","index":0,"block":{"type":"reasoning","text":"Let me verify the staged plan with agent_teams_status, then write my final message.\n\nAlso: should the roster need any member additions? The profile already has all 11 members. I used: Planner, Explorer, Senior Engineer, Junior Engineer, Deep Worker, Reviewer, Architect, Plan Reviewer, Lead = 9. Unused: Researcher, Vision Analyst. That's fine (unassigned members produce no work — and the protocol says never wait for unassigned members). Should I give Researcher something? Not necessary — but the user's request included \"遍历工程，了解工程详细信息\" which is assigned to Explorer; Researcher could add an external/OSS evidence angle... Not needed; avoid busywork. Vision Analyst — no images in this work. Fine: they stay idle.\n\nLet me check status to confirm the plan and then compose the final message.\n\nAlso I should record a memory write for the requirements decisions (self-iteration rule: persist concise entries after meaningful milestones). Let me do that as part of this turn — it's a meaningful milestone (requirements agreed). And check memory status/reflection. Good practice per my instructions.\n\nLet me do: status + mpd_memory_write in parallel."}}}}
evidence/agent-teams/scheduler-wakeup-fix/2026-09-10T10-16-23Z/captain-session-f333e946.jsonl:1768:{"type":"assistant/chunk","seq":46104,"time":1789027178652,"data":{"turn":1,"step":22,"chunk":{"type":"block-end","index":2,"block":{"type":"tool-call","id":"call_01_X0er5aNKFWNtG6YXFZPU4227","name":"mpd_memory_write","arguments":"{\"title\": \"Workmate rename/delete — agreed requirements (2026-09-10)\", \"kind\": \"note\", \"description\": \"User-approved requirements for adding workmate rename + delete to mpd-workmate-plugin, including five binding decisions and the discovered read-only deny-list defect.\", \"tags\": [\"workmate\", \"mpd-workmate-plugin\", \"requirements\", \"agent-teams\"], \"content\": \"Goal: 遍历工程 + 优化 workmate 系统 — (1) rename a workmate, (2) delete a workmate.\\n\\nFive user decisions (binding):\\nD1 Delete = archive-first: default move to ~/.mpd/workmate/.archive/<name>-<ISO>/ (hidden from list/match, restorable); real removal only via explicit purge; GUI gets a confirmation step.\\nD2 In-use gate + full cascade: refuse rename/delete while the workmate is in use (in-flight spawn in this process; a member bound by name in a live/non-archived team). Once allowed, update ALL library-owned name references (dir key, meta.name, index.json key, note.md self-reference, continuity metadata). Archived team records are historical — never rewritten.\\nD3 The read-only deny-list defect is IN scope: READONLY_DENY (mpd-roles-plugin/src/index.ts ~L23-27 and mpd-workmate-plugin/src/index.ts L30) names tools this harness does not register (str_replace_editor, apply_patch) and the harness rejects the WHOLE tools.restrict() call, so every read-only spawn (mpd_role_spawn, readonly workmate) fails. Existing tests only asserted the constructed array against a stub.\\nD4 Surface = agent tools + web routes + Workmates sidebar GUI (zh/en).\\nD5 ASCII-only key scheme now: names limited to [a-z0-9_-]; invalid/empty-sanitized names rejected BEFORE any fs call. Hazard: sanitizeName(\\\"\\\") === \\\"\\\" and wmDir(\\\"\\\") IS the library root.\\n\\nKey facts measured: workmate binding is name-equality only (packages/mpd-agent-teams-plugin/lib/members.js#workmateKey vs mpd-workmate's sanitizeName — must stay byte-identical); no cordis service exists for agent-teams state (only agent_teams_* tools); index.json has no reader today; the Workmates tab is DSH-better-sidebar-only (no floating fallback) with zh as locale key-set source of truth and a required `node scripts/build-mpd-client.mjs` rebuild.\\n\\nTeam: staged \\\"MPD Default\\\" (profile mpd, 11 members, captain planning) with DAG t1..t12: requirements (Planner) -> core impl (Senior Engineer) + GUI impl (Junior Engineer) parallel, read-only fix (Deep Worker) -> verification (Reviewer) + 3 reviews (Architect/Plan Reviewer/Senior Engineer) -> bilingual docs+QA sync (Lead) -> integration (Lead).\"}"}}}}
