alling ONLY the T1-pinned routes, methods and payloads.\", \"Every user-visible string added exists in BOTH the zh and en dictionaries with identical key sets (zh remains the key-set source of truth).\", \"After a rename the view follows to the new name or returns to the refreshed list; after a delete it returns to the list; no stale detail polling, no 404 loop, no second tab.\", \"An in-use refusal returned by the host surfaces as a readable, actionable message (naming why the mutation was refused), never as an unhandled failure or a silent no-op.\", \"The tab stays sidebar-only (no floating fallback, no footer toggle reintroduced) and the sidebar seam policy (ctx.inject(['betterSidebar']), probe-never-throw for optional seams) is unchanged.\", \"node scripts/build-mpd-client.mjs succeeds, the committed packages/mpd-bundle-plugin/client.js contains the new UI markers, and bun test packages/mpd-bundle-plugin/test passes.\", \"Evidence written under evidence/workmate/rename-delete-gui/<timestamp>/ (build output plus the test run).\"], \"dependencies\": [\"t1\"], \"description\": \"Deliver the human-facing half of the feature in the existing Workmates DSH-better-sidebar tab. Read the T1 wire contract first and treat it as binding — call exactly those routes and payloads; if the contract is missing something the UI needs, report it in your task output rather than inventing a route.\\n\\nSource of truth is packages/mpd-bundle-plugin/src/web-client.js: the WorkmateLibraryView component, its list/detail/init form, the request() helper, the WORKMATE_LOCALE_NAMESPACE zh+en dictionaries, SIDEBAR_TAB_ID=\\\"mpd-workmate\\\" and registerWorkmateSidebarTab. The tab is sidebar-only BY DESIGN (the old overlay floater and footer toggle were deliberately removed and the build fails if they come back), it is single: true, and it must never reintroduce an unguarded service declaration: optional seams are probed through ctx.get behind a helper that never throws (see the AGENTS.md troubleshooting rows and packages/mpd-bundle-plugin/test/sidebar-tab.test.mjs, which pins this seam policy).\\n\\nAfter editing the source you MUST rebuild the shipped client with `node scripts/build-mpd-client.mjs`, otherwise the bundle shows nothing new.\\n\\nScope boundary: the host tools and web routes belong to the core implementation task; documentation and QA scripts belong to the docs task. Do not touch them.\", \"inScope\": [\"packages/mpd-bundle-plugin/src/web-client.js\", \"packages/mpd-bundle-plugin/test/\", \"packages/mpd-bundle-plugin/client.js\", \"evidence/workmate/rename-delete-gui/\"], \"kind\": \"implementation\", \"nonGoals\": [\"Adding or changing the host-side routes and tools (the core task owns them)\", \"The AgentTeams page (src/team-page.js) except where a test requires keeping its assertions intact\", \"Documentation and QA scripts (the docs task owns them)\"], \"objective\": \"Give the Workmates sidebar tab a real rename and delete flow wired to the T1 wire contract: rename with a prefilled input, delete behind an explicit confirmation that matches archive-first semantics, bilingual (zh/en) strings with identical key sets, correct stale-selection handling after a mutation, a readable surface for an in-use refusal, and a rebuilt packages/mpd-bundle-plugin/client.js so the change actually ships.\", \"outOfScope\": [\"packages/mpd-workmate-plugin/\", \"packages/mpd-roles-plugin/\", \"packages/mpd-bundle-plugin/src/team-page.js\", \"AGENTS.md\", \"docs/\"], \"round\": 1, \"subject\": \"Workmates sidebar tab: rename + delete controls (zh/en) and rebuilt client\", \"verify\": [\"node scripts/build-mpd-client.mjs\", \"bun test packages/mpd-bundle-plugin/test\", \"bun run typecheck\"]}"}],"source":{"kind":"model","provider":"deepseek-official","model":"deepseek-v4-flash"},"id":"caf7b3e1-f66d-4e13-91ac-fb70055f89bb"},"usage":{"inputTokens":199,"outputTokens":2408,"totalTokens":134319,"cacheReadTokens":131712,"reasoningTokens":100}},"sourceEventSeqs":[