ist).\\n\\nThe deny list lives at packages/mpd-roles-plugin/src/index.ts (READONLY_DENY, ~line 23-27, used at ~line 123 as `toolFilter: { deny: READONLY_DENY }` when spec.readonly). Two of the denied names come from a different agent harness and do not exist here, and this harness rejects the WHOLE restriction call when any name is unknown, so the read-only discipline silently became 'no spawn at all'. The existing unit tests only assert the deny array's construction against a stub adapter, so they never caught it. A sibling line exists in mpd-workmate-plugin (line 30) but it belongs to the core implementation task, NOT to you — do not touch it.\\n\\nNote the trap: the roster's read-only guarantee is a security-ish property (read-only specialists must not be able to write files). Fix the mechanism, verify the authority is unchanged, and do not 'fix' it by simply deleting the restriction.\\n\\nThe QA skill at skills/dsh-qa is yours for the new case; follow its discipline (SKILL.md case table, --self-test on every script, evidence under evidence/, isolated DSH_HOME with HOME=<sandbox>, credentials copied once into the sandbox, stdio to files rather than pipes for long-lived MCP children).\", \"inScope\": [\"packages/mpd-roles-plugin/\", \"skills/dsh-qa/scripts/\", \"evidence/workmate/roles-readonly/\"], \"kind\": \"implementation\", \"nonGoals\": [\"The workmate-side READONLY_DENY line (the core implementation task owns it)\", \"Changing the roster, its personas or its model routes\", \"Widening or removing the read-only restriction itself\", \"The Workmates GUI and documentation (other tasks own them)\"], \"objective\": \"Fix the live defect that makes read-only specialist spawn (mpd_role_spawn) and read-only workmate spawn fail on this harness: the tool deny lists name global tools this harness does not register (str_replace_editor, apply_patch), and the harness rejects the entire restriction call, so no read-only spawn can be created at all. Prove the fix against the REAL dsh tool registry, keep read-only authority intact, and leave a regression that would catch the next stale name.\", \"outOfScope\": [\"packages/mpd-workmate-plugin/\", \"packages/mpd-bundle-plugin/\", \"AGENTS.md\", \"docs/\"], \"round\": 1, \"subject\": \"Fix read-only deny lists so read-only spawn works on the real harness\", \"verify\": [\"bun test packages/mpd-roles-plugin/test\", \"bun run test:qa\", \"bun run typecheck\"]}"}}
