evidence/agent-teams/scheduler-wakeup-fix/2026-09-10T10-16-23Z/captain-session-f333e946.jsonl:2246:{"type":"assistant/chunk","seq":57961,"time":1789027254220,"data":{"turn":1,"step":34,"chunk":{"type":"block-end","index":0,"block":{"type":"reasoning","text":"Now Wave B: verification (deps t15,t16,t17) + 3 reviews (reviewedTaskId t15/t16/t17 with deps).\n\nLet me create all 4 in one block.\n\nFor reviews: include dependencies [reviewed task]. If rejected, retry without.\n\nNote for the verification task: kind=verification requires objective+acceptance; will it require a dependency on an implementation task? Probably. I give deps [t15,t16,t17].\n\nLet me write them (reusing the earlier text, updating task references)."}}}}
evidence/agent-teams/scheduler-wakeup-fix/2026-09-10T10-16-23Z/captain-session-f333e946.jsonl:2247:{"type":"assistant/chunk","seq":57962,"time":1789027254221,"data":{"turn":1,"step":34,"chunk":{"type":"block-end","index":1,"block":{"type":"tool-call","id":"call_00_AuMLJ5YzotGqEoc4pyX18644","name":"agent_teams_create_task","arguments":"{\"acceptance\": [\"Every AGENTS.md §4 gate is run on the integrated tree with real output recorded: bun test packages, bun run typecheck, bun run test:qa, node scripts/verify-vendor.mjs, and a `dsh --profile headless --dump-config` boot in an isolated DSH_HOME.\", \"A real sandbox-HOME lifecycle exercise demonstrates, from the outside (tools/service/routes, not by reading the implementer's code): rename preserves persona/memory/note/uses/createdAt and frees the old key; delete archives by default and the instance is restorable from .archive/; purge removes it; list/match/service views agree with the filesystem immediately after every mutation.\", \"Negative cases demonstrably behave: invalid/empty/CJK/punctuation-only names are rejected before any filesystem call with the library root untouched; unknown names error with zero side effects; a repeated delete errors; a rename collision is refused; a rename or delete is refused while the workmate is in use.\", \"The new web routes answer per the T1 contract on a real boot (correct status codes for success, invalid body, unknown name, wrong verb) and the read-only spawn path is demonstrated to work against the real harness.\", \"Every command result is recorded in commandsRun with exit codes and evidence, and results.json/output.log are written under evidence/workmate/rename-delete-verify/<timestamp>/.\", \"The real HOME and the real ~/.dsh are never touched (the sandbox path is asserted in the evidence).\"], \"dependencies\": [\"t15\", \"t16\", \"t17\"], \"description\": \"Verify the delivered feature independently. Do not trust the implementers' summaries: reproduce from the real artifacts (source, built dist, real dsh boot, sandboxed filesystem) and treat any mismatch between a claim and the observed behaviour as a finding you report — you do not fix code yourself.\\n\\nMethod that fits this repo: follow the dsh-qa discipline (skills/dsh-qa) — an isolated DSH_HOME and HOME per run, credentials copied once into the sandbox, sandbox paths asserted, evidence written under evidence/<domain>/<slug>/<timestamp>/{result.json,output.log}, and long-lived MCP children run with stdio to files rather than pipes. The workmate library lives under $HOME, so every lifecycle exercise MUST run with HOME pointing at a sandbox and the evidence must show it.\\n\\nPay particular attention to the cases where a naive implementation is quietly wrong: a name that sanitizes to an empty string (wmDir(\\\"\\\") is the library root itself), a rename that loses evolved memory or bumps uses, a delete that leaves the index stale or removes only part of the instance, a mutation racing an in-flight spawn, and a GUI-visible route that answers 200 on an unknown name.\\n\\nIf something fails, report it as a failed verification with the exact command, exit code and output — the scheduler turns that into a repair loop. Do not edit implementation files.\", \"inScope\": [\"evidence/workmate/rename-delete-verify/\"], \"kind\": \"verification\", \"nonGoals\": [\"Fixing anything yourself\", \"Approving the implementation\", \"Editing package sources, docs or QA scripts\"], \"objective\": \"Independently verify the shipped rename/delete feature and the read-only deny fix against the REAL harness and the REAL gates: run every gate, exercise the full lifecycle and its negative cases with HOME pointed at a sandbox, boot the bundle in an isolated DSH_HOME, confirm the web routes and the read-only spawn path behave as contracted, and leave reproducible evidence on disk.\", \"outOfScope\": [\"packages/\", \"AGENTS.md\", \"docs/\", \"skills/dsh-qa/scripts/\"], \"round\": 1, \"subject\": \"Independent verification: rename/delete end-to-end, negative cases, full gate sweep\", \"verify\": [\"bun test packages\", \"bun run typecheck\", \"bun run test:qa\", \"node scripts/verify-vendor.mjs\"]}"}}}}
evidence/agent-teams/scheduler-wakeup-fix/2026-09-10T10-16-23Z/captain-session-f333e946.jsonl:2248:{"type":"assistant/chunk","seq":57963,"time":1789027254221,"data":{"turn":1,"step":34,"chunk":{"type":"block-end","index":2,"block":{"type":"tool-call","id":"call_01_DioKTENo4FBUanLfW3qd6022","name":"agent_teams_create_task","arguments":"{\"acceptance\": [\"Every T1 acceptance criterion is checked against the shipped code and the on-disk evidence, each with an explicit pass/fail and a concrete citation (file/line or command output).\", \"The review actively tries to falsify the invariants and reports any counterexample: name↔dir↔index bijection and root safety; rename is identity-preserving and never a re-instantiation; delete is complete and all-or-nothing; the cross-module binding outcome is deterministic with no state where directory, index.json, service view and team-member backing disagree.\", \"Race and failure analysis covers: a reflect landing after a rename (old-directory resurrection), reflect/delete ordering, partial failure between the directory move and the metadata write, and whether the in-use refusal gate actually closes the in-flight race.\", \"The implementation is judged against the LATEST state of the code, including any repair that already ran — not against the first submitted version.\", \"Verdict is pass only with zero unresolved blocker/high findings; otherwise the task fails with structured findings (id, severity, problem, requiredFix) naming the exact file and the required correction.\"], \"dependencies\": [\"t15\"], \"description\": \"Adversarially review the core implementation task t15 on the axes where a mistake is expensive and hard to see. Read the T1 contract first, then the actual code in packages/mpd-workmate-plugin/src/index.ts, the tests and the evidence — and treat the implementer's summary as a claim to be checked, not as fact.\\n\\nSpecific things to attack:\\n- sanitizeName as the single key algorithm: can any input reach a filesystem call before validation? What exactly happens for an empty sanitized name, a CJK name, a punctuation-only name, a name differing only by case, and a name colliding after sanitization?\\n- rename identity: is the evolved instance really moved rather than recreated? Are persona/memory/note content, the caps, uses, lastTask and createdAt preserved? Is the note self-reference and the continuity metadata consistent with the new name?\\n- delete: archive-first behaviour, hidden-from-list/match, restorability, purge, index-key removal, and all-or-nothing failure behaviour.\\n- the in-use gate: does it really prevent the spawn/reflect race, or does it only shift the window? Is the chosen detection mechanism sound in this harness, and does it avoid writing to another plugin's state?\\n- index.json: it has no reader today — judge whether the rename/delete handling leaves it consistent and whether the contract's treatment of it is defensible.\\n- the workmate-side READONLY_DENY correction (part of t15): does it actually fix readonly spawn, and does it keep read-only authority intact?\\n\\nYou are a read-only role: report findings, do not edit files. A 'pass' verdict with an unverified criterion is worse than a 'needs_revision' with a real finding.\", \"kind\": \"review\", \"nonGoals\": [\"Editing any file\", \"Reviewing the GUI task or the roles-plugin fix task\", \"Re-litigating decisions the user already made\"], \"objective\": \"Adversarially review the core rename/delete implementation against the T1 contract and the four invariants: root safety and name validation, identity-preserving rename, complete all-or-nothing delete, and deterministic behaviour under races and partial failure. Judge the latest code state and cite evidence for every claim.\", \"reviewedTaskId\": \"t15\", \"round\": 1, \"subject\": \"Review: core rename/delete implementation (safety, identity, atomicity, races)\"}"}}}}
evidence/agent-teams/scheduler-wakeup-fix/2026-09-10T10-16-23Z/captain-session-f333e946.jsonl:2251:{"type":"assistant/message","seq":57966,"time":1789027254223,"data":{"turn":1,"step":34,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"reasoning","text":"Now Wave B: verification (deps t15,t16,t17) + 3 reviews (reviewedTaskId t15/t16/t17 with deps).\n\nLet me create all 4 in one block.\n\nFor reviews: include dependencies [reviewed task]. If rejected, retry without.\n\nNote for the verification task: kind=verification requires objective+acceptance; will it require a dependency on an implementation task? Probably. I give deps [t15,t16,t17].\n\nLet me write them (reusing the earlier text, updating task references)."},{"type":"tool-call","id":"call_00_AuMLJ5YzotGqEoc4pyX18644","name":"agent_teams_create_task","arguments":"{\"acceptance\": [\"Every AGENTS.md §4 gate is run on the integrated tree with real output recorded: bun test packages, bun run typecheck, bun run test:qa, node scripts/verify-vendor.mjs, and a `dsh --profile headless --dump-config` boot in an isolated DSH_HOME.\", \"A real sandbox-HOME lifecycle exercise demonstrates, from the outside (tools/service/routes, not by reading the implementer's code): rename preserves persona/memory/note/uses/createdAt and frees the old key; delete archives by default and the instance is restorable from .archive/; purge removes it; list/match/service views agree with the filesystem immediately after every mutation.\", \"Negative cases demonstrably behave: invalid/empty/CJK/punctuation-only names are rejected before any filesystem call with the library root untouched; unknown names error with zero side effects; a repeated delete errors; a rename collision is refused; a rename or delete is refused while the workmate is in use.\", \"The new web routes answer per the T1 contract on a real boot (correct status codes for success, invalid body, unknown name, wrong verb) and the read-only spawn path is demonstrated to work against the real harness.\", \"Every command result is recorded in commandsRun with exit codes and evidence, and results.json/output.log are written under evidence/workmate/rename-delete-verify/<timestamp>/.\", \"The real HOME and the real ~/.dsh are never touched (the sandbox path is asserted in the evidence).\"], \"dependencies\": [\"t15\", \"t16\", \"t17\"], \"description\": \"Verify the delivered feature independently. Do not trust the implementers' summaries: reproduce from the real artifacts (source, built dist, real dsh boot, sandboxed filesystem) and treat any mismatch between a claim and the observed behaviour as a finding you report — you do not fix code yourself.\\n\\nMethod that fits this repo: follow the dsh-qa discipline (skills/dsh-qa) — an isolated DSH_HOME and HOME per run, credentials copied once into the sandbox, sandbox paths asserted, evidence written under evidence/<domain>/<slug>/<timestamp>/{result.json,output.log}, and long-lived MCP children run with stdio to files rather than pipes. The workmate library lives under $HOME, so every lifecycle exercise MUST run with HOME pointing at a sandbox and the evidence must show it.\\n\\nPay particular attention to the cases where a naive implementation is quietly wrong: a name that sanitizes to an empty string (wmDir(\\\"\\\") is the library root itself), a rename that loses evolved memory or bumps uses, a delete that leaves the index stale or removes only part of the instance, a mutation racing an in-flight spawn, and a GUI-visible route that answers 200 on an unknown name.\\n\\nIf something fails, report it as a failed verification with the exact command, exit code and output — the scheduler turns that into a repair loop. Do not edit implementation files.\", \"inScope\": [\"evidence/workmate/rename-delete-verify/\"], \"kind\": \"verification\", \"nonGoals\": [\"Fixing anything yourself\", \"Approving the implementation\", \"Editing package sources, docs or QA scripts\"], \"objective\": \"Independently verify the shipped rename/delete feature and the read-only deny fix against the REAL harness and the REAL gates: run every gate, exercise the full lifecycle and its negative cases with HOME pointed at a sandbox, boot the bundle in an isolated DSH_HOME, confirm the web routes and the read-only spawn path behave as contracted, and leave reproducible evidence on disk.\", \"outOfScope\": [\"packages/\", \"AGENTS.md\", \"docs/\", \"skills/dsh-qa/scripts/\"], \"round\": 1, \"subject\": \"Independent verification: rename/delete end-to-end, negative cases, full gate sweep\", \"verify\": [\"bun test packages\", \"bun run typecheck\", \"bun run test:qa\", \"node scripts/verify-vendor.mjs\"]}"},{"type":"tool-call","id":"call_01_DioKTENo4FBUanLfW3qd6022","name":"agent_teams_create_task","arguments":"{\"acceptance\": [\"Every T1 acceptance criterion is checked against the shipped code and the on-disk evidence, each with an explicit pass/fail and a concrete citation (file/line or command output).\", \"The review actively tries to falsify the invariants and reports any counterexample: name↔dir↔index bijection and root safety; rename is identity-preserving and never a re-instantiation; delete is complete and all-or-nothing; the cross-module binding outcome is deterministic with no state where directory, index.json, service view and team-member backing disagree.\", \"Race and failure analysis covers: a reflect landing after a rename (old-directory resurrection), reflect/delete ordering, partial failure between the directory move and the metadata write, and whether the in-use refusal gate actually closes the in-flight race.\", \"The implementation is judged against the LATEST state of the code, including any repair that already ran — not against the first submitted version.\", \"Verdict is pass only with zero unresolved blocker/high findings; otherwise the task fails with structured findings (id, severity, problem, requiredFix) naming the exact file and the required correction.\"], \"dependencies\": [\"t15\"], \"description\": \"Adversarially review the core implementation task t15 on the axes where a mistake is expensive and hard to see. Read the T1 contract first, then the actual code in packages/mpd-workmate-plugin/src/index.ts, the tests and the evidence — and treat the implementer's summary as a claim to be checked, not as fact.\\n\\nSpecific things to attack:\\n- sanitizeName as the single key algorithm: can any input reach a filesystem call before validation? What exactly happens for an empty sanitized name, a CJK name, a punctuation-only name, a name differing only by case, and a name colliding after sanitization?\\n- rename identity: is the evolved instance really moved rather than recreated? Are persona/memory/note content, the caps, uses, lastTask and createdAt preserved? Is the note self-reference and the continuity metadata consistent with the new name?\\n- delete: archive-first behaviour, hidden-from-list/match, restorability, purge, index-key removal, and all-or-nothing failure behaviour.\\n- the in-use gate: does it really prevent the spawn/reflect race, or does it only shift the window? Is the chosen detection mechanism sound in this harness, and does it avoid writing to another plugin's state?\\n- index.json: it has no reader today — judge whether the rename/delete handling leaves it consistent and whether the contract's treatment of it is defensible.\\n- the workmate-side READONLY_DENY correction (part of t15): does it actually fix readonly spawn, and does it keep read-only authority intact?\\n\\nYou are a read-only role: report findings, do not edit files. A 'pass' verdict with an unverified criterion is worse than a 'needs_revision' with a real finding.\", \"kind\": \"review\", \"nonGoals\": [\"Editing any file\", \"Reviewing the GUI task or the roles-plugin fix task\", \"Re-litigating decisions the user already made\"], \"objective\": \"Adversarially review the core rename/delete implementation against the T1 contract and the four invariants: root safety and name validation, identity-preserving rename, complete all-or-nothing delete, and deterministic behaviour under races and partial failure. Judge the latest code state and cite evidence for every claim.\", \"reviewedTaskId\": \"t15\", \"round\": 1, \"subject\": \"Review: core rename/delete implementation (safety, identity, atomicity, races)\"}"}],"source":{"kind":"model","provider":"deepseek-official","model":"deepseek-v4-flash"},"id":"d6a53416-d6e3-41fa-907c-4e323c14cc7a"},"usage":{"inputTokens":232,"outputTokens":1982,"totalTokens":137638,"cacheReadTokens":135424,"reasoningTokens":116}},"sourceEventSeqs":[[56193,57965]],"surfaceOp":"append"}
