evidence/agent-teams/scheduler-wakeup-fix/2026-09-10T10-16-23Z/captain-session-f333e946.jsonl:2507:{"type":"agent/inbox/spliced","seq":64323,"time":1789027336332,"data":{"target":"next-step","start":7,"inserted":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Agent beb66991-bb9a-47f0-bd8e-5b74bba14ae8 sent a message:"},{"type":"text","text":"Architect status — no work started (turn ended idle, as instructed).\n\nOwned task: t19 \"Review: core rename/delete implementation (safety, identity, atomicity, races)\" (deps: t15). Claim attempt rejected by the scheduler: \"task t19 is blocked by unfinished dependencies: t15\". No attempt_id exists yet, so nothing was claimed or modified.\n\nFull team snapshot: 11 tasks, all pending/attempt 0 (t1 requirements→Planner, t2 dossier→Explorer, t15 core impl→Senior Engineer, t16 sidebar tab→Junior Engineer, t17 read-only deny-list fix→Deep Worker, t18 verification→Reviewer, t19→Architect, t20→Plan Reviewer, t21→Senior Engineer, t22 docs→Lead, t23 integration→Lead). Those with `deps: t1` are also blocked, so no member can start yet.\n\nWhat unblocks me / what you should do next: nothing on my side. When t15 completes, the scheduler will make t19 ready and I will claim it, review the workmate rename/delete core against t15's changedPaths/acceptance evidence, and update with verdict=pass or a failed review carrying severity-tagged findings (id/severity/problem/requiredFix). If t15 slips or is reassigned, t19 stays parked — do not expect interim output from me.\n\nNote for the captain: the whole DAG currently hangs on t1 (requirements). If t1 (or any t15–t17 implementation) fails, the system will generate repair + next-review tasks automatically; t19 does not need manual recreation."}],"source":{"kind":"agent-message","form":"relay","senderSessionId":"beb66991-bb9a-47f0-bd8e-5b74bba14ae8"},"role":"user","id":"6e1e46aa-9401-47d5-a524-a24bdcf59ad2"}]}}
evidence/agent-teams/scheduler-wakeup-fix/2026-09-10T10-16-23Z/captain-session-f333e946.jsonl:2522:{"type":"agent/inbox/spliced","seq":64658,"time":1789027338072,"data":{"target":"next-step","start":9,"inserted":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Background subagent a4626f91-c3d1-497f-8587-87d96e6d39be finished and will do no further work unless you send it more."},{"type":"text","text":"Its closing message:"},{"type":"reasoning","text":"Wait — a subtlety: the send_message tool says \"Send a message to a direct continuable child by its agent id. If you are a resident continuable child, you may also target your direct parent.\" That worked.\n\nNow, I have no task to do in this turn. I should end my turn with a concise reply.\n\nHmm, but hold on — is there a risk that ending my turn now means I never get woken? Rule 6 says the scheduler may assign my next ready task automatically. And deps t1 → t15/t16/t17 → t18. Those are pending; the captain/scheduler will drive them. Also, there's a bit of a concern: 11 members all \"working/running\" but all tasks pending — meaning nothing is actually being executed? That may be because the captain hasn't kicked off. But that's the captain's business.\n\nActually wait, let me think more carefully. All tasks are pending with attempt 0, and all members show \"working/running\". That could mean each member is currently in their first turn (like me) waiting. The captain will manage. I shouldn't over-step.\n\nShould I perhaps proactively prepare for t18? I could do read-only reconnaissance of the repo so that when t18 unblocks I can verify quickly. But rule 8: \"Do not start a teammate's assigned task.\" Reading the repo isn't a task. But my turn should end. Given \"Do not start work until the scheduler or captain assigns a task in this turn\" — I must not start work.\n\nI'll end the turn with a concise reply."},{"type":"text","text":"Standing by — no work started this turn.\n\n**Status:** my only assignment is `t18` (verification r1: workmate rename/delete end-to-end, negative cases, full gate sweep), which is not ready: `t18` depends on `t15`/`t16`/`t17`, and all three depend on `t1` (requirements, still pending). Claiming it now would be a blocked claim, so I left it pending.\n\n**Next:** the scheduler/captain will wake me when `t15`–`t17` complete; I will then claim `t18`, run the independent verification/gate sweep, and report findings (with evidence) to the captain and the parent agent. I sent the parent a short standing-by note."}],"source":{"kind":"subagent-settled","form":"notice","summary":"Background subagent a4626f91-c3d1-497f-8587-87d96e6d39be finished and will do no further work unless you send it more.","senderSessionId":"a4626f91-c3d1-497f-8587-87d96e6d39be"},"role":"user","id":"2b8f215a-299d-401c-950c-f66ab41e0c70"}]}}
