n the plan runs). Since the plan is staged, adding a task is a plan edit, not a spawn. Good: no wake-up.\n\nLet me check playwright availability, then decide on adding the visual task.\n\nLet me also reconsider: is adding the visual QA task scope creep that the user didn't ask for? The user asked to traverse the project and optimize the workmate system with rename + delete. Verifying the GUI visually is part of delivering a GUI feature well. Given the roster includes a Vision Analyst asking for work and the repo has `visual-qa` skill + playwright browser cache, it's a reasonable, bounded addition. But plan bloat is a real cost: the user must review it.\n\nMiddle ground: add ONE visual-verification task (kind=verification, Vision Analyst, deps t16 + t22?) — placed after t16 so the UI exists, and it can run in parallel with t18's gate sweep. Then t23 integration depends on it too.\n\nHmm, but if t23 depends on it and it fails for environmental reasons, integration blocks. I could make it NOT a dependency of t23 (integration can proceed; the visual verdict is reported separately)... but then a failing visual task wouldn't gate delivery, which is odd for a quality gate. Standard practice: any quality task in the plan participates in the gate. The system may auto-handle failures with repair loops.\n\nLet me first check playwright. Decide after."},{"type":"text","text":"A wave of teammates checked in — all correctly idle, none claiming blocked work. The Vision Analyst's offer is legitimate though: a GUI change deserves rendered verification. Let me check whether this sandbox can actually drive a browser before amending the plan."},{"type":"tool-call","id":"call_00_TjjNN1T0IbLUDpqYCYgW6003","name":"bash","arguments":"{\"command\": \"echo \\\"=== playwright browser binaries ===\\\" ; ls -d ~/.cache/ms-playwright/*/ 2>/dev/null; ls ~/.cache/ms-playwright/chromium-1228/chrome-linux/chrome 2>/dev/null || echo \\\"no chrome binary\\\"; ls ~/.cache/ms-playwright/chromium_headless_shell-1228/chrome-linux/headless_shell 2>/dev/null || echo \\\"no headless_shell\\\"; echo; echo \\\"=== playwright/puppeteer packages anywhere relevant ===\\\"; for d in \\\"$(npm root -g 2>/dev/null)\\\" /root/.nvm/versions/node/v24.16.0/lib/node_modules /root/dshProj/my-power-dsh/node_modules /root/.bun/install/global/node_modules; do echo \\\"--- $d\\\"; ls \\\"$d\\\" 2>/dev/null | grep -iE 'playwright|puppeteer' || echo \\\"(none)\\\"; done\", \"description\": \"Check for a usable browser driver\"}"}],"source":{"kind":"model","provider":"deepseek-official","model":"deepseek-v4-flash"},"id":"d6d029e3-75a1-4c28-bb7f-5d29b69e5f29"},"usage":{"inputTokens":3083,"outputTokens":1885,"totalTokens":152296,"cacheReadTokens":147328,"reasoningTokens":1570}},"sourceEventSeqs":[[65397,67255]],"surfaceOp":"append"}
