evidence/agent-teams/scheduler-wakeup-fix/2026-09-10T10-16-23Z/captain-session-f333e946.jsonl:3463:{"type":"assistant/chunk","seq":87483,"time":1789027768644,"data":{"turn":3,"step":3,"chunk":{"type":"block-end","index":1,"block":{"type":"tool-call","id":"call_00_31ThbpkZIizjlwswSPMJ2271","name":"mpd_memory_write","arguments":"{\"content\": \"Defect class discovered while fixing the read-only deny list (mpd-roles-plugin + mpd-workmate-plugin):\\n\\nA tool name that appears in a patch file row, or that ships as an installed package, is NOT proof that the tool is registered in the live harness registry. In this dsh install `@deepseek-ai/dsh-tool-str-replace-editor` exists and dsh-base/cordis.patch.yml has a row for it, but the row is not composed into the active profile — so `str_replace_editor` is unregistered at spawn time.\\n\\nHow to test authoritatively: `ToolRuntime.restrict()` fails loudly and prints the live registry:\\n  Error: tools.restrict() names unknown global tools \\\"X\\\", \\\"Y\\\"; known global tools: <full list>\\nThat \\\"known global tools\\\" enumeration is the ground truth for the current profile. Measured for the mpd/web profile: it contains write, edit, mpd_hashline_edit, read, bash, ... but NOT str_replace_editor and NOT apply_patch.\\n\\nConsequence: BOTH str_replace_editor and apply_patch must be removed from every READONLY_DENY list (a subagent error report from the Planner claimed only apply_patch was dead and that str_replace_editor must be kept — verified wrong twice by live mpd_role_spawn). Correct list = the live-registered subset: [\\\"write\\\",\\\"edit\\\",\\\"mpd_hashline_edit\\\"].\\n\\nSecond trap, keep it: do NOT filter the deny list with `dsh.hasTool` — it reads the GLOBAL view only, so agent-plane tools registered by the preset (write/edit/bash) answer false and would be silently dropped, leaving read-only children un-guarded. Filter only genuinely optional MCP names.\\n\\nGeneral lesson: when a subagent cites a config file/package as evidence about runtime behavior, verify against a live runtime signal before propagating the claim into code.\", \"description\": \"Lesson: a patch row or installed package is not proof of live tool registration; the restrict() error's known-tools list is ground truth. Both str_replace_editor and apply_patch must leave READONLY_DENY.\", \"kind\": \"fact\", \"tags\": [\"mpd-roles-plugin\", \"mpd-workmate-plugin\", \"readonly\", \"toolFilter\", \"verification\", \"lesson\"], \"title\": \"Live tool registry vs patch rows: how to test toolFilter names (and both dead deny names)\"}"}}}}
