evidence/agent-teams/scheduler-wakeup-fix/2026-09-10T10-16-23Z/captain-session-f333e946.jsonl:3649:{"type":"assistant/chunk","seq":91666,"time":1789029042846,"data":{"turn":4,"step":3,"chunk":{"type":"block-end","index":1,"block":{"type":"tool-call","id":"call_00_95aiUdyw41HqUk1jjuHQ4402","name":"agent_teams_send_message","arguments":"{\"content\": \"Captain → Researcher. You now own t2 (project traversal dossier), reassigned from Explorer whose attempt died with zero output and left the task orphaned. This is the lane you volunteered for. Claim it and deliver in ONE turn.\\n\\nBOUNDED DELIVERABLE (the previous attempt almost certainly over-scoped itself and produced nothing — a labelled partial is strictly better than a silent death):\\n- Target roughly 150-200 lines of dense structured text in your task output. No exhaustive file dumps, no pasted source, no per-package essays.\\n- If you cannot finish everything, STOP and deliver what you have with an explicit line \\\"PARTIAL — not covered: <sections>\\\". Do not go dark, and do not end a turn with the task still open and no output.\\n\\nCONTENT PRIORITY — breadth and coupling, not the workmate internals:\\n1. Whole-repo map: every package under packages/ with what it ACTUALLY does (from its src/index.ts + README, not its name), plus presets/, skills/, scripts/, tests/, evidence/, and the .mpd state roots. One line each.\\n2. Where the workmate system sits: the package, its library root, its state files and caps, its tools, its routes, its GUI tab — and then every OTHER surface that references workmate (bundle patch rows, presets, the agent-teams member binding, QA scripts that assert its route literals, every doc that mentions it). Cite file:line.\\n3. Coupling + stale-surface map: where a workmate NAME is load-bearing (directory key, index.json key, team-member binding by name equality, note self-reference), which cross-plugin assumptions must stay byte-identical (sanitizeName vs members.js#workmateKey), and exactly which surfaces go stale if a workmate is renamed or deleted.\\n4. Execution + gates: how the bundle installs, how QA isolates DSH_HOME/HOME, what each AGENTS.md §4 gate really runs, and the evidence-on-disk convention.\\n5. Contradictions: anything where the docs and the real code disagree — report it explicitly.\\n\\nDO NOT re-derive the workmate internals in depth: t1's contract already pins sanitizeName, the wmDir(\\\"\\\") hazard, the index.json writer-with-no-reader, the tool/route surface and the in-use gate mechanism. Reference it; do not duplicate it. Your value here is the whole-project picture the user explicitly asked for (\\\"遍历工程，了解工程详细信息\\\").\\n\\nUSEFUL CONTEXT, already verified by me so you need not re-check:\\n- HEAD is f697088 and the tree is DIRTY BY DESIGN: 33 uncommitted entries from a previous session's sidebar-migration work (AGENTS.md, READMEs, docs/*, VENDOR_LOCK.json, packages/mpd-agent-teams-plugin/lib/client.js, packages/mpd-bundle-plugin/{client.js,src/web-client.js,test/*}, scripts/*, skills/dsh-qa/*, untracked evidence/ + two new test files). Do not report those as this team's changes.\\n- The real workmate library currently holds exactly one instance, \\\"oracle-1\\\" (~/.mpd/workmate).\\n- .mpd/team/ holds six stale non-archived team records plus an archive/ dir — relevant to section 3.\\n\\nYou are a read-only member: your dossier is the task output text; the Lead persists it to evidence/ during integration.\", \"to\": \"Researcher\"}"}}}}
