evidence/agent-teams/scheduler-wakeup-fix/2026-09-10T10-16-23Z/captain-session-f333e946.jsonl:3771:{"type":"assistant/message","seq":94517,"time":1789029062846,"data":{"turn":4,"step":5,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"reasoning","text":"State now:\n- t2: pending, attempt 2, → Researcher, guidance message in its inbox. Good.\n- t15/t17: pending with attempt 1, members idle/ready. Hmm — \"attempt 1\" while pending and idle. Is this the same orphaning pattern? For t2, attempt 1 was in_progress while idle. Here t15/t17 are *pending* with attempt 1.\n\nWhat does \"pending attempt 1\" mean? Probably: the member claimed it, the attempt id was issued... but the status stayed pending? Or the scheduler issued an attempt and the member hasn't started? Since the members are idle/ready (not \"working/running\"), no one is actively working.\n\nConcerning: if the attempts are parked (member turned, didn't claim properly), t15/t17 may be stalled just like t2 — waiting for someone to re-dispatch. The members' inboxes have my messages (which should start turns for them): Deep Worker and Senior Engineer each have 1 unread message. A send_message to an idle member \"starts a turn\" — so they should wake and process it (which also lets them claim t15/t17).\n\nSo the mailbox messages may have already triggered them to run; they show idle now (perhaps they ran and finished? but the tasks are still pending attempt 1...).\n\nHmm. Given the pattern I just saw with t2 (attempt held, member idle, no output → orphaned), I suspect t15/t17 are in the same orphaned state: the attempt exists but no one is working and nothing will advance them.\n\nThe status detail: for t2 the task was \"in_progress attempt 1\" (member claimed properly). For t15/t17: \"pending attempt 1\" — maybe the scheduler allocated an attempt but the member never claimed it (their turns ended early due to my message arriving?).\n\nThe user asked me to \"调度一下\" (dispatch) — primarily t2, but the spirit is: make the team move. Let me check the tasks' actual state more concretely. I can't read state files (forbidden). But the captain has `agent_teams_reassign_task` to retry/revive. The tool says: \"Atomically retry, reassign, or let the captain take over one ready unfinished/failed task... Use assignee=<member> to give it to an active member.\"\n\nIf t15/t17 are stuck with stale attempts, reassigning to the same member with a reason (\"retry: attempt 1 held but member idle with no progress\") is the sanctioned revival, and it revokes the old attempt so the new one is clean.\n\nBut careful: maybe they're NOT stuck; maybe the members are mid-run and the status snapshot is stale (members show idle/ready though). Earlier, when Planner was working, the status showed \"working/running\". Now all show idle/ready → nobody is working.\n\nSo yes: 3 tasks (t2, t15, t17) all have open attempts with idle members and no output → all orphaned. t16 has attempt 0 (never started).\n\nHmm, why did t15/t17 get attempt 1 but no work? Possibly the members attempted to claim, got the attempt, then their turn was interrupted/ended (maybe my messages arrived and steered them... messages are delivered at the nearest step boundary; that shouldn't kill a turn).\n\nWhatever the cause, the fix is the same: re-dispatch each with reassign_task (same member is fine; \"retry with the same member\") — and importantly, a fresh attempt + the member will wake and run.\n\nBut hold on: is reassigning the right revival for a *pending* task with attempt 1? The tool says it's for \"one ready unfinished/failed task\". t15/t17 are ready (deps satisfied: t1 completed). So yes, eligible.\n\nHowever — maybe simply having messages in their inboxes will wake them. But their turns may already have consumed those messages (the inbox shows the message as \"latest\"), meaning they've been delivered. Since members are idle and the attempt is open, action is needed.\n\nLet me reassign t15 → Senior Engineer (retry) and t17 → Deep Worker (retry) with reasons. Two calls. Then also t16 → Junior Engineer? t16 has attempt 0 and is ready (deps t1 done). Nobody claimed it. Junior Engineer is idle and has my message in its inbox. Hmm — why hasn't it started? Maybe the scheduler only releases one task at a time per member... or the loop isn't scheduling reliably.\n\nGiven the user's ask (\"调度一下\"), I should re-dispatch the whole ready frontier: t2 (done), t15, t16, t17. Three are ready-and-not-progressing: t15, t16, t17.\n\nFor t16 with attempt 0 and pending status: nothing is stuck; it's just unclaimed. Reassign would give it to a member — reassign_task with assignee=Junior Engineer would create attempt 1. That's the same as \"retry\" and would likely wake it. Hmm, is reassign appropriate for an unclaimed task? \"Atomically retry, reassign, or let the captain take over one ready unfinished/failed task.\" Yes, it's for ready unfinished tasks.\n\nBut careful: reassigning a task whose assignee is already correct just to \"kick\" it might be a misuse. The cleaner kick for an idle member is a send_message (which starts a turn). The members already HAVE unread... hmm, do they? The inbox shows \"Junior Engineer (1): latest — Captain → Junior Engineer...\" — meaning it's in the mailbox; \"delivered via mailbox\" earlier. Whether it was consumed (turn started) is unclear; the member is idle now, suggesting it processed it and went idle.\n\nPractical approach for maximum effect with minimal abuse:\n1. t15, t17: reassign (retry) to the same members — revokes the stale attempts and gives fresh ones. Reason: attempt held with no progress; member idle.\n2. t16: send a short guidance message to Junior Engineer to claim and run it now (send_message to an idle member starts a turn — that's the documented \"kick\").\n\nHmm, but if the members are idle because the loop won't schedule without an explicit kick, then messages are the general mechanism. And for t15/t17, reassign + (their existing message) should suffice — reassign presumably notifies the new assignee... Actually, does reassign wake the member? \"Reassignment revokes the old attempt and waits for that member to quiesce, preventing late results from overwriting the new attempt.\" It doesn't explicitly say it starts a turn. So I may ALSO need to message them.\n\nLet me be pragmatic and decisive (the user wants the team moving):\n- reassign t15 → Senior Engineer (reason: stale attempt, no progress)\n- reassign t17 → Deep Worker (same)\n- reassign t16 → Junior Engineer? Hmm. For t16 I'd rather send a message to wake it. But its inbox already has my baseline message... and it went idle. So the loop may simply not re-wake members automatically. Therefore an explicit send_message per member is the kick.\n\nRisk of double-kicking: reassign + message. Overlapping? The message starts a turn; the task is fresh; the member claims it. Fine.\n\nSimplification: for all three, do reassign (fresh attempt, same owner) — because their attempts/tasks are in non-progress states — and then send ONE short message each: \"fresh attempt issued; claim and run it now; report terminal status\". Hmm, that's 3 reassigns + 3 messages = 6 calls. A lot but justified: the user explicitly asked me to get it moving.\n\nHmm, wait. Let me reconsider whether t15/t17 really need reassign. Their attempts exist (attempt 1) but status pending — maybe the *scheduler* holds the attempt and will dispatch it when the member is free. But the members ARE free (idle) and nothing is running. So no.\n\nAlternatively: maybe the members are \"idle/ready\" because they were never spawned (ready = exists only in storage, per list_agents semantics: \"ready means it exists only in storage — resumable, not terminal\"). In the agent_teams status, members showed \"idle/unspawned\" initially, then \"idle/ready\" after spawn. Hmm: \"idle/ready · deepseek-official/...\" — the taxonomy earlier was \"idle/unspawned\" vs \"working/running\" vs \"idle/ready\". So \"idle/ready\" = spawned and idle. OK.\n\nSo these members are alive but not working, with open attempts. Kick needed.\n\nDecision: do it in two batches:\nBatch 1 (3 reassigns): t15→Senior Engineer, t16→Junior Engineer, t17→Deep Worker.\nBatch 2 (3 messages): short kick messages.\n\nHmm, tokens. Can I combine? A message is needed to wake them; the reassign may itself notify. Let me do Batch 1 and then check status: if the members show working/running, no messages needed. That saves tokens and avoids double-waking.\n\nLet me do batch 1 with the three reassigns in one block.\n\nWait — one concern about reassigning t16: it has attempt 0 (never claimed). Reassign might be rejected (\"no active attempt\")? Unknown. Let me just try; if it errors, I'll message instead.\n\nAlso: is it wise to retry with the same member when the member already stalled once? The stall may have been caused by my messages interrupting them mid-turn (the messages arrived while they were working — \"the plugin also schedules live delivery (member recipients get the message as their next turn)\"). Hmm! That's plausible: my guidance messages may have caused the members to take a new turn (processing the mail) which *interrupted/parked* their in-flight task attempt. That would explain the pattern: I sent messages to Junior Engineer/Reviewer/Lead → they woke; for Senior Engineer and Deep Worker I sent corrections → they woke to process mail and their open attempts went stale/parked.\n\nHmm, if so, the fix is fine: reassign + let them run.\n\nLet me proceed."},{"type":"text","text":"`t2` is re-dispatched (→ Researcher, attempt 2). But the same orphan pattern is now visible on the ready frontier: `t15`/`t17` hold open attempts with **idle** members and no output, and `t16` was never claimed. Reviving all three so the frontier actually runs:"},{"type":"tool-call","id":"call_00_8E0hnW8GTok59NwmyMFo2035","name":"agent_teams_reassign_task","arguments":"{\"assignee\": \"Senior Engineer\", \"reason\": \"Orphaned attempt: t15 is ready (t1 passed) but shows attempt 1 held while Senior Engineer sits idle with no progress and no task output — the attempt is parked and the scheduler will not re-run it. Revoking attempt 1 and issuing a fresh one so the member can claim and execute. The captain's live-verified correction to the t1 contract (READONLY_DENY: drop BOTH str_replace_editor and apply_patch, keep write/edit/mpd_hashline_edit) is already in its mailbox and still applies.\", \"task_id\": \"t15\"}"},{"type":"tool-call","id":"call_01_SQPAuhkopF5Yaq9FMZLp2588","name":"agent_teams_reassign_task","arguments":"{\"assignee\": \"Deep Worker\", \"reason\": \"Orphaned attempt: t17 is ready (t1 passed) but shows attempt 1 held while Deep Worker sits idle with no progress and no task output — the attempt is parked and will not be re-run. Revoking attempt 1 and issuing a fresh one. The captain's live-verified correction (both deny names are unregistered in this profile; the live-valid subset is write/edit/mpd_hashline_edit; do not hasTool-filter write/edit/bash) is already in its mailbox and still applies.\", \"task_id\": \"t17\"}"}],"source":{"kind":"model","provider":"deepseek-official","model":"deepseek-v4-flash"},"id":"78474f52-2033-478d-a9a4-1492f01f556b"},"usage":{"inputTokens":1451,"outputTokens":2636,"totalTokens":195575,"cacheReadTokens":191488,"reasoningTokens":2201}},"sourceEventSeqs":[[91956,94516]],"surfaceOp":"append"}
