evidence/agent-teams/scheduler-wakeup-fix/2026-09-10T10-16-23Z/captain-session-f333e946.jsonl:3856:{"type":"assistant/chunk","seq":95954,"time":1789029079855,"data":{"turn":4,"step":8,"chunk":{"type":"block-end","index":0,"block":{"type":"reasoning","text":"Reassignment alone didn't wake anybody: all still idle/ready, tasks still pending. So the scheduler is not dispatching. The documented mechanism to start a turn for an idle member is `agent_teams_send_message` (\"when the captain agent is online the plugin also schedules live delivery (member recipients get the message as their next turn)\").\n\nAnd note: the inboxes show exactly 1 message each (my earlier guidance) — which suggests those messages were consumed... or still sitting there. If they were consumed but the member is idle, then delivery didn't start a working turn, or the member's turn ended after processing the mail.\n\nHmm, so why did t1/t2 run initially but now nothing runs? Pattern: the team loop apparently woke members once at start (t1 claimed+completed by Planner; t2 claimed by Explorer who then died). Since then, nothing has been scheduled. The attempts for t15/t17 came from... hmm.\n\nKey insight: maybe the members' turns are driven by mailbox messages only in this deployment, and the scheduler needs... Let me test the hypothesis directly: send ONE short message to Junior Engineer telling it to claim t16 and run it. Then check status: if Junior Engineer shows working/running and t16 goes in_progress with attempt, then messages are the working kick mechanism, and I should do the same for the others.\n\nThat's a cheap, decisive experiment (1 message + 1 status). Let me do it.\n\nActually, better: send messages to all three (t15/t16/t17 owners) at once and check? If the hypothesis is wrong, I've woken 3 members to no effect (some token cost). If right, I've unstuck the frontier in one shot. The efficient path: message one (Junior Engineer), verify, then message the rest. That's 2 rounds but safer.\n\nGiven the user is waiting and asked me to dispatch, and token cost of a wake is small relative to a stuck team, let me do the single-message experiment first — it's the scientific approach and cheap.\n\nHmm, but if the experiment works, I then need another round for the other two. Fine.\n\nLet me message Junior Engineer: \"Claim t16 now and execute it\" — concise, action-forcing.\n\nHmm, one important consideration: my earlier messages to Deep Worker/Senior Engineer are still unread in their inboxes (count 1 each). If delivery didn't start a turn, then those messages are pending and would be delivered when the member next turns. So the same \"kick\" message would be the trigger.\n\nWait, actually — maybe the issue is different: perhaps members CAN'T run because the team loop is waiting on something (e.g. the \"deliverable\" loop phase, or the scheduler is idle because... hmm).\n\nLet me just test with Junior Engineer."}}}}
