nGiven the user is waiting and asked me to dispatch, and token cost of a wake is small relative to a stuck team, let me do the single-message experiment first — it's the scientific approach and cheap.\n\nHmm, but if the experiment works, I then need another round for the other two. Fine.\n\nLet me message Junior Engineer: \"Claim t16 now and execute it\" — concise, action-forcing.\n\nHmm, one important consideration: my earlier messages to Deep Worker/Senior Engineer are still unread in their inboxes (count 1 each). If delivery didn't start a turn, then those messages are pending and would be delivered when the member next turns. So the same \"kick\" message would be the trigger.\n\nWait, actually — maybe the issue is different: perhaps members CAN'T run because the team loop is waiting on something (e.g. the \"deliverable\" loop phase, or the scheduler is idle because... hmm).\n\nLet me just test with Junior Engineer."},{"type":"text","text":"Reassignment revoked the stale attempts but did **not** wake anyone — every member is still `idle/ready` and the frontier has not moved. Testing whether an explicit mailbox message is the working dispatch mechanism:"},{"type":"tool-call","id":"call_00_Aps7j22TQLULXQY4C6zw0792","name":"agent_teams_send_message","arguments":"{\"content\": \"Captain → Junior Engineer. ACTION NOW: claim t16 and execute it end-to-end in this turn.\\n\\nt16 (\\\"Workmates sidebar tab: rename + delete controls (zh/en) and rebuilt client\\\") is READY — its dependency t1 (requirements contract, verdict=pass) is completed, and I have issued you a fresh attempt. Nothing else blocks you.\\n\\nSteps:\\n1. Read t1's task output (the binding wire contract) and build against it verbatim: use exactly the routes/verbs/payloads it pins (`POST /plugins/mpd-workmate/rename` and `POST /plugins/mpd-workmate/delete` per the contract's table). Do not invent route shapes; if the contract is silent on something you need, state that in your task output.\\n2. Edit packages/mpd-bundle-plugin/src/web-client.js (WorkmateLibraryView + WORKMATE_LOCALE_NAMESPACE zh/en, zh is the key-set source of truth).\\n3. Run `node scripts/build-mpd-client.mjs` and confirm the rebuilt packages/mpd-bundle-plugin/client.js contains the new UI markers.\\n4. Run `bun test packages/mpd-bundle-plugin/test` and `bun run typecheck`.\\n5. Complete the task with update_task (task t16, your attempt_id, status completed) including changedPaths, commandsRun with exit codes, and acceptanceResults. If you must fail it, fail it with the concrete blocker instead of going idle silently.\\n\\nBaseline reminder (already sent, still binding): the 33 uncommitted entries in the tree are the BASELINE, not yours — never commit/stash/revert them, and report only your own changed paths. client.js is not stale (rebuilt 15:36 vs source 15:27), but you still must rebuild after your edit.\\n\\nDo not end this turn with t16 unclaimed or with an open attempt and no output — that is exactly how the previous task on this team (t2) was lost.\", \"to\": \"Junior Engineer\"}"}],"source":{"kind":"model","provider":"deepseek-official","model":"deepseek-v4-flash"},"id":"a4f34dc2-fb91-401e-bd99-84632cb1a869"},"usage":{"inputTokens":1478,"outputTokens":1108,"totalTokens":198554,"cacheReadTokens":195968,"reasoningTokens":593}},"sourceEventSeqs":[[94882,95958]],"surfaceOp":"append"}
