Run with exit codes, acceptanceResults).\\n\\nDo not end this turn with t15 unclaimed, or with an open attempt and no output — that is how t2 was lost earlier on this team.\", \"to\": \"Senior Engineer\"}"},{"type":"tool-call","id":"call_01_PQGxt4kPLGUkoW4aB8EL5551","name":"agent_teams_send_message","arguments":"{\"content\": \"Captain → Deep Worker. ACTION NOW: claim t17 and execute it end-to-end in this turn. Its dependency t1 is completed and I have issued you a fresh attempt — nothing blocks you.\\n\\nApply my correction (already in your mailbox) over the t1 contract's finding #1: BOTH str_replace_editor and apply_patch are unregistered in this profile. Evidence is the live restrict() error itself, which enumerates the known global tools (write, edit, mpd_hashline_edit are present; both deny-list names are reported unknown). So the correct fix is READONLY_DENY = write, edit, mpd_hashline_edit, and keeping str_replace_editor would leave read-only spawn broken with the identical error. Do not hasTool-filter write/edit/bash.\\n\\nDeliver: the roles-plugin fix, a regression that fails pre-fix and passes after, a dsh-qa case (script + --self-test + SKILL.md row) booting the real dsh in an isolated DSH_HOME/HOME, the before/after evidence under evidence/workmate/roles-readonly/<timestamp>/ (before = the exact restrict error), and proof that a real read-only spawn now STARTS while the read-only authority is not widened. Then complete the task with update_task (your attempt_id, status completed, changedPaths, commandsRun with exit codes, acceptanceResults).\\n\\nDo not end this turn with t17 unclaimed, or with an open attempt and no output — that is how t2 was lost earlier on this team.\", \"to\": \"Deep Worker\"}"}],"source":{"kind":"model","provider":"deepseek-official","model":"deepseek-v4-flash"},"id":"d47b0220-e573-4ceb-aa49-c74a486572dd"},"usage":{"inputTokens":1474,"outputTokens":2194,"totalTokens":202196,"cacheReadTokens":198528,"reasoningTokens":1455}},"sourceE