 Create a fresh team with profile=mpd, approval=\"required\" (per protocol; the user must approve... hmm, the user said \"重新拉一下队伍\" — they want it running. But my instructions: create with approval=\"required\" and let the user approve; the Web panel is where they approve. Since the user just asked me to re-pull the team, and they know the approve flow (they approved the last one), creating with approval=\"required\" is right. Hmm — but if the scheduler is what's stuck, will a new team's scheduler work? The user says the stuck thing is the scheduler; a new team presumably gets a fresh scheduler. Whether the *user's approval* re-triggers... They approved the previous plan via the panel, and t1 ran. So approval → scheduler starts. Right: the previous plan WAS approved (loop went running). So a fresh team + user approval should spin up a fresh scheduler.\n\n   Wait — should I create with approval=\"automatic\" to avoid depending on the panel? The protocol: \"approval='automatic' preserves the legacy immediate-execution path\" and \"Call agent_teams_create with approval='required'... Use approval='automatic' only when the user explicitly asks to skip review and run immediately.\" The user asked to re-pull the team (implicitly to get work moving), not explicitly to skip review. Hmm. Given they're frustrated with the stall and the plan is already agreed (requirements + contract), approval=\"required\" costs one more click. But \"required\" is the binding default. The user said \"你这边重新拉一下队伍吧，不然估计就都一直这么卡着了\" — they want it unstuck. I'll use approval=\"required\" (protocol default) — one click for them, and the plan panel is where they can also see the re-staged DAG. Hmm, but if the same scheduler bug persists... no, new team = new scheduler.\n   \n   Hmm, let me reconsider: is it *safer* for the user if I use automatic? The user explicitly wants it run. The protocol allows automatic only on explicit request. They didn't explicitly say \"skip review\". I'll go with required,