e workmate-side READONLY_DENY contains exactly the live-registered subset (write, edit, mpd_hashline_edit) — both str_replace_editor and apply_patch removed per contract section G — pinned by a test, with the live spawn proof recorded.\", \"GATES + EVIDENCE: bun test packages/mpd-workmate-plugin/test/workmate.test.ts, bun run typecheck and the dist rebuild pass; evidence written under evidence/workmate/rename-delete-core/<timestamp>/ with real command output and the git baseline captured before/after.\", \"NO SILENT DEATH: the task is completed with structured results (changedPaths, commandsRun, acceptanceResults) or failed with a concrete blocker — never left claimed with no output.\"], \"dependencies\": [\"t1\"], \"description\": \"Read first, in this order: (1) .mpd/plans/workmate-rename-delete-contract.md — the BINDING interface document (sections A-I; section G already contains the captain's live-corrected deny list, which overrides the earlier team's claim), (2) the t1 contract-validation output, which may carry corrections.\\n\\nWork is centred on packages/mpd-workmate-plugin/src/index.ts: the 5 existing tools, the mpdWorkmate service, the index.json writer (no reader today), and the 4 lazily registered web routes. The dangerous details: sanitizeName() is the single key algorithm and wmDir(\\\"\\\") resolves to the LIBRARY ROOT; the rename must move the evolved identity rather than re-instantiate it; delete must be all-or-nothing; and a mutation racing an in-flight spawn/reflect must be closed by the in-use gate, not by hope.\\n\\nHouse rules: every harness seam goes through the mpd-dsh-adapter — never ctx.tools/ctx.subagents directly; state stays under ~/.mpd/workmate (the one sanctioned HOME exception); English-only comments/docstrings; minimal diff, no speculative refactors. Rebuild dist when done: `cd packages/mpd-workmate-plugin && bun build src/index.ts --target node --format esm --outfile dist/index.js` (a checkout install reads dist directly).\\n\\nBASELINE: the tree is dirty BY DESIGN — HEAD f697088 plus 33 uncommitted entries from a previous session. Never commit/stash/revert them, record HEAD + `git status --porcelain` before and after, and report only YOUR delta.\\n\\nDo not end the turn with this task claimed and no output: complete it with structured results, or fail it with a concrete blocker.\", \"inScope\": [\"packages/mpd-workmate-plugin/\", \"evidence/workmate/rename-delete-core/\"], \"kind\": \"implementation\", \"nonGoals\": [\"The roles-plugin deny list (the separate fix task owns it)\", \"The Workmates GUI and client.js (the GUI task owns them)\", \"Docs, AGENTS.md and QA scripts (the docs task owns them)\", \"Changing the library root, the size caps, or the matching algorithm\"], \"objective\": \"Implement rename and delete for the workmate library in packages/mpd-workmate-plugin exactly as the preserved contract pins them: the two new agent tools, their mpdWorkmate service methods, the two new POST routes, the in-use refusal gate, archive-first delete, the complete rename cascade, root-safety and name-safety guards, the workmate-side read-only deny correction, plus tests, a rebuilt dist and evidence on disk.\", \"outOfScope\": [\"packages/mpd-roles-plugin/\", \"packages/mpd-bundle-plugin/\", \"packages/mpd-agent-teams-plugin/\", \"AGENTS.md\", \"docs/\", \"skills/\"], \"round\": 1, \"subject\": \"Implement workmate rename + delete core: tools, service, routes, safety, tests\", \"verify\": [\"bun test packages/mpd-workmate-plugin/test/workmate.test.ts\", \"bun run typecheck\", \"cd packages/mpd-workmate-plugin && bun build src/index.ts --target node --format esm --outfile dist/index.js\"]}"}}}}
