evidence/agent-teams/scheduler-wakeup-fix/2026-09-10T10-16-23Z/captain-session-f333e946.jsonl:4492:{"type":"assistant/chunk","seq":112544,"time":1789029533646,"data":{"turn":5,"step":6,"chunk":{"type":"block-end","index":1,"block":{"type":"tool-call","id":"call_00_ZtgNohebtt3ynQBJ84AO9849","name":"agent_teams_create_task","arguments":"{\"acceptance\": [\"READONLY_DENY in packages/mpd-roles-plugin contains exactly the live-registered subset (write, edit, mpd_hashline_edit): BOTH str_replace_editor and apply_patch are removed, per contract section G — keeping either leaves every read-only spawn failing with the identical restrict() error.\", \"The root cause is demonstrated against the REAL harness, not a config file: evidence shows the pre-fix failure (the exact 'names unknown global tools' error) and the fixed behaviour with the live registry's known-tools list.\", \"The fix is not a dsh.hasTool filter over write/edit/bash (that reads the global view only and would silently drop them, leaving read-only children un-guarded); only optional MCP names may be resolved that way.\", \"A real read-only mpd_role_spawn now STARTS a child, and that child receives UNKNOWN_TOOL if it attempts a write — the restriction still binds, with before/after evidence.\", \"A regression test can fail on the pre-fix state and passes after; a stub-only assertion is not acceptable.\", \"A dsh-qa case exists (script + --self-test + SKILL.md case-table row) booting the real dsh in an ISOLATED DSH_HOME and HOME; the real ~/.dsh, the real HOME and real credentials are never touched.\", \"bun run test:qa and bun run typecheck pass, evidence is written under evidence/workmate/roles-readonly/<timestamp>/, and the task is completed with structured results or failed with a concrete blocker — never left claimed with no output.\"], \"dependencies\": [\"t1\"], \"description\": \"Read .mpd/plans/workmate-rename-delete-contract.md section G first — it is the corrected, live-measured version of this defect and it overrides any earlier claim that str_replace_editor is valid.\\n\\nReproduction (measured twice by the captain with a read-only mpd_role_spawn):\\n  Error: tools.restrict() names unknown global tools \\\"str_replace_editor\\\", \\\"apply_patch\\\";\\n  known global tools: … bash … edit … mpd_hashline_edit … read … write\\nThe harness validates the whole list, reports BOTH names as unknown, and runs this check in applyChildComposition before the child starts — so today every read-only roster role and every read-only workmate fails to spawn. The live registry enumeration in that message IS the ground truth for this profile: it contains write/edit/mpd_hashline_edit and neither dead name. A `@deepseek-ai/dsh-tool-str-replace-editor` package and a dsh-base patch row exist in the install but are not composed into this profile, so they are not evidence of registration.\\n\\nYour surface: packages/mpd-roles-plugin/src/index.ts (READONLY_DENY ~L23-27, used ~L123 as toolFilter deny when spec.readonly). The workmate-side line (packages/mpd-workmate-plugin/src/index.ts L30) belongs to the core implementation task — do not touch it.\\n\\nThe point of the list is a security-ish property: read-only specialists must not be able to write. Do not \\\"fix\\\" this by deleting the restriction, and do not switch to a hasTool filter over write/edit/bash.\\n\\nFollow the dsh-qa discipline for the new case (skills/dsh-qa): SKILL.md case table, --self-test on every script, evidence under evidence/, isolated DSH_HOME with HOME=<sandbox>, credentials copied once into the sandbox, stdio to files rather than pipes for long-lived MCP children.\\n\\nBASELINE: the tree is dirty by design (HEAD f697088 + 33 uncommitted entries). Never commit/stash/revert them; capture HEAD + `git status --porcelain` before and after and report only your own delta.\\n\\nDo not end the turn with this task claimed and no output: complete it with structured results, or fail it with a concrete blocker.\", \"inScope\": [\"packages/mpd-roles-plugin/\", \"skills/dsh-qa/scripts/\", \"evidence/workmate/roles-readonly/\"], \"kind\": \"implementation\", \"nonGoals\": [\"The workmate-side READONLY_DENY line (the core task owns it)\", \"Changing the roster, its personas or its model routes\", \"Widening or removing the read-only restriction itself\", \"The Workmates GUI and documentation (other tasks own them)\"], \"objective\": \"Fix the live defect that makes read-only specialist spawn (and, on the workmate side, read-only workmate spawn) fail on this harness: the deny list names tools this harness does not register, and the harness rejects the entire restriction call, so no read-only spawn can be created at all. Prove the fix against the REAL dsh registry, keep read-only authority intact, and leave a regression that catches the next stale name.\", \"outOfScope\": [\"packages/mpd-workmate-plugin/\", \"packages/mpd-bundle-plugin/\", \"AGENTS.md\", \"docs/\"], \"round\": 1, \"subject\": \"Fix read-only deny lists so read-only spawn works on the real harness\", \"verify\": [\"bun test packages/mpd-roles-plugin/test\", \"bun run test:qa\", \"bun run typecheck\"]}"}}}}
