evidence/agent-teams/scheduler-wakeup-fix/2026-09-10T10-16-23Z/captain-session-f333e946.jsonl:4556:{"type":"assistant/chunk","seq":114496,"time":1789029544103,"data":{"turn":5,"step":7,"chunk":{"type":"block-end","index":0,"block":{"type":"reasoning","text":"Now wave 3: V1 verification (deps t3,t4,t5) and the 3 reviews (t6? no — next ids: t6 verification, t7 review core (reviewedTaskId t3), t8 review GUI (t4), t9 review fix (t5)).\n\nLet me create the verification task t6 and the three reviews in one block (4 calls)."}}}}
evidence/agent-teams/scheduler-wakeup-fix/2026-09-10T10-16-23Z/captain-session-f333e946.jsonl:4557:{"type":"assistant/chunk","seq":114497,"time":1789029544104,"data":{"turn":5,"step":7,"chunk":{"type":"block-end","index":1,"block":{"type":"tool-call","id":"call_00_3CCBSTfteFKhrRuRGVGR7351","name":"agent_teams_create_task","arguments":"{\"acceptance\": [\"Every gate is run on the integrated tree with real output recorded: bun test packages, bun run typecheck, bun run test:qa, node scripts/verify-vendor.mjs, and a `dsh --profile headless --dump-config` boot in an isolated DSH_HOME.\", \"A real sandbox-HOME lifecycle exercise, driven from the outside (tools/service/routes, not by reading the implementers' code), demonstrates: rename preserves persona/memory/note/uses/createdAt and frees the old key; delete archives by default and the instance is restorable from .archive/; purge removes it; list/match/service views agree with the filesystem immediately after each mutation.\", \"Negative cases demonstrably behave: invalid/empty/CJK/punctuation-only names are rejected before any filesystem call with the library root untouched; unknown names error with zero side effects; a repeated delete returns 404; a rename collision is refused; a rename or delete is refused while the workmate is in use, with the refusal naming the blocking team and member.\", \"The new routes answer per contract section D on a real boot (status code + reason value for success, invalid body, unknown name, wrong verb, collision, in-use refusal), and the read-only spawn fix is demonstrated against the real harness.\", \"Every command result is recorded in commandsRun with exit codes and evidence; results.json/output.log land under evidence/workmate/rename-delete-verify/<timestamp>/; the git baseline (HEAD + status) is captured before and after; the real HOME and real ~/.dsh are never touched and the sandbox path is asserted in the evidence.\", \"The task is completed with structured results or failed with the concrete failing command/output — never left claimed with no output, and never silently passing a criterion that was not actually exercised.\"], \"dependencies\": [\"t3\", \"t4\", \"t5\"], \"description\": \"Verify the delivered feature independently. Do not trust the implementers' summaries: reproduce from the real artifacts (source, built dist, real dsh boot, sandboxed filesystem). Any mismatch between a claim and observed behaviour is a finding you report — you do not fix code yourself.\\n\\nRead .mpd/plans/workmate-rename-delete-contract.md first; it defines the exact behaviour you are verifying (sections C, D, E, F, H are your acceptance reference).\\n\\nMethod: follow the dsh-qa discipline (skills/dsh-qa) — an isolated DSH_HOME and HOME per run, credentials copied once into the sandbox, sandbox paths asserted, evidence under evidence/<domain>/<slug>/<timestamp>/{result.json,output.log}, long-lived MCP children with stdio to files rather than pipes. The workmate library lives under $HOME, so every lifecycle exercise MUST run with HOME pointing at a sandbox and the evidence must show it.\\n\\nWhere a naive implementation is quietly wrong — check these specifically: a name that sanitizes to the empty string (wmDir(\\\"\\\") is the library root itself); a rename that loses evolved memory or bumps uses; a delete that leaves the index stale or removes only part of the instance; a mutation racing an in-flight spawn; a route that answers 200 for an unknown name; a refusal that does not name the blocking team.\\n\\nBASELINE: the tree is dirty by design (HEAD f697088 + 33 uncommitted entries from a previous session). Record HEAD + `git status --porcelain` at the start and end so the verified delta is attributable; never commit, stash or \\\"clean up\\\" pre-existing changes to make a run look tidy.\\n\\nIf something fails, fail the task with the exact command, exit code and output — the scheduler turns that into a repair loop.\", \"inScope\": [\"evidence/workmate/rename-delete-verify/\"], \"kind\": \"verification\", \"nonGoals\": [\"Fixing anything yourself\", \"Approving the implementation\", \"Editing package sources, docs or QA scripts\"], \"objective\": \"Independently verify the shipped rename/delete feature and the read-only deny fix against the REAL harness and the REAL gates: run every gate, exercise the full lifecycle and its negative cases with HOME pointed at a sandbox, boot the bundle in an isolated DSH_HOME, confirm the routes and the read-only spawn path behave as contracted, and leave reproducible evidence on disk.\", \"outOfScope\": [\"packages/\", \"AGENTS.md\", \"docs/\", \"skills/dsh-qa/scripts/\"], \"round\": 1, \"subject\": \"Independent verification: rename/delete end-to-end, negative cases, full gate sweep\", \"verify\": [\"bun test packages\", \"bun run typecheck\", \"bun run test:qa\", \"node scripts/verify-vendor.mjs\"]}"}}}}
evidence/agent-teams/scheduler-wakeup-fix/2026-09-10T10-16-23Z/captain-session-f333e946.jsonl:4558:{"type":"assistant/chunk","seq":114498,"time":1789029544104,"data":{"turn":5,"step":7,"chunk":{"type":"block-end","index":2,"block":{"type":"tool-call","id":"call_01_qdc1RUQpLr9ttr9tznA92746","name":"agent_teams_create_task","arguments":"{\"acceptance\": [\"Every contract acceptance criterion (sections C, D, F, G, H) is checked against the shipped code and on-disk evidence, each with an explicit pass/fail and a concrete citation (file/line or command output).\", \"The review actively falsifies the four invariants and reports any counterexample: name↔dir↔index bijection and root safety; rename is identity-preserving and never a re-instantiation; delete is complete and all-or-nothing; the cross-module binding outcome is deterministic with no state where directory, index.json, service view and team-member backing disagree.\", \"Race and failure analysis covers: a reflect landing after a rename (old-directory resurrection), reflect/delete ordering, partial failure between directory move and metadata write, and whether the in-use gate actually closes the in-flight window rather than shifting it.\", \"The workmate-side READONLY_DENY correction is verified against the live registry claim in contract section G, including that read-only authority was not widened.\", \"The implementation is judged against the LATEST code state, including any repair that already ran.\", \"Verdict=pass only with zero unresolved blocker/high findings; otherwise the task FAILS with structured findings (id, severity, problem, requiredFix) naming the exact file and required correction.\"], \"dependencies\": [\"t3\"], \"description\": \"Adversarially review the core implementation (t3) on the axes where a mistake is expensive and hard to see. Read .mpd/plans/workmate-rename-delete-contract.md first, then the actual code in packages/mpd-workmate-plugin/src/index.ts, the tests and the evidence — treating the implementer's summary as a claim to be checked, not as fact.\\n\\nAttack in particular:\\n- sanitizeName as the single key algorithm: can any input reach a filesystem call before validation? What happens for an empty sanitized name, a CJK name, a punctuation-only name, a case-only variant, and a name colliding after sanitization?\\n- rename identity: is the evolved instance really moved rather than recreated, with persona/memory/note content, caps, uses, lastTask and createdAt preserved, and the note self-reference plus renamedFrom consistent with the new key?\\n- delete: archive-first behaviour, hidden-from-list/match, restorability, purge + confirm semantics, index-key removal, all-or-nothing failure behaviour.\\n- the in-use gate: does it actually close the spawn/reflect race, is the .mpd/team read implemented as read-only (never writing another plugin's state), is fail-open correct here, and is the refusal actionable (blocking team id + member)?\\n- index.json: it has no reader today — judge whether the rename/delete handling leaves it consistent and whether the contract's treatment is defensible.\\n- the workmate-side READONLY_DENY correction: does it follow contract section G exactly, and does it keep read-only authority intact?\\n\\nYou are a read-only role: report findings, do not edit files. A 'pass' verdict with an unverified criterion is worse than a 'needs_revision' with a real finding. Never end the turn with the task claimed and no output.\", \"kind\": \"review\", \"nonGoals\": [\"Editing any file\", \"Reviewing the GUI task or the roles-plugin fix task\", \"Re-litigating the five agreed user decisions\"], \"objective\": \"Adversarially review the core rename/delete implementation against the contract and the four invariants: root safety and name validation, identity-preserving rename, complete all-or-nothing delete, and deterministic behaviour under races and partial failure. Judge the latest code state and cite evidence for every claim.\", \"reviewedTaskId\": \"t3\", \"round\": 1, \"subject\": \"Review: core rename/delete implementation (safety, identity, atomicity, races)\"}"}}}}
