evidence/agent-teams/scheduler-wakeup-fix/2026-09-10T10-16-23Z/captain-session-f333e946.jsonl:4564:{"type":"tool/call","seq":114504,"time":1789029544119,"data":{"turn":5,"step":7,"callId":"call_01_qdc1RUQpLr9ttr9tznA92746","name":"agent_teams_create_task","arguments":"{\"acceptance\": [\"Every contract acceptance criterion (sections C, D, F, G, H) is checked against the shipped code and on-disk evidence, each with an explicit pass/fail and a concrete citation (file/line or command output).\", \"The review actively falsifies the four invariants and reports any counterexample: name↔dir↔index bijection and root safety; rename is identity-preserving and never a re-instantiation; delete is complete and all-or-nothing; the cross-module binding outcome is deterministic with no state where directory, index.json, service view and team-member backing disagree.\", \"Race and failure analysis covers: a reflect landing after a rename (old-directory resurrection), reflect/delete ordering, partial failure between directory move and metadata write, and whether the in-use gate actually closes the in-flight window rather than shifting it.\", \"The workmate-side READONLY_DENY correction is verified against the live registry claim in contract section G, including that read-only authority was not widened.\", \"The implementation is judged against the LATEST code state, including any repair that already ran.\", \"Verdict=pass only with zero unresolved blocker/high findings; otherwise the task FAILS with structured findings (id, severity, problem, requiredFix) naming the exact file and required correction.\"], \"dependencies\": [\"t3\"], \"description\": \"Adversarially review the core implementation (t3) on the axes where a mistake is expensive and hard to see. Read .mpd/plans/workmate-rename-delete-contract.md first, then the actual code in packages/mpd-workmate-plugin/src/index.ts, the tests and the evidence — treating the implementer's summary as a claim to be checked, not as fact.\\n\\nAttack in particular:\\n- sanitizeName as the single key algorithm: can any input reach a filesystem call before validation? What happens for an empty sanitized name, a CJK name, a punctuation-only name, a case-only variant, and a name colliding after sanitization?\\n- rename identity: is the evolved instance really moved rather than recreated, with persona/memory/note content, caps, uses, lastTask and createdAt preserved, and the note self-reference plus renamedFrom consistent with the new key?\\n- delete: archive-first behaviour, hidden-from-list/match, restorability, purge + confirm semantics, index-key removal, all-or-nothing failure behaviour.\\n- the in-use gate: does it actually close the spawn/reflect race, is the .mpd/team read implemented as read-only (never writing another plugin's state), is fail-open correct here, and is the refusal actionable (blocking team id + member)?\\n- index.json: it has no reader today — judge whether the rename/delete handling leaves it consistent and whether the contract's treatment is defensible.\\n- the workmate-side READONLY_DENY correction: does it follow contract section G exactly, and does it keep read-only authority intact?\\n\\nYou are a read-only role: report findings, do not edit files. A 'pass' verdict with an unverified criterion is worse than a 'needs_revision' with a real finding. Never end the turn with the task claimed and no output.\", \"kind\": \"review\", \"nonGoals\": [\"Editing any file\", \"Reviewing the GUI task or the roles-plugin fix task\", \"Re-litigating the five agreed user decisions\"], \"objective\": \"Adversarially review the core rename/delete implementation against the contract and the four invariants: root safety and name validation, identity-preserving rename, complete all-or-nothing delete, and deterministic behaviour under races and partial failure. Judge the latest code state and cite evidence for every claim.\", \"reviewedTaskId\": \"t3\", \"round\": 1, \"subject\": \"Review: core rename/delete implementation (safety, identity, atomicity, races)\"}"}}
