-client.js (WorkmateLibraryView, the request() helper, WORKMATE_LOCALE_NAMESPACE zh+en, registerWorkmateSidebarTab) and the rebuilt packages/mpd-bundle-plugin/client.js. Cross-check packages/mpd-bundle-plugin/test/sidebar-tab.test.mjs, test/client-harness.mjs and test/team-page.test.mjs.\\n\\nAttack in particular:\\n- does the flow actually let a human rename a workmate and delete one, with archive-first semantics communicated rather than hidden behind a destructive-looking button?\\n- what happens to the view when a mutation succeeds, when it is refused because the workmate is in use, when the host returns an error, and when the selected workmate disappears underneath the detail view?\\n- are the zh and en key sets genuinely identical, and is the Chinese wording accurate and natural?\\n- is the shipped bundle actually rebuilt (the build script fails the build if the removed floater/toggle come back), and does it still respect the seam policy where a declared-but-unregistered service takes the whole page down?\\n\\nNote on evidence limits: the sandbox has NO browser driver (no chromium binary, no playwright package) — the captain verified this. So do NOT require rendered screenshots; judge from source, tests, the built artifact and the route contract, and say so explicitly in your verdict rather than implying visual verification happened.\\n\\nYou are a read-only role: report findings, do not edit files. Never end the turn with the task claimed and no output.\", \"kind\": \"review\", \"nonGoals\": [\"Editing any file\", \"Requiring screenshot evidence that this sandbox cannot produce\", \"Reviewing the core library task or the roles-plugin fix task\"], \"objective\": \"Review the Workmates tab rename/delete UI as a UI/UX and contract-conformance critic: does it let a human rename and safely delete a workmate, does it match the wire contract exactly including per-reason error handling, are all zh/en strings complete and natural, and are the destructive path, stale-selection handling and sidebar-only constraints sound in the shipped client bundle?\", \"reviewedTaskId\": \"t4\", \"round\": 1, \"subject\": \"Review: Workmates tab rename/delete UI, zh/en strings, rebuilt client\"}"}}
evidence/agent-teams/scheduler-wakeup-fix/2026-09-10T10-16-23Z/captain-session-f333e946.jsonl:4628:{"type":"tool/call","seq":116293,"time":1789029554750,"data":{"turn":5,"step":8,"callId":"call_01_nciz1tydbvd2VUjbDE3h9534","name":"agent_teams_create_task","arguments":"{\"acceptance\": [\"The root cause is confirmed against the harness's real tool registry and the fix is shown to remove it, with before/after evidence cited (the pre-fix error text and the post-fix live spawn).\", \"The claim from the earlier team (that str_replace_editor is valid) is explicitly resolved: the review states which list ships and cites live or source-anchored evidence for it.\", \"The proof is evaluated for real-harness fidelity: the regression or QA case must have been able to fail on the pre-fix state and must pass after it; an assertion that only exercises a stub or a constructed array is a finding.\", \"Read-only authority is verified not to have widened — after the fix a read-only role still cannot write files (no write/edit/apply_patch-class tool becomes available), and the mechanism cannot silently degrade to 'no restriction' on a future harness.\", \"The QA case follows repo discipline: isolated DSH_HOME and HOME, sandbox path asserted, no real credentials or real home touched, stdio handled safely, self-test present and passing, matching SKILL.md case-table row. At least one high finding if the case does not actually boot the real dsh.\", \"Verdict=pass only with zero unresolved blocker/high findings; otherwise the task FAILS with structured findings (id, severity, problem, requiredFix) naming the exact file and required correction.\", \"The task is completed with the verdict or failed with findings — never left claimed with no output.\"], \"dependencies\": [\"t5\"], \"description\": \"Review the read-only deny-list fix (t5), which unblocked a defect that made every read-only spawn fail on this harness. You did not implement it, so this is an independent review. Read contract section G first — it carries the captain's live-measured correction (BOTH str_replace_editor and apply_patch are unregistered in this profile; the live-valid subset is write/edit/mpd_hashline_edit).\\n\\nAttack in particular:\\n- was the diagnosis correct and complete? Confirm the shipped list against the live registry, and check whether the same class of staleness exists anywhere else in the tree (other toolFilter/deny lists), reporting it as a finding rather than fixing it.\\n- is the mechanism robust, or a literal patch that will rot when the harness renames a tool? Judge whether the chosen approach can silently degrade to \\\"no restriction\\\" — that would be a blocker, not a pass.\\n- does the verification actually exercise the real dsh (isolated home, real boot, real spawn path) rather than a stub adapter? Cross-check the evidence under evidence/workmate/roles-readonly/.\\n- did the read-only guarantee survive? The purpose of the list is that read-only specialists must not write; a fix that weakens or voids the restriction is a blocker.\\n- does the new QA case follow skills/dsh-qa discipline (SKILL.md case table, --self-test, evidence path, isolated homes, credentials handling)?\\n\\nYou are a worker role, so you may inspect anything and run commands, but do not change t5's files: report findings instead. Never end the turn with the task claimed and no output.\", \"kind\": \"review\", \"nonGoals\": [\"Editing the files under review\", \"Reviewing the core task or the GUI task\", \"Changing the roster or the read-only policy itself\"], \"objective\": \"Review the read-only deny-list defect fix on diagnosis correctness and proof strength: does the deny list now name only tools this harness registers, is the mechanism robust rather than a literal patch, does the regression genuinely exercise the real harness and fail pre-fix, and did the fix preserve read-only authority?\", \"reviewedTaskId\": \"t5\", \"round\": 1, \"subject\": \"Review: read-only deny-list fix and its real-harness proof\"}"}}
