cker — never left claimed with no output.\"], \"dependencies\": [\"t1\", \"t2\", \"t6\", \"t7\", \"t8\", \"t9\", \"t10\"], \"description\": \"Integrate the verified, reviewed work into one coherent change on disk and report it honestly. You own the last mile: nothing may be described as done that the evidence does not support.\\n\\nConcretely:\\n1. Persist the deliverables that exist as task text — the contract file path plus the t1 validation result and the t2 dossier — into evidence/workmate/rename-delete-integration/<timestamp>/, together with a summary of t6's verification results.\\n2. Re-run the gate sweep on the FINAL integrated tree (after t10's doc/QA-script sync) and record the real output; an earlier green run on a pre-sync tree does not count.\\n3. Check code↔docs consistency in both directions and fix drift only inside your inScope (documentation paths); report code-side drift as an open finding instead of editing implementation files.\\n4. Produce the delivery report as your task output: changed files, decisions implemented, explicit non-goals and non-rewrites, evidence paths, residual risk, and the open items for the user.\\n5. Confirm the release path is coherent: rebuilt dists and rebuilt web client correspond to the sources.\\n\\nBASELINE: the tree was already dirty before this team started (HEAD f697088 + 33 uncommitted entries from a previous session, several inside the packages this team touched). State that baseline explicitly and separate THIS team's change set from the pre-existing work; never commit, stash or revert anyone else's changes.\\n\\nAlso record explicitly for the user: no visual/browser verification exists for the GUI (the sandbox has no browser driver — the captain verified there is no chromium binary and no playwright package), so the UI is verified at source/test/route level only. Do not let the report imply otherwise.\\n\\nIf a required review or verification is still failing, do not paper over it: fail the task with the concrete blocker.\", \"inScope\": [\"evidence/workmate/rename-delete-integration/\", \"AGENTS.md\", \"docs/\", \"README.md\", \"README.zh-CN.md\", \"packages/mpd-workmate-plugin/README.md\", \"packages/mpd-workmate-plugin/README.zh-CN.md\"], \"kind\": \"integration\", \"nonGoals\": [\"Changing implementation code to make a gate pass\", \"Restarting or redoing a review that already returned pass\", \"Re-litigating the five agreed user decisions\"], \"objective\": \"Integrate the verified and reviewed rename/delete feature, the read-only deny fix and the documentation sync into one coherent, gate-clean change: persist the contract, validation and dossier as on-disk evidence, re-run the full gate sweep on the final tree, reconcile documentation against the shipped code, and report what changed, what was proven, what was deliberately not done, and what remains open.\", \"outOfScope\": [\"packages/mpd-workmate-plugin/src/\", \"packages/mpd-bundle-plugin/src/\", \"packages/mpd-roles-plugin/src/\", \"skills/dsh-qa/scripts/\"], \"round\": 1, \"subject\": \"Integrate and report: rename/delete + read-only fix + docs as one coherent change\", \"verify\": [\"bun test packages\", \"bun run typecheck\", \"bun run test:qa\", \"node scripts/verify-vendor.mjs\"]}"}}}}
