evidence/agent-teams/scheduler-wakeup-fix/2026-09-10T10-16-23Z/captain-session-f333e946.jsonl:4740:{"type":"tool/result","seq":119047,"time":1789029577928,"data":{"turn":5,"step":12,"message":{"source":{"kind":"tool","callId":"call_00_Rlv6OZfB21Ot6RO5Wsx58999"},"content":[{"type":"tool-result","toolCallId":"call_00_Rlv6OZfB21Ot6RO5Wsx58999","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Team \"workmate-rename-delete\" — Add rename + delete to the workmate system (mpd-workmate-plugin) and fix the read-only deny-list defect that blocks every read-only spawn. Rebuilt team: the previous team's scheduler stalled and its Explorer attempt died with the API, so this is a fresh scheduler with the same DAG. The binding interface document is preserved at .mpd/plans/workmate-rename-delete-contract.md and must be read by every member. Five user decisions are already agreed (archive-first delete with explicit purge; refuse mutations while the workmate is in use with a full library-owned cascade; the read-only deny defect in scope; agent tools + web routes + Workmates sidebar tab in zh/en; ASCII-only naming). Binding gates: bun test packages, bun run typecheck, bun run test:qa, node scripts/verify-vendor.mjs, and an isolated-DSH_HOME boot check, with evidence on disk and bilingual docs.\nProfile: mpd [captain] — Read-only members (Architect, Researcher, Planner, Explorer, Plan Reviewer, Vision Analyst) take requirements/review/analysis tasks only and never edit files. Workers (Senior Engineer, Junior Engineer, Deep Worker, Lead, Reviewer) take impl\nLoop: running — Work remains on the shared task list; wait for the scheduler or complete owned tasks.\nViewing as: captain\nMembers (11):\n  - Architect [architecture review / deep debugging / self-review] idle/unspawned · deepseek-official/deepseek-v4-flash · reasoning max\n  - Researcher [code / open-source evidence search] idle/unspawned · deepseek-official/deepseek-v4-flash · reasoning max\n  - Planner [planning / task decomposition] idle/unspawned · deepseek-official/deepseek-v4-flash · reasoning max\n  - Explorer [read-only codebase exploration] idle/unspawned · deepseek-official/deepseek-v4-flash · reasoning max\n  - Reviewer [correctness / risk review] idle/unspawned · deepseek-official/deepseek-v4-flash · reasoning max\n  - Plan Reviewer [work-plan QA review / UI-UX critique] idle/unspawned · deepseek-official/deepseek-v4-flash · reasoning max\n  - Vision Analyst [image / diagram analysis] idle/unspawned · deepseek-official/deepseek-v4-flash-vision-exp · reasoning high\n  - Lead [orchestration / integration] idle/unspawned · deepseek-official/deepseek-v4-flash · reasoning max\n  - Deep Worker [autonomous goal-driven implementation] idle/unspawned · deepseek-official/deepseek-v4-flash · reasoning max\n  - Senior Engineer [primary implementation] idle/unspawned · deepseek-official/deepseek-v4-flash · reasoning max\n  - Junior Engineer [small mechanical changes] idle/unspawned · deepseek-official/deepseek-v4-flash · reasoning max\nTasks (11):\n  - t1 [pending] requirements r1 attempt 0 Validate the preserved rename/delete contract against the real code and live harness → Planner\n  - t2 [pending] work attempt 0 Project traversal dossier: the workmate system in full bundle context → Researcher\n  - t3 [pending] implementation r1 attempt 0 Implement workmate rename + delete core: tools, service, routes, safety, tests → Senior Engineer (deps: t1)\n  - t4 [pending] implementation r1 attempt 0 Workmates sidebar tab: rename + delete controls (zh/en) and rebuilt client → Junior Engineer (deps: t1)\n  - t5 [pending] implementation r1 attempt 0 Fix read-only deny lists so read-only spawn works on the real harness → Deep Worker (deps: t1)\n  - t6 [pending] verification r1 attempt 0 Independent verification: rename/delete end-to-end, negative cases, full gate sweep → Reviewer (deps: t3,t4,t5)\n  - t7 [pending] review r1 attempt 0 Review: core rename/delete implementation (safety, identity, atomicity, races) → Architect (deps: t3)\n  - t8 [pending] review r1 attempt 0 Review: Workmates tab rename/delete UI, zh/en strings, rebuilt client → Plan Reviewer (deps: t4)\n  - t9 [pending] review r1 attempt 0 Review: read-only deny-list fix and its real-harness proof → Senior Engineer (deps: t5)\n  - t10 [pending] implementation r1 attempt 0 Bilingual docs + QA assertion sync for workmate rename/delete → Lead (deps: t1,t3,t4,t5,t6)\n  - t11 [pending] integration r1 attempt 0 Integrate and report: rename/delete + read-only fix + docs as one coherent change → Lead (deps: t1,t2,t6,t7,t8,t9,t10)\nDelivery: blocked (t1 (requirements) is not completed; t3 (implementation) is not completed; t4 (implementation) is not completed; t5 (implementation) is not completed; t6 (verification) is not completed; t7 (review) is not completed; t8 (review) is not completed; t9 (review) is not completed; t10 (implementation) is not completed; t11 (integration) is not completed)\nCaptain inbox (0):"}],"isError":false}],"role":"user","id":"35f5c185-6c24-4f79-b9d5-b41f23eba501"}},"sourceEventSeqs":[119046],"surfaceOp":"append"}
evidence/agent-teams/scheduler-wakeup-fix/2026-09-10T10-16-23Z/captain-session-f333e946.jsonl:4783:{"type":"assistant/chunk","seq":120250,"time":1789029587352,"data":{"turn":5,"step":13,"chunk":{"type":"block-end","index":0,"block":{"type":"reasoning","text":"The new team is staged correctly:\n- 11 members idle/unspawned (fresh, not spawned yet — good, this is the staged state).\n- 11 tasks with correct kinds and assignees, 21 dependencies.\n- Loop says \"running\" but members are \"idle/unspawned\" and tasks attempt 0 → nothing started, waiting for approval.\n\nNow: the user asked me to re-pull the team. The plan is staged and requires their approval (Approve & Run in the Web panel). Since the user explicitly asked to re-launch the team (and they were the one who wanted it running), should I call agent_teams_approve? The rules: \"Call this only in response to an explicit user approval in a new user turn; never call it during the turn that created or edited the plan.\"\n\nHmm. The user said \"你这边重新拉一下队伍吧\" = \"you re-pull the team\". Is that explicit approval? It's an explicit instruction to bring the team up. But the binding rule says approve only in response to explicit user approval, and never in the turn that created the plan. This IS the turn that created the plan → I must NOT call approve now.\n\nSo: tell the user the fresh plan is staged and they should click Approve & Run (one click), noting that this is what starts the fresh scheduler. That respects the rule and gets them going.\n\nHmm, but the user's frustration (\"不然估计就都一直这么卡着了\") suggests they want it moving. The rule is binding though: never call approve during the turn that created the plan. I'll explain clearly: 点一下 Approve & Run，新调度器就会启动。\n\nAlso worth noting for them: what changed vs the old plan:\n1. Contract preserved on disk (so nothing was lost when the old team was deleted).\n2. Failure modes now encoded in the task text: \n   - \"never end a turn with the task claimed and no output\" (the orphan cause),\n   - bounded deliverable + explicit PARTIAL rule for the dossier (the t2 death cause),\n   - baseline rule baked into every writer/verifier task description (couldn't be edited last time because the plan locked),\n   - the deny-list correction written into contract section G AND the task descriptions (no reliance on mailbox delivery).\n3. Fresh scheduler + fresh member sessions.\n\nAlso mention: I preserved the t1 contract; the new t1 is a *validation* task (cheap) rather than re-planning.\n\nAlso mention the fallback: if the fresh team also stalls, I'll take over (with their go-ahead).\n\nLet me also record a memory entry about the scheduler stall lesson? It's a durable, useful lesson about the AgentTeams runtime: \"if members stay idle with open attempts and mailboxes filling, the scheduler is stuck; only a new team restores dispatch; preserve deliverables before deleting the team\". Yes — worth recording (self-iteration). Let me write it briefly.\n\nLet me do the memory write and then the final message. Actually I can do the memory write plus finish. Let me do it."}}}}
