cause),\n   - bounded deliverable + explicit PARTIAL rule for the dossier (the t2 death cause),\n   - baseline rule baked into every writer/verifier task description (couldn't be edited last time because the plan locked),\n   - the deny-list correction written into contract section G AND the task descriptions (no reliance on mailbox delivery).\n3. Fresh scheduler + fresh member sessions.\n\nAlso mention: I preserved the t1 contract; the new t1 is a *validation* task (cheap) rather than re-planning.\n\nAlso mention the fallback: if the fresh team also stalls, I'll take over (with their go-ahead).\n\nLet me also record a memory entry about the scheduler stall lesson? It's a durable, useful lesson about the AgentTeams runtime: \"if members stay idle with open attempts and mailboxes filling, the scheduler is stuck; only a new team restores dispatch; preserve deliverables before deleting the team\". Yes — worth recording (self-iteration). Let me write it briefly.\n\nLet me do the memory write and then the final message. Actually I can do the memory write plus finish. Let me do it."},{"type":"tool-call","id":"call_00_d5e6FJmzM3UeUqo7LDzf8957","name":"mpd_memory_write","arguments":"{\"content\": \"AgentTeams runtime failure mode observed in this workspace (session 2026-09-10): the member scheduler can die while the team still reports Loop: running.\\n\\nSymptoms (all four together): every member shows idle/ready with no working/running member; tasks keep an open attempt (in_progress/pending with attempt N) but produce no output; agent_teams_send_message reports \\\"delivered via mailbox\\\" yet inboxes only accumulate (members never turn); `ps` shows no member processes; no files are written.\\n\\nKey facts learned:\\n- agent_teams_reassign_task revives an ORPHANED attempt (revokes it, issues a fresh one) and works while the team is running — but it does NOT wake members by itself.\\n- Captain messages do not wake members when the scheduler is dead; the mailbox is a queue, not a trigger.\\n- While the team is running the plan can NO LONGER be edited (agent_teams_edit_plan -> \\\"already running\\\"), so any guidance must go through messages. Bake all standing guidance (baseline, corrections, delivery rules) into task DESCRIPTIONS while the team is staged.\\n- Only a new team restores dispatch: agent_teams_delete + agent_teams_create(profile=mpd, approval=required).\\n- Deleting the team DESTROYS its task records, so salvage completed deliverables to disk FIRST (read-only members deliver text only; write it to a file yourself).\\n\\nPlan-authoring lessons that came out of this:\\n- A quality-kind task created WITH an explicit assignee silently degrades to kind=work; create without assignee and set the assignee via agent_teams_edit_plan update_task.\\n- implementation kind is rejected unless it depends on the staged requirements task.\\n- Dependencies must be removed before their dependents can be removed (edit_plan enforces order).\\n- Long, unbounded deliverables are an attempt-killer: bound the output (target lines) and require an explicit \\\"PARTIAL — not covered: X\\\" trailer, plus \\\"never end a turn with the task claimed and no output\\\".\", \"description\": \"Runbook for the AgentTeams scheduler stall: symptoms, what does and does not revive it, how to rebuild the team without losing deliverables, and the plan-authoring traps hit while rebuilding.\", \"kind\": \"note\", \"tags\": [\"agent-teams\", \"scheduler\", \"runbook\", \"orphaned-attempt\", \"plan-authoring\"], \"title\": \"AgentTeams scheduler stall: symptoms, salvage, and the rebuild runbook\"}"}],"source":{"kind":"model","provider":"deepseek-official","model":"deepseek-v4-flash"},"id":"b8d086fa-cc5a-485d-9ad9-58c4ad950be6"},"usage":{"inputTokens":1231,"outputTokens":1262,"totalTokens":229309,"cacheReadTokens":226816,"reasoningTokens":649}},"sourceEventSeqs":[[119050,120253]],"surfaceOp":"append"}
