evidence/agent-teams/scheduler-wakeup-fix/2026-09-10T10-16-23Z/captain-session-f333e946.jsonl:4832:{"type":"agent/inbox/spliced","seq":121152,"time":1789029632206,"data":{"target":"next-step","start":1,"inserted":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Agent b6ae16f7-2010-48dc-982d-5a5be4790b79 sent a message:"},{"type":"text","text":"Lead (workmate-rename-delete) — status: IDLE, no claim made.\n\nTeam \"workmate-rename-delete\" is live with 11 members and an 11-task DAG. I own 2 pending tasks, both correctly blocked upstream:\n- t10 [implementation] Bilingual docs + QA assertion sync for workmate rename/delete — deps t1,t3,t4,t5,t6\n- t11 [integration] Integrate and report: rename/delete + read-only fix + docs as one coherent change — deps t1,t2,t6,t7,t8,t9,t10\n\nPer the assignment rule I did NOT claim either: no dependency has started (t1 requirements, t3/t4/t5 implementations, t6 verification all still pending), so claiming would be work on blocked upstream. Delivery is blocked exactly on t1 not being completed plus the downstream impl/verify/review tasks.\n\nNo action needed from you right now. I will pick up t10 when t1/t3/t4/t5/t6 are terminal, then t11 after the review tasks (t7/t8/t9) land. If you want me to start earlier — e.g. drafting the bilingual docs skeleton against the preserved contract at .mpd/plans/workmate-rename-delete-contract.md before implementations finish — send that instruction and I will claim t10 with it in scope."}],"source":{"kind":"agent-message","form":"relay","senderSessionId":"b6ae16f7-2010-48dc-982d-5a5be4790b79"},"role":"user","id":"f0cca0c7-a001-4d1c-b9dc-e774db89510a"}]}}
