evidence/agent-teams/scheduler-wakeup-fix/2026-09-10T10-16-23Z/captain-session-f333e946.jsonl:4859:{"type":"tool-call-chunks","seq0":121823,"time0":1789029637665,"data":{"turn":6,"step":1,"index":1,"dt":[0,0,0,12,1,0,0,11,0,0,10,0,18,7,0,32,0,0,0,1,10,0,0,12,0,14,18,1,10,17,0,0,9,0,1,14,0,1,0,0],"id":"call_00_FuU6V099RBxZn9ll7IDU5974","name":"agent_teams_send_message","args":[" be"," driven",","," no"," screenshot"," can"," be"," captured",","," and"," any"," task"," asking"," you"," to"," analyse"," rendered"," UI"," would"," fail"," for"," environmental"," reasons","."," The"," Work","mates"," tab"," change"," will"," therefore"," be"," verified"," at"," source","/test","/","route"," level"," only",","]}}
evidence/agent-teams/scheduler-wakeup-fix/2026-09-10T10-16-23Z/captain-session-f333e946.jsonl:4868:{"type":"assistant/chunk","seq":121961,"time":1789029638529,"data":{"turn":6,"step":1,"chunk":{"type":"block-end","index":0,"block":{"type":"reasoning","text":"The Vision Analyst (new team) is up and reporting standby. Same as before by design — no task for it (no browser tooling in the sandbox; verified: no chromium binary, no playwright package).\n\nImportant: the new team's members are spawning and turning, which means the new scheduler IS alive. Good news.\n\nThe Vision Analyst keeps asking for work. It's now the second time. Should I:\n(a) Ignore (it's idle; no task);\n(b) Reply to decline with the reason (costs a turn but closes the loop and prevents future repeats — and good captaincy is to answer a direct offer).\n\nGiven it has now asked twice (in two different teams), a concise authoritative answer is right: explain the sandbox has no browser driver, so visual tasks would fail; state that its lane is deliberately unused this session and it should stay idle; and tell it not to re-report.\n\nHmm, but send_message to an idle member starts a turn → costs tokens. The alternative is silence. The instructions: \"never wait for an unassigned member to produce work it was never given\" — that's about not waiting; silence is acceptable. But a repeated standby pester wastes turns too, and a single clear \"no visual task this session, stay idle, do not re-report\" message reduces future noise.\n\nI'll send one short message. Also — I should check the team's dispatch state (is the scheduler working? are t1/t2 running?). The user hasn't approved yet... but members are spawning/turning, which happened in the last team too (before approval!). Hmm, in the previous team members turned while staged, and then the plan \"went running\" (approval). Here the Vision Analyst says \"team workmate-rename-delete\" and it's online → so the members are spawned/turning. Did the user approve? Let me check status.\n\nThat's the key question for my reply to the user: is the new team running already (approved by user) or still staged?\n\nLet me check status first, then decide the message to Vision Analyst, then report briefly to the user.\n\nActually let me do both: status + send the Vision Analyst message in one block? The message content doesn't depend on status. But whether I should even bother depends... no, the message is appropriate either way. Let me do both in parallel to save a round trip.\n\nWait — careful: if the team is still staged and members are turning (like last time), that's the same pre-approval churn. The message to Vision Analyst is still fine.\n\nLet me send a concise message + status check."}}}}
evidence/agent-teams/scheduler-wakeup-fix/2026-09-10T10-16-23Z/captain-session-f333e946.jsonl:4869:{"type":"assistant/chunk","seq":121962,"time":1789029638530,"data":{"turn":6,"step":1,"chunk":{"type":"block-end","index":1,"block":{"type":"tool-call","id":"call_00_FuU6V099RBxZn9ll7IDU5974","name":"agent_teams_send_message","arguments":"{\"content\": \"Captain → Vision Analyst. Standing answer, so you do not need to ask again: there is NO image/screenshot task for you in this session, and it is a verified environment limit rather than a scoping choice.\\n\\nI checked the sandbox myself: there is no chromium/chrome binary on PATH, ~/.cache/ms-playwright contains only empty cache directories (no chrome-linux/chrome and no headless_shell), and neither the repo, the global npm root, the bun global root nor the dsh install has a playwright/puppeteer package. So no browser can be driven, no screenshot can be captured, and any task asking you to analyse rendered UI would fail for environmental reasons. The Workmates tab change will therefore be verified at source/test/route level only, and I have told both the Plan Reviewer (t8) and the Lead (t11) not to require rendered visual evidence.\\n\\nYour lane stays deliberately unused: do not claim anything, do not report standby again, and do not treat idleness as a problem. If a future task ever needs diagram analysis (for example a design sketch or a rendered asset), I will assign it with the concrete file path.\", \"to\": \"Vision Analyst\"}"}}}}
evidence/agent-teams/scheduler-wakeup-fix/2026-09-10T10-16-23Z/captain-session-f333e946.jsonl:4873:{"type":"assistant/message","seq":121966,"time":1789029638531,"data":{"turn":6,"step":1,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"reasoning","text":"The Vision Analyst (new team) is up and reporting standby. Same as before by design — no task for it (no browser tooling in the sandbox; verified: no chromium binary, no playwright package).\n\nImportant: the new team's members are spawning and turning, which means the new scheduler IS alive. Good news.\n\nThe Vision Analyst keeps asking for work. It's now the second time. Should I:\n(a) Ignore (it's idle; no task);\n(b) Reply to decline with the reason (costs a turn but closes the loop and prevents future repeats — and good captaincy is to answer a direct offer).\n\nGiven it has now asked twice (in two different teams), a concise authoritative answer is right: explain the sandbox has no browser driver, so visual tasks would fail; state that its lane is deliberately unused this session and it should stay idle; and tell it not to re-report.\n\nHmm, but send_message to an idle member starts a turn → costs tokens. The alternative is silence. The instructions: \"never wait for an unassigned member to produce work it was never given\" — that's about not waiting; silence is acceptable. But a repeated standby pester wastes turns too, and a single clear \"no visual task this session, stay idle, do not re-report\" message reduces future noise.\n\nI'll send one short message. Also — I should check the team's dispatch state (is the scheduler working? are t1/t2 running?). The user hasn't approved yet... but members are spawning/turning, which happened in the last team too (before approval!). Hmm, in the previous team members turned while staged, and then the plan \"went running\" (approval). Here the Vision Analyst says \"team workmate-rename-delete\" and it's online → so the members are spawned/turning. Did the user approve? Let me check status.\n\nThat's the key question for my reply to the user: is the new team running already (approved by user) or still staged?\n\nLet me check status first, then decide the message to Vision Analyst, then report briefly to the user.\n\nActually let me do both: status + send the Vision Analyst message in one block? The message content doesn't depend on status. But whether I should even bother depends... no, the message is appropriate either way. Let me do both in parallel to save a round trip.\n\nWait — careful: if the team is still staged and members are turning (like last time), that's the same pre-approval churn. The message to Vision Analyst is still fine.\n\nLet me send a concise message + status check."},{"type":"tool-call","id":"call_00_FuU6V099RBxZn9ll7IDU5974","name":"agent_teams_send_message","arguments":"{\"content\": \"Captain → Vision Analyst. Standing answer, so you do not need to ask again: there is NO image/screenshot task for you in this session, and it is a verified environment limit rather than a scoping choice.\\n\\nI checked the sandbox myself: there is no chromium/chrome binary on PATH, ~/.cache/ms-playwright contains only empty cache directories (no chrome-linux/chrome and no headless_shell), and neither the repo, the global npm root, the bun global root nor the dsh install has a playwright/puppeteer package. So no browser can be driven, no screenshot can be captured, and any task asking you to analyse rendered UI would fail for environmental reasons. The Workmates tab change will therefore be verified at source/test/route level only, and I have told both the Plan Reviewer (t8) and the Lead (t11) not to require rendered visual evidence.\\n\\nYour lane stays deliberately unused: do not claim anything, do not report standby again, and do not treat idleness as a problem. If a future task ever needs diagram analysis (for example a design sketch or a rendered asset), I will assign it with the concrete file path.\", \"to\": \"Vision Analyst\"}"},{"type":"tool-call","id":"call_01_57ZNi05ftGtgJhXhnax81846","name":"agent_teams_status","arguments":"{}"}],"source":{"kind":"model","provider":"deepseek-official","model":"deepseek-v4-flash"},"id":"1cbe46d6-b509-45ff-a7a6-98a69bc23a3c"},"usage":{"inputTokens":258,"outputTokens":856,"totalTokens":231258,"cacheReadTokens":230144,"reasoningTokens":541}},"sourceEventSeqs":[[121153,121332],[121334,121925],[121927,121965]],"surfaceOp":"append"}
