evidence/agent-teams/scheduler-wakeup-fix/2026-09-10T10-16-23Z/captain-session-f333e946.jsonl:4961:{"type":"assistant/chunk","seq":123745,"time":1789029658075,"data":{"turn":6,"step":2,"chunk":{"type":"block-end","index":0,"block":{"type":"reasoning","text":"Excellent — the new team's scheduler is ALIVE and working: t1 in_progress (Planner), t2 claimed (Researcher), and 8 members show \"working/running\"! Members are running: Architect, Researcher, Planner, Explorer, Reviewer, Plan Reviewer, Deep Worker, Senior Engineer, Junior Engineer. Wait — that's 9 members \"working/running\" but only t1/t2 are active tasks. Hmm, several members are \"working/running\" without ready work (Architect, Reviewer, Plan Reviewer are running for t7/t8/t6 which are blocked...). They may be turning to process standby, or the runtime shows them as running while idle-ish.\n\nAnyway: dispatch works. The team is moving (t1 in progress, t2 claimed). So the rebuild fixed the stall.\n\nNow: two members reported idle-with-offers (Lead, Explorer). Explorer has no task this time (Researcher took the dossier) — it's offering help. Lead's tasks are blocked (correct).\n\nShould I act on the Explorer offer? Options: no (it's unassigned; no need). The Explorer offered lanes that duplicate t1 (contract validation — Planner) and t2 (dossier — Researcher). So: no new task. Don't wake it. (Same reasoning as before.)\n\nDo I need to respond to the Lead? It asked: \"If you want me to start earlier — e.g. drafting the bilingual docs skeleton... send that instruction.\" Hmm. Should I? The docs task depends on the implementations being done (documenting verified behaviour). Starting early risks writing docs that don't match shipping code (the acceptance explicitly says docs must match the shipped code). But drafting the *skeleton* (structure/sections + the parts already fixed by the contract: new tool names, routes, semantics from the contract) could save time. However, it risks doc drift and rework; also it burns a member turn. The value: the docs task is late in the chain; starting early could compress the critical path.\n\nGiven the team is now moving, and t3/t4/t5 will take a while, having the Lead pre-draft docs against the contract is genuinely useful and low-risk IF the drafts are clearly marked as pending verification. But the acceptance requires docs match the shipped code — a draft would need re-checking anyway (which the task already requires).\n\nDecision: I'll allow a bounded pre-draft, but only as guidance for when t10 becomes ready? Hmm — the Lead asked for an explicit instruction to claim t10 early with the skeleton in scope. Claiming t10 early would leave it unfinished while deps are pending... and the protocol says a task is only claimable when deps complete. The Lead itself said it can't claim blocked work. So \"claim t10 early\" isn't possible without... it said \"send that instruction and I will claim t10 with it in scope\" — but the scheduler would reject the claim (blocked deps). So its offer is technically infeasible; it would loop.\n\nSo: the right captain answer is \"no, wait for the deps; the scheduler will release t10\" — and no message needed (messaging wakes it pointlessly). I'll simply not act, and mention in my report that the two idle members correctly stayed idle and I declined the early-start offers.\n\nHmm, but the user asked me nothing right now — these are teammate messages arriving mid-session. My job: keep leading, report status.\n\nActually, one thing worth doing: the CURRENT turn was triggered by teammate messages. The user's last instruction was \"重新拉一下队伍吧\" — done. The team is now running (they must have clicked Approve, since t1/t2 are progressing... or the loop auto-started again). Either way, dispatch works.\n\nLet me verify that the previous stall symptoms are gone and give the user a short status. Also: is there anything I should proactively fix? \n\nOne item: I told the Vision Analyst \"do not report standby again\" — good.\n\nAnother: should I check whether the mailing of my earlier guidance succeeded this time? Not needed — I baked it into task text.\n\nLet me also record progress: t1 in progress, t2 claimed; 9 members running. And note the mails: Vision Analyst (answered), Lead (declined early start implicitly), Explorer (no lane needed).\n\nLet me do a quick sanity check that the contract file is in place and readable by members... it is (I wrote it).\n\nShould I do anything else productive while waiting? Yes — one genuinely useful thing: verify that the contract file doesn't contradict the live repo in ways that would mislead implementers. But the Planner's t1 is doing exactly that validation. Don't duplicate.\n\nAnother useful captain action: monitor. The runtime notifies me on progress. So: report to the user and end the turn so the scheduler can keep running (important: members run between captain turns!).\n\nGiven dispatch works best when my turn ends, I should keep this brief and end the turn.\n\nLet me write a concise update:\n- 调度器活了：t1 in_progress、t2 claimed、9 名成员在跑（这是新队伍重建后的第一波）。\n- 三名成员来报告：Vision Analyst（我给了终止性答复：本会话不做视觉任务，附沙箱无浏览器驱动的实测依据，并要求它不要再报 standby）；Lead（t10/t11 正确阻塞，它请求提前起草文档——我研判为不可行：依赖未完成时调度器不会放行认领，且文档必须对齐最终实现，所以让它按 DAG 排队）；Explorer（本次没有它的任务线，其提议的三条线与 t1/t2 重复，不新建任务）。\n- 我的下一步：等 t1/t2 落地后检查产出，重点核对 G 节 deny 纠正有没有被真正执行。\n- 提醒：成员回合在我的回合之间执行，所以我会尽量短回合让其推进。\n\nKeep it tight."}}}}
