evidence/agent-teams/scheduler-wakeup-fix/2026-09-10T10-16-23Z/captain-session-f333e946.jsonl:5009:{"type":"agent/inbox/spliced","seq":124846,"time":1789029669411,"data":{"target":"next-step","start":1,"inserted":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"AgentTeams message from member Architect:\n\nArchitect recon (no task claimed — t7 still blocked on t3; staying idle for the scheduler).\n\nI read the binding contract and the real sources. Four verified, implementation-shaping findings the workers will hit (all evidence-based, file:line):\n\n1. BLOCKER for t5 (read-only fix): updating only the source turns `bun test packages` RED. `packages/mpd-roles-plugin/test/roles.test.ts:106-107` asserts the deny list CONTAINS `str_replace_editor` and `apply_patch`:\n   `const writeTools = [\"write\",\"edit\",\"str_replace_editor\",\"apply_patch\",\"mpd_hashline_edit\",\"bash\",\"mcp__ast_grep__rewrite\",\"mcp__ast_grep__scan\",\"mcp__lsp__rename\"]; for (const t of writeTools) expect(READONLY_DENY).toContain(t)`\n   That assertion must be rewritten in the same change (drop the two dead names, keep `write`/`edit`/`mpd_hashline_edit`); otherwise t5 and t6 both fail the gate. Note `bash` is correctly NOT in the deny list (read-only children still need read/bash) — keep it out.\n\n2. dist/ is a runtime hazard, not just an artifact: `packages/mpd-roles-plugin/dist/index.js:338-342` and `packages/mpd-workmate-plugin/dist/index.js:215` still carry the 5-name deny list. The repo rule is \"rebuild the touched package's dist\" (AGENTS.md §8), so both `bun build …` steps must land in t5/t3 — a fix that only edits src leaves every real-harness read-only spawn failing with the identical `tools.restrict() names unknown global tools` error.\n\n3. t3 rename must NOT rely on `existsSync(target)` as the collision guard alone. Node's `fs.renameSync(oldDir, newDir)` on Linux silently OVERWRITES an existing empty target directory, and `rm -rf`-style purge of a symlink needs `lstat`. Recommendation: (a) use `lstatSync` and refuse if the instance dir or target is a symlink (contract §H \"symlinked instance dir — refused, not resolved\"); (b) keep the collision check + `renameSync` inside the SAME synchronous block as the in-use gate (contract §E already says gate+mutation share one block, no `await` between them — apply the identical rule to rename, not just delete).\n\n4. Bookkeeping gaps the contract explicitly requires and the current code does not do:\n   - `writeIndexEntry` (`src/index.ts:104-108`) only ever sets the NEW key; rename/delete must drop the OLD key (`delete idx[oldKey]`) and write once — the stale key otherwise lingers in index.json forever.\n   - `wmDir(\"\")` → library root (`src/index.ts:55`): guard `sanitizeName(raw) !== \"\" && raw === sanitizeName(raw)` at the top of both tools so the root can never be moved/removed.\n   - `mpd_workmate_spawn` must increment/decrement its in-process in-use counter around the `dsh.spawnAgent` await with a `finally` (throw path included), or a failed spawn leaks a permanent in-use block.\n   - `mpdWorkmate.delete` is a reserved-word property name: declare it as `delete: (…) => …` in the object literal, never `delete(...)` as a bare member (parse error).\n\nNo action needed from me; this is pre-emptive guidance for t3/t5. I will claim t7 the moment the scheduler assigns it."}],"source":{"kind":"plugin","plugin":"dsh-agent-teams"},"role":"user","id":"8761d4cf-96d5-4439-bf6e-abe4b84c1d57"}]}}
