evidence/agent-teams/scheduler-wakeup-fix/2026-09-10T10-16-23Z/captain-session-f333e946.jsonl:5037:{"type":"agent/inbox/spliced","seq":125113,"time":1789029673067,"data":{"target":"next-step","start":1,"inserted":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"AgentTeams message from member Plan Reviewer:\n\nPlan Reviewer — t8 readiness report (NOT claimed: t8 deps=[t4], t4 deps=[t1], all pending).\n\nRead: contract (all 146 lines incl. the middle section E/F/G that the earlier summary truncated), t4+t8 task descriptions, web-client.js, the offline client harness + sidebar-tab tests, build-mpd-client.mjs guards.\nBaseline recorded: HEAD f697088, 33 porcelain entries; client.js 15:36 vs src/web-client.js 15:27 — matches your freshness note (client.js carries `SIDEBAR_TAB_ID = \"mpd-workmate\"`); build guards for the removed workmate overlay floater / footer toggle are present and `process.exit(1)`.\n\nFIVE PRE-IDENTIFIED REVIEW CHECKPOINTS for t4 — forwarding now so the implementation can absorb them before I review (each is a contract requirement, not taste):\n\n1. BLOCKER-CLASS: `request()` (web-client.js:205-217) collapses every non-OK response to `new Error(body.error)` — it drops `status`, `reason` and `blocking[]`. Contract D says \"The GUI branches on `reason`\", and the wire table has four semantically distinct failures (400 invalid-name / 400 confirm-required / 404 unknown / 409 collision / 409 in-use). As written the UI CANNOT distinguish them, so the in-use refusal cannot name the blocking team+member that decision D2 explicitly requires. t4 must carry status+reason+blocking into the error path.\n\n2. Stale selection after mutation: `openDetail()` sets `selected`+`detail` from the old key. After rename the key changes, after delete the row is gone — the view must clear or reselect, else the detail pane shows a workmate that no longer exists (contract edge-case row \"GUI stale selection after a mutation\").\n\n3. zh/en key-set identity: zh is declared the source of truth and en must match key-for-key. Any new control needs entries in BOTH, plus assertions in the offline harness (sidebar-tab.test.mjs renders the real component, no browser needed).\n\n4. Delete must not be one destructive-looking click: D1 wants archive-first semantics communicated, and purge requires `confirm === <name>` — needs an explicit confirmation step in the UI.\n\n5. QUESTION for t4's scope: `SIDEBAR_TAB_TITLE = \"Workmates\"` is a hardcoded constant resolved at registration (web-client.js:373), and both dicts carry an identical `\"tab.title\": \"Workmates\"`, so the tab-strip label is NOT localized while the page body is. D4 says the surface is \"the Workmates sidebar tab (zh/en)\". Please confirm whether strip-label localization is in t4's scope or a documented deferral — I will review against whatever you decide, but it must be decided rather than left implicit.\n\nEvidence limit noted from your t8 description (no browser driver in sandbox) — I will judge from source + tests + built artifact + route contract and say so explicitly instead of implying visual verification.\n\nIdle and ready; will claim t8 the moment t4 completes."}],"source":{"kind":"plugin","plugin":"dsh-agent-teams"},"role":"user","id":"c0634c3b-19fa-4044-94f6-03449abeb932"}]}}
evidence/agent-teams/scheduler-wakeup-fix/2026-09-10T10-16-23Z/captain-session-f333e946.jsonl:5039:{"type":"agent/inbox/spliced","seq":125115,"time":1789029673610,"data":{"target":"next-step","start":3,"inserted":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Agent 6002e950-adbd-426f-878c-ac3ce3d1de4a sent a message:"},{"type":"text","text":"Architect (read-only reviewer) status: NO task claimed this turn — my only assigned task t7 (\"Review: core rename/delete implementation, safety/identity/atomicity/races\", deps t3) is still pending because t3 (Senior Engineer) is blocked on t1 (Planner requirements, in_progress). Team scheduler still dispatching to Planner/Researcher/Senior Engineer; I remain idle/ready and will claim t7 as soon as it is unlocked.\n\nWhat I did instead (pre-emptive recon, no files touched, no writes):\n- Read the binding contract .mpd/plans/workmate-rename-delete-contract.md in full (all sections A–I, including the captain-corrected §G and the §H edge-case matrix).\n- Read the real feature surface packages/mpd-workmate-plugin/src/index.ts (all 439 lines) to know exactly what t3 must extend: sanitizeName/wmDir, readIndex/writeIndexEntry, ensureInstance, listInstances, workmateLibrary {list,get,read}, mpd_workmate_{list,init,spawn,reflect,match}, and the lazy webRegistered route block.\n- Verified the regression test + dist hazards against the tree.\n\nFour verified findings sent to the captain (message 2ac18138), all actionable for t3/t5:\n1. packages/mpd-roles-plugin/test/roles.test.ts:106-107 currently asserts READONLY_DENY CONTAINS \"str_replace_editor\" and \"apply_patch\" — so the §G fix turns `bun test packages` red unless that assertion is updated in the same change. (bash must stay OUT of the deny list.)\n2. The dead names also live in packages/mpd-roles-plugin/dist/index.js:338-342 and packages/mpd-workmate-plugin/dist/index.js:215 — the dist rebuild is part of t5/t3, or the real-harness read-only spawn keeps failing.\n3. t3 rename must use lstatSync (refuse symlinked instance/target) and keep the collision check + renameSync in one synchronous block; fs.renameSync silently overwrites an existing empty target dir on Linux.\n4. Bookkeeping the contract requires but current code lacks: writeIndexEntry never deletes the OLD index key on rename/delete; wmDir(\"\") resolves to the library root and needs the raw===sanitizeName(raw) guard; spawn must decrement its in-use counter in a finally; mpdWorkmate `delete` is a reserved-word key.\n\nNo blockers, no permission issues, no edits made. Next turn: claim t7 when the scheduler assigns it."}],"source":{"kind":"agent-message","form":"relay","senderSessionId":"6002e950-adbd-426f-878c-ac3ce3d1de4a"},"role":"user","id":"dc9eae8d-3772-49ce-bdea-8625d3bddd10"}]}}
evidence/agent-teams/scheduler-wakeup-fix/2026-09-10T10-16-23Z/captain-session-f333e946.jsonl:5042:{"type":"user/message","seq":125118,"time":1789029673716,"data":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"AgentTeams message from member Architect:\n\nArchitect recon (no task claimed — t7 still blocked on t3; staying idle for the scheduler).\n\nI read the binding contract and the real sources. Four verified, implementation-shaping findings the workers will hit (all evidence-based, file:line):\n\n1. BLOCKER for t5 (read-only fix): updating only the source turns `bun test packages` RED. `packages/mpd-roles-plugin/test/roles.test.ts:106-107` asserts the deny list CONTAINS `str_replace_editor` and `apply_patch`:\n   `const writeTools = [\"write\",\"edit\",\"str_replace_editor\",\"apply_patch\",\"mpd_hashline_edit\",\"bash\",\"mcp__ast_grep__rewrite\",\"mcp__ast_grep__scan\",\"mcp__lsp__rename\"]; for (const t of writeTools) expect(READONLY_DENY).toContain(t)`\n   That assertion must be rewritten in the same change (drop the two dead names, keep `write`/`edit`/`mpd_hashline_edit`); otherwise t5 and t6 both fail the gate. Note `bash` is correctly NOT in the deny list (read-only children still need read/bash) — keep it out.\n\n2. dist/ is a runtime hazard, not just an artifact: `packages/mpd-roles-plugin/dist/index.js:338-342` and `packages/mpd-workmate-plugin/dist/index.js:215` still carry the 5-name deny list. The repo rule is \"rebuild the touched package's dist\" (AGENTS.md §8), so both `bun build …` steps must land in t5/t3 — a fix that only edits src leaves every real-harness read-only spawn failing with the identical `tools.restrict() names unknown global tools` error.\n\n3. t3 rename must NOT rely on `existsSync(target)` as the collision guard alone. Node's `fs.renameSync(oldDir, newDir)` on Linux silently OVERWRITES an existing empty target directory, and `rm -rf`-style purge of a symlink needs `lstat`. Recommendation: (a) use `lstatSync` and refuse if the instance dir or target is a symlink (contract §H \"symlinked instance dir — refused, not resolved\"); (b) keep the collision check + `renameSync` inside the SAME synchronous block as the in-use gate (contract §E already says gate+mutation share one block, no `await` between them — apply the identical rule to rename, not just delete).\n\n4. Bookkeeping gaps the contract explicitly requires and the current code does not do:\n   - `writeIndexEntry` (`src/index.ts:104-108`) only ever sets the NEW key; rename/delete must drop the OLD key (`delete idx[oldKey]`) and write once — the stale key otherwise lingers in index.json forever.\n   - `wmDir(\"\")` → library root (`src/index.ts:55`): guard `sanitizeName(raw) !== \"\" && raw === sanitizeName(raw)` at the top of both tools so the root can never be moved/removed.\n   - `mpd_workmate_spawn` must increment/decrement its in-process in-use counter around the `dsh.spawnAgent` await with a `finally` (throw path included), or a failed spawn leaks a permanent in-use block.\n   - `mpdWorkmate.delete` is a reserved-word property name: declare it as `delete: (…) => …` in the object literal, never `delete(...)` as a bare member (parse error).\n\nNo action needed from me; this is pre-emptive guidance for t3/t5. I will claim t7 the moment the scheduler assigns it."}],"source":{"kind":"plugin","plugin":"dsh-agent-teams"},"role":"user","id":"8761d4cf-96d5-4439-bf6e-abe4b84c1d57"},"surfaceOp":"append"}
