108`) only ever SETS the new key: rename/delete must delete the OLD key and write the file once, or the stale key lingers in `index.json` forever.\n- Guard `wmDir(\"\")` (line 55) at the top of both tools: `raw === sanitizeName(raw) && raw !== \"\"` before any fs call.\n- `mpd_workmate_spawn` must decrement its in-process in-use counter in a `finally` (throw path included), or one failed spawn leaks a permanent in-use block.\n- `mpdWorkmate.delete` must be declared as an object-literal property `delete: (…) => …` — a bare `delete(...)` member is a parse error.\n```\n\nGood. Now messages.\n\nMessage to Deep Worker (t5 owner):\n- Your pinned 7-name list is CORRECT; my contract §G wording was too narrow and I have amended it.\n- Do NOT remove bash or the MCP names.\n- Must: rebuild dist, re-point roles.test.ts:106-107, add a guard against re-adding dead names.\n\nMessage to Senior Engineer (t3 + t9):\n- §G amended: roles list keeps bash + MCP names; the workmate list (your t3 line 30) is the 3-name list — so your t3 change is exactly that.\n- Warn: for your t9 review, judge t5 against the amended §G, not the original text.\n- Plus the Architect's 5 t3 hazards.\n\nLet me execute: edit file (2 edits: §G replace + §J append), then 2 messages. The edits are dependent? No, independent (different strings). I can do both edits in parallel — careful: both modify the same file. Parallel edits to the same file could conflict. Let me do them sequentially: first the §G replace, then the append. Actually the edit tool applies literal replacement; doing them in one block risks a race on the file. Safer sequential.\n\nLet me start with the §G edit."},{"type":"text","text":"**Caught a security-relevant error in my own contract.** The real roles list is 7 names including `bash` and three write-capable MCP tools — my §G wording (\"leaving exactly write/edit/mpd_hashline_edit\") would have told t5 to delete `bash`, opening a shell-write bypass. Fixing the binding document first:"},{"type":"tool-call","id":"call_00_rZokHQ4U2pUK1nUH6GnX6819","name":"edit","arguments":"{\"file_path\": \"/root/dshProj/my-power-dsh/.mpd/plans/workmate-rename-delete-contract.md\", \"old_string\": \"Therefore **both** names must be removed from every `READONLY_DENY`\\n(`packages/mpd-roles-plugin/src/index.ts` and `packages/mpd-workmate-plugin/src/index.ts`), leaving exactly\\n`[\\\"write\\\",\\\"edit\\\",\\\"mpd_hashline_edit\\\"]`. Keeping either dead name leaves every read-only spawn failing with the\\nidentical error.\", \"new_string\": \"Therefore **both** names must be removed — and ONLY those two. Every other entry in each list is deliberately\\nkept, because those entries ARE the read-only guarantee:\\n\\n| File | Ships as | Removed |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| `packages/mpd-roles-plugin/src/index.ts:23-33` | `write, edit, mpd_hashline_edit, bash, mcp__ast_grep__rewrite, mcp__ast_grep__scan, mcp__lsp__rename` | `str_replace_editor`, `apply_patch` |\\n| `packages/mpd-workmate-plugin/src/index.ts:30` | `write, edit, mpd_hashline_edit` | `str_replace_editor`, `apply_patch` |\\n\\n**`bash` stays denied in the roles list.** It is not a read tool — a shell can write files, and\\n`packages/mpd-roles-plugin/test/roles.test.ts:106` exists precisely to keep the \\\"no shell/AST/LSP write bypass\\\"\\nproperty. Any claim that read-only children \\\"still need bash\\\" is wrong: `read`, `glob`, `grep` are not denied and\\nremain available. Likewise `mcp__ast_grep__rewrite`, `mcp__ast_grep__scan` and `mcp__lsp__rename` are\\nwrite-capable and stay denied — and unlike the two dead names, all three are live-registered.\\n\\nBoth `dist/index.js` copies must be rebuilt in the same change (the repo reads dist, not src), and\\n`packages/mpd-roles-plugin/test/roles.test.ts:106-107` currently PINS the two dead names and must be re-pointed in\\nthe same change, gaining a guard that they cannot come back. Keeping either dead name leaves every read-only spawn\\nfailing with the identical error.\"}"}],"source":{"kind":"model","provider":"deepseek-official","model":"deepseek-v4-flash"},"id":"88dd7f4c-705d-40b7-a73b-7c8a26f8493a"},"usage":{"inputTokens":1896,"outputTokens":3505,"totalTokens":244889,"cacheReadTokens":239488,"reasoningTokens":2868}},"sourceEventSeqs":[[125121,128593]],"surfaceOp":"append"}
evidence/agent-teams/scheduler-wakeup-fix/2026-09-10T10-16-23Z/captain-session-f333e946.jsonl:5160:{"type":"user/message","seq":128601,"time":1789029697357,"data":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"AgentTeams message from member Plan Reviewer:\n\nPlan Reviewer — t8 readiness report (NOT claimed: t8 deps=[t4], t4 deps=[t1], all pending).\n\nRead: contract (all 146 lines incl. the middle section E/F/G that the earlier summary truncated), t4+t8 task descriptions, web-client.js, the offline client harness + sidebar-tab tests, build-mpd-client.mjs guards.\nBaseline recorded: HEAD f697088, 33 porcelain entries; client.js 15:36 vs src/web-client.js 15:27 — matches your freshness note (client.js carries `SIDEBAR_TAB_ID = \"mpd-workmate\"`); build guards for the removed workmate overlay floater / footer toggle are present and `process.exit(1)`.\n\nFIVE PRE-IDENTIFIED REVIEW CHECKPOINTS for t4 — forwarding now so the implementation can absorb them before I review (each is a contract requirement, not taste):\n\n1. BLOCKER-CLASS: `request()` (web-client.js:205-217) collapses every non-OK response to `new Error(body.error)` — it drops `status`, `reason` and `blocking[]`. Contract D says \"The GUI branches on `reason`\", and the wire table has four semantically distinct failures (400 invalid-name / 400 confirm-required / 404 unknown / 409 collision / 409 in-use). As written the UI CANNOT distinguish them, so the in-use refusal cannot name the blocking team+member that decision D2 explicitly requires. t4 must carry status+reason+blocking into the error path.\n\n2. Stale selection after mutation: `openDetail()` sets `selected`+`detail` from the old key. After rename the key changes, after delete the row is gone — the view must clear or reselect, else the detail pane shows a workmate that no longer exists (contract edge-case row \"GUI stale selection after a mutation\").\n\n3. zh/en key-set identity: zh is declared the source of truth and en must match key-for-key. Any new control needs entries in BOTH, plus assertions in the offline harness (sidebar-tab.test.mjs renders the real component, no browser needed).\n\n4. Delete must not be one destructive-looking click: D1 wants archive-first semantics communicated, and purge requires `confirm === <name>` — needs an explicit confirmation step in the UI.\n\n5. QUESTION for t4's scope: `SIDEBAR_TAB_TITLE = \"Workmates\"` is a hardcoded constant resolved at registration (web-client.js:373), and both dicts carry an identical `\"tab.title\": \"Workmates\"`, so the tab-strip label is NOT localized while the page body is. D4 says the surface is \"the Workmates sidebar tab (zh/en)\". Please confirm whether strip-label localization is in t4's scope or a documented deferral — I will review against whatever you decide, but it must be decided rather than left implicit.\n\nEvidence limit noted from your t8 description (no browser driver in sandbox) — I will judge from source + tests + built artifact + route contract and say so explicitly instead of implying visual verification.\n\nIdle and ready; will claim t8 the moment t4 completes."}],"source":{"kind":"plugin","plugin":"dsh-agent-teams"},"role":"user","id":"c0634c3b-19fa-4044-94f6-03449abeb932"},"surfaceOp":"append"}
evidence/agent-teams/scheduler-wakeup-fix/2026-09-10T10-16-23Z/captain-session-f333e946.jsonl:5162:{"type":"user/message","seq":128603,"time":1789029697358,"data":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Agent 6002e950-adbd-426f-878c-ac3ce3d1de4a sent a message:"},{"type":"text","text":"Architect (read-only reviewer) status: NO task claimed this turn — my only assigned task t7 (\"Review: core rename/delete implementation, safety/identity/atomicity/races\", deps t3) is still pending because t3 (Senior Engineer) is blocked on t1 (Planner requirements, in_progress). Team scheduler still dispatching to Planner/Researcher/Senior Engineer; I remain idle/ready and will claim t7 as soon as it is unlocked.\n\nWhat I did instead (pre-emptive recon, no files touched, no writes):\n- Read the binding contract .mpd/plans/workmate-rename-delete-contract.md in full (all sections A–I, including the captain-corrected §G and the §H edge-case matrix).\n- Read the real feature surface packages/mpd-workmate-plugin/src/index.ts (all 439 lines) to know exactly what t3 must extend: sanitizeName/wmDir, readIndex/writeIndexEntry, ensureInstance, listInstances, workmateLibrary {list,get,read}, mpd_workmate_{list,init,spawn,reflect,match}, and the lazy webRegistered route block.\n- Verified the regression test + dist hazards against the tree.\n\nFour verified findings sent to the captain (message 2ac18138), all actionable for t3/t5:\n1. packages/mpd-roles-plugin/test/roles.test.ts:106-107 currently asserts READONLY_DENY CONTAINS \"str_replace_editor\" and \"apply_patch\" — so the §G fix turns `bun test packages` red unless that assertion is updated in the same change. (bash must stay OUT of the deny list.)\n2. The dead names also live in packages/mpd-roles-plugin/dist/index.js:338-342 and packages/mpd-workmate-plugin/dist/index.js:215 — the dist rebuild is part of t5/t3, or the real-harness read-only spawn keeps failing.\n3. t3 rename must use lstatSync (refuse symlinked instance/target) and keep the collision check + renameSync in one synchronous block; fs.renameSync silently overwrites an existing empty target dir on Linux.\n4. Bookkeeping the contract requires but current code lacks: writeIndexEntry never deletes the OLD index key on rename/delete; wmDir(\"\") resolves to the library root and needs the raw===sanitizeName(raw) guard; spawn must decrement its in-use counter in a finally; mpdWorkmate `delete` is a reserved-word key.\n\nNo blockers, no permission issues, no edits made. Next turn: claim t7 when the scheduler assigns it."}],"source":{"kind":"agent-message","form":"relay","senderSessionId":"6002e950-adbd-426f-878c-ac3ce3d1de4a"},"role":"user","id":"dc9eae8d-3772-49ce-bdea-8625d3bddd10"},"surfaceOp":"append"}
