evidence/agent-teams/scheduler-wakeup-fix/2026-09-10T10-16-23Z/captain-session-f333e946.jsonl:5246:{"type":"assistant/chunk","seq":131043,"time":1789029714966,"data":{"turn":6,"step":5,"chunk":{"type":"block-end","index":1,"block":{"type":"text","text":"Contract §G corrected. Now appending the verified hazards and the one open scope decision the reviewer escalated:"}}}}
evidence/agent-teams/scheduler-wakeup-fix/2026-09-10T10-16-23Z/captain-session-f333e946.jsonl:5247:{"type":"assistant/chunk","seq":131044,"time":1789029714966,"data":{"turn":6,"step":5,"chunk":{"type":"block-end","index":2,"block":{"type":"tool-call","id":"call_00_eEi636AQmTD7R3argipg1336","name":"edit","arguments":"{\"file_path\": \"/root/dshProj/my-power-dsh/.mpd/plans/workmate-rename-delete-contract.md\", \"new_string\": \"- Docs are BILINGUAL: every human-facing doc needs both `*.md` and `*.zh-CN.md` updated in the same change, each\\n  with the language switch link under its title. `AGENTS.md` is English-only.\\n\\n## J. Verified implementation hazards (member recon, file:line — absorb before coding)\\n\\n- Linux `fs.renameSync` **silently overwrites an existing empty target directory**, so `existsSync(target)` alone is\\n  not a sufficient collision guard. Use `lstatSync` and keep the collision check + `renameSync` in the SAME\\n  synchronous block as the in-use gate (§E) — the one-block rule applies to rename, not only to delete.\\n- Refuse a **symlinked** instance dir or symlinked target with `lstatSync` instead of resolving it (§H row).\\n- `writeIndexEntry` (`packages/mpd-workmate-plugin/src/index.ts:104-108`) only ever SETS the new key: rename and\\n  delete must delete the OLD key and write once, or the stale key lingers in `index.json` forever.\\n- Guard `wmDir(\\\"\\\")` (`src/index.ts:55`) at the top of both tools: require `raw === sanitizeName(raw) && raw !== \\\"\\\"`\\n  before any filesystem call.\\n- `mpd_workmate_spawn` must decrement its in-process in-use counter in a `finally` (throw path included); one failed\\n  spawn otherwise leaks a permanent in-use block on that workmate.\\n- `mpdWorkmate.delete` must be an object-literal property (`delete: (…) => …`); a bare `delete(...)` member is a\\n  parse error.\\n- GUI: `request()` in `packages/mpd-bundle-plugin/src/web-client.js:205-217` collapses every non-OK response into\\n  `new Error(body.error)` and **discards `status`, `reason` and `blocking[]`**. Contract §D requires the GUI to\\n  branch on `reason` and D2 requires the in-use refusal to name the blocking team + member, so the error path must\\n  carry them. Also: clear or reselect the detail view after a mutation (no stale selection), and keep the zh/en key\\n  sets identical with assertions in the offline harness.\\n- Every `dist/index.js` that embeds a deny list must be rebuilt in the same change — the repo runs dist, not src.\\n\\n## K. Deliberate deferral (captain decision, ask no further)\\n\\nThe sidebar **tab-strip label** (`SIDEBAR_TAB_TITLE = \\\"Workmates\\\"`, resolved at tab-registration time) stays a\\nhardcoded English constant in this change. The page body is fully localized zh/en; the strip label is not, because\\nit is resolved at registration where no localized `t` is in scope, and the sibling AgentTeams tab has the same\\nproperty. This is a documented deferral, not an oversight: record it in the docs (t10) and in the delivery report\\n(t11), and do NOT raise it as a review finding.\", \"old_string\": \"- Docs are BILINGUAL: every human-facing doc needs both `*.md` and `*.zh-CN.md` updated in the same change, each\\n  with the language switch link under its title. `AGENTS.md` is English-only.\"}"}}}}
evidence/agent-teams/scheduler-wakeup-fix/2026-09-10T10-16-23Z/captain-session-f333e946.jsonl:5250:{"type":"assistant/message","seq":131047,"time":1789029714969,"data":{"turn":6,"step":5,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"reasoning","text":"Now I must:\n1. Append §J to the contract (implementation hazards).\n2. Resolve the Plan Reviewer's open scope question (tab-strip label localization) — it's a genuine captain decision. Decision: the tab-strip label is a hardcoded constant in the tab registration; localizing it means making `title: () => t(...)` dynamic. The AgentTeams tab does... hmm. Options: (a) in scope (localize the strip label), (b) documented deferral. \n\nConsider: `title: () => SIDEBAR_TAB_TITLE` — making it localized requires the locale to be available at that point; `t` is passed into the component via props (translateFor). The registration uses a static function. Localizing would require the sidebar's locale service at registration time. Risky/fragile. Also the AgentTeams tab probably has a hardcoded title too, so localizing one and not the other is inconsistent.\n\nDecision: **documented deferral** — the page body is fully zh/en; the tab-strip label stays the hardcoded English \"Workmates\" for this change, recorded as an explicit deferral in the docs (t10) and the report (t11). Rationale: the label is resolved at tab-registration time when no localized `t` is in scope; localizing it would couple registration to the locale service and diverge from the sibling AgentTeams tab. The reviewer then judges against that decision. \n\nHmm, but is that the best for the user? The user's D4 was \"工具 + Workmates 侧边栏 GUI（zh/en）\" — meaning the GUI supports zh/en. The page body does; the strip label is a 1-word label. Deferring is defensible. Alternatively, in-scope: change `SIDEBAR_TAB_TITLE` to be resolved through the locale dict at registration... The sidebar may re-evaluate `title()` on each render — it's a function `() => ...`. So making it read from a module-level locale accessor could work. But we don't know if the locale service is reachable at that point (the component receives `t` via props). Risky.\n\nDecision: **explicit deferral**, documented. I need to tell the Plan Reviewer (t8 owner) and the t4 owner (Junior Engineer)? The Junior Engineer is waiting for t4; the decision affects t4's scope only if in-scope. Since it's a deferral, t4 stays as-is. I should reply to the Plan Reviewer (it asked for a decision) and record the decision in the contract (so it's visible). Adding it to the contract §A/§D area as a decision note is the cleanest — then no message needed... but the Plan Reviewer explicitly asked the captain to decide; if I only put it in the file, the reviewer may not re-read it. It said it reads the contract each turn. And I can also put it in the deferred list.\n\nHmm, messaging Plan Reviewer wakes it (cost). But it asked a direct question that gates its review verdict (\"it must be decided rather than left implicit\"). If I don't answer, when it reviews t8 it may raise it as a finding/needs_revision → repair loop. Cheaper to answer now: 1 message.\n\nAlso the Plan Reviewer's other 4 checkpoints are excellent (request() dropping status/reason/blocking; stale selection; zh/en key identity; delete confirmation). Those need to reach the **t4 implementer (Junior Engineer)** — otherwise the implementer won't know and the reviewer will return needs_revision, costing a full repair round. So: message Junior Engineer with those 5 checkpoints + the deferral decision. That's high value (prevents a repair loop).\n\nSimilarly, the Architect's 4 findings for t3 need to reach **Senior Engineer (t3)** — it said it deferred reading src lines 114-397 until t3 is assigned. I already planned to send Senior Engineer a message combining: (a) the amended §G (roles list keeps bash + MCP; workmate list = 3 names), (b) the Architect's hazards.\n\nAnd Deep Worker (t5) needs the §G amendment (its own reading was right; confirm + point to the amended §G).\n\nSo messages to send:\n1. Junior Engineer — t4 checkpoints (5 items) + deferral decision.\n2. Senior Engineer — t3 hazards + §G clarification (roles vs workmate list) for its t9 review later.\n3. Deep Worker — §G amended; your 7-name pinning is correct; plus dist rebuild + test re-point.\n4. Plan Reviewer — decision on the tab label (deferral) + acknowledgment.\n\nThat's 4 messages; each wakes an idle member (cost). But each prevents a repair loop or a wrong implementation — worth it. Hmm, can I reduce? \n\n- Deep Worker: critical (it will execute t5 soon; §G wording was wrong). MUST.\n- Senior Engineer: critical (t3 hazards + roles/workmate list distinction). MUST.\n- Junior Engineer: high value (5 checkpoints, else repair loop). YES.\n- Plan Reviewer: it asked; the decision also goes into the contract file. I could skip the message since the file now carries it... but it asked explicitly and will review against \"whatever you decide\". If the decision lives in the contract file, and the reviewer re-reads the contract, fine. Risk: it reviews t8 later and might have forgotten. It said it will review against the decision — as long as the decision is documented somewhere it can find. The contract file is the canonical place. I'll put it in the contract AND skip the message? Hmm.\n\nGiven the reviewer explicitly said \"Please confirm whether ... in t4's scope or a documented deferral — I will review against whatever you decide\", and I'm putting it in the contract file which it reads every turn... I think documenting in the contract + telling the Junior Engineer (so the implementation is consistent) is sufficient. But to be safe and explicit (it's cheap relative to a repair loop), I'll include the deferral decision in the Junior Engineer message and the contract, and skip a separate Plan Reviewer wake. Hmm, but the reviewer might not re-read... It read it \"in full\" this turn; the file changed since. It will re-read before reviewing t8 (that's its stated practice: \"Read ... in full\" each prep turn). Risk acceptable.\n\nActually — hold on. There's a subtlety: the contract file lives in `.mpd/plans/`, which members read. Good.\n\nDecision: 3 messages (Junior Engineer, Senior Engineer, Deep Worker) + contract updates (§J append + a deferral note).\n\nLet me now:\n1. Append §J + deferral note to contract (one edit or two).\n2. Send 3 messages.\n\nLet me write the §J append and a §K deferral note in a single edit appended to the end of the file (the file ends with the §I bullets: \"Docs are BILINGUAL: ...\"). Let me append after that.\n\nThe file's last lines:\n```\n- Docs are BILINGUAL: every human-facing doc needs both `*.md` and `*.zh-CN.md` updated in the same change, each\n  with the language switch link under its title. `AGENTS.md` is English-only.\n```\n\nI'll append §J and §K after that.\n\nLet me write the edit with old_string = that last block, new_string = same block + new sections.\n\nThen the 3 messages. Messages can go in one block (independent). But the edit should come first (so I can tell members the file is updated). Let me do the edit, then the messages in one block."},{"type":"text","text":"Contract §G corrected. Now appending the verified hazards and the one open scope decision the reviewer escalated:"},{"type":"tool-call","id":"call_00_eEi636AQmTD7R3argipg1336","name":"edit","arguments":"{\"file_path\": \"/root/dshProj/my-power-dsh/.mpd/plans/workmate-rename-delete-contract.md\", \"new_string\": \"- Docs are BILINGUAL: every human-facing doc needs both `*.md` and `*.zh-CN.md` updated in the same change, each\\n  with the language switch link under its title. `AGENTS.md` is English-only.\\n\\n## J. Verified implementation hazards (member recon, file:line — absorb before coding)\\n\\n- Linux `fs.renameSync` **silently overwrites an existing empty target directory**, so `existsSync(target)` alone is\\n  not a sufficient collision guard. Use `lstatSync` and keep the collision check + `renameSync` in the SAME\\n  synchronous block as the in-use gate (§E) — the one-block rule applies to rename, not only to delete.\\n- Refuse a **symlinked** instance dir or symlinked target with `lstatSync` instead of resolving it (§H row).\\n- `writeIndexEntry` (`packages/mpd-workmate-plugin/src/index.ts:104-108`) only ever SETS the new key: rename and\\n  delete must delete the OLD key and write once, or the stale key lingers in `index.json` forever.\\n- Guard `wmDir(\\\"\\\")` (`src/index.ts:55`) at the top of both tools: require `raw === sanitizeName(raw) && raw !== \\\"\\\"`\\n  before any filesystem call.\\n- `mpd_workmate_spawn` must decrement its in-process in-use counter in a `finally` (throw path included); one failed\\n  spawn otherwise leaks a permanent in-use block on that workmate.\\n- `mpdWorkmate.delete` must be an object-literal property (`delete: (…) => …`); a bare `delete(...)` member is a\\n  parse error.\\n- GUI: `request()` in `packages/mpd-bundle-plugin/src/web-client.js:205-217` collapses every non-OK response into\\n  `new Error(body.error)` and **discards `status`, `reason` and `blocking[]`**. Contract §D requires the GUI to\\n  branch on `reason` and D2 requires the in-use refusal to name the blocking team + member, so the error path must\\n  carry them. Also: clear or reselect the detail view after a mutation (no stale selection), and keep the zh/en key\\n  sets identical with assertions in the offline harness.\\n- Every `dist/index.js` that embeds a deny list must be rebuilt in the same change — the repo runs dist, not src.\\n\\n## K. Deliberate deferral (captain decision, ask no further)\\n\\nThe sidebar **tab-strip label** (`SIDEBAR_TAB_TITLE = \\\"Workmates\\\"`, resolved at tab-registration time) stays a\\nhardcoded English constant in this change. The page body is fully localized zh/en; the strip label is not, because\\nit is resolved at registration where no localized `t` is in scope, and the sibling AgentTeams tab has the same\\nproperty. This is a documented deferral, not an oversight: record it in the docs (t10) and in the delivery report\\n(t11), and do NOT raise it as a review finding.\", \"old_string\": \"- Docs are BILINGUAL: every human-facing doc needs both `*.md` and `*.zh-CN.md` updated in the same change, each\\n  with the language switch link under its title. `AGENTS.md` is English-only.\"}"}],"source":{"kind":"model","provider":"deepseek-official","model":"deepseek-v4-flash"},"id":"4fe8315f-74ee-4f05-afbf-0c23c4bda135"},"usage":{"inputTokens":3501,"outputTokens":2473,"totalTokens":250838,"cacheReadTokens":244864,"reasoningTokens":1642}},"sourceEventSeqs":[[128606,131046]],"surfaceOp":"append"}
