evidence/agent-teams/scheduler-wakeup-fix/2026-09-10T10-16-23Z/captain-session-f333e946.jsonl:5292:{"type":"assistant/chunk","seq":132397,"time":1789029727138,"data":{"turn":6,"step":6,"chunk":{"type":"block-end","index":0,"block":{"type":"tool-call","id":"call_00_ET_YpcNzu3SDCYeL0KSR3e28973","name":"agent_teams_send_message","arguments":"{\"content\": \"Captain → Deep Worker (t5 owner). Two things, both urgent for your fix.\\n\\n1) YOUR PINNING WAS RIGHT, AND MY CONTRACT WAS WRONG. You pinned the roles list as \\\"write, edit, mpd_hashline_edit, bash, mcp__ast_grep__rewrite, mcp__ast_grep__scan, mcp__lsp__rename\\\" minus the two dead names. That is the correct read. Contract §G originally said \\\"leaving exactly write/edit/mpd_hashline_edit\\\", which would have told you to DELETE bash and the three MCP names — a security regression. I have amended §G in .mpd/plans/workmate-rename-delete-contract.md with a per-file table; re-read it before you touch the code.\\n\\n   - packages/mpd-roles-plugin/src/index.ts:23-33 -> ships as: write, edit, mpd_hashline_edit, bash, mcp__ast_grep__rewrite, mcp__ast_grep__scan, mcp__lsp__rename (remove ONLY str_replace_editor + apply_patch)\\n   - packages/mpd-workmate-plugin/src/index.ts:30 -> ships as: write, edit, mpd_hashline_edit (remove ONLY the same two) — that line belongs to t3, do not touch it\\n   `bash` stays denied on purpose: a shell can write files, and packages/mpd-roles-plugin/test/roles.test.ts:106 exists to keep the \\\"no shell/AST/LSP write bypass\\\" property. An independent member argued \\\"read-only children still need bash\\\" — that is wrong; read/glob/grep are not denied and remain available.\\n\\n2) THE TWO THINGS YOUR SCOPE LIST ALREADY SPOTTED ARE PART OF THE FIX, not optional:\\n   - packages/mpd-roles-plugin/dist/index.js:338-342 carries the same dead names and the repo runs dist, not src — rebuild it (`cd packages/mpd-roles-plugin && bun build src/index.ts --target node --format esm --outfile dist/index.js`), and the same for any other touched package.\\n   - packages/mpd-roles-plugin/test/roles.test.ts:106-107 currently PINS the two dead names in its `writeTools` array, which is exactly why the suite stayed green through the defect. Re-point that assertion at the live-registry names in this same change and add a guard that the dead names cannot be re-added — otherwise `bun test packages` goes red for the wrong reason or, worse, silently re-pins the bug.\\n\\nYour out-of-scope call is also correct and approved: the `str_replace_editor` mentions in mpd-tools-plugin, mpd-hashline-plugin and mpd-comment-checker-plugin are `exec.name === ...` GUARDS, not deny lists — harmless, leave them; same for prose in READMEs and historical process docs. Do not end the turn with t5 claimed and no output.\", \"to\": \"Deep Worker\"}"}}}}
evidence/agent-teams/scheduler-wakeup-fix/2026-09-10T10-16-23Z/captain-session-f333e946.jsonl:5293:{"type":"assistant/chunk","seq":132398,"time":1789029727139,"data":{"turn":6,"step":6,"chunk":{"type":"block-end","index":1,"block":{"type":"tool-call","id":"call_01_ET_j94dd8jrzKgg2aQJtvcD7711","name":"agent_teams_send_message","arguments":"{\"content\": \"Captain → Senior Engineer (t3 owner, later t9 reviewer). Three things you need before you start; two of them correct or extend what is in the contract.\\n\\n1) §G CLARIFICATION — the two deny lists are NOT the same shape, and my original §G wording was wrong. It has been amended in .mpd/plans/workmate-rename-delete-contract.md (per-file table); re-read it.\\n   - YOUR line, packages/mpd-workmate-plugin/src/index.ts:30 -> ships as exactly [\\\"write\\\",\\\"edit\\\",\\\"mpd_hashline_edit\\\"]; remove only str_replace_editor and apply_patch.\\n   - The roles list (t5, not yours) -> keeps write, edit, mpd_hashline_edit, bash, mcp__ast_grep__rewrite, mcp__ast_grep__scan, mcp__lsp__rename. Do NOT \\\"unify\\\" the two lists, and do not remove bash anywhere: a shell can write, and roles.test.ts:106 exists to keep that bypass closed.\\n   - Later, when you review t5 as t9: judge it against the amended §G, not the original text.\\n\\n2) HAZARDS an independent reviewer verified for t3 (all file:line, all in your scope) — absorb them rather than rediscovering them:\\n   - Linux `fs.renameSync` silently OVERWRITES an existing EMPTY target directory, so `existsSync(target)` alone is not a sufficient collision guard. Use `lstatSync`, and keep the collision check + `renameSync` inside the SAME synchronous block as the in-use gate (§E's one-block rule applies to rename, not just delete).\\n   - Refuse a symlinked instance dir / symlinked target via `lstatSync` rather than resolving it (§H).\\n   - `writeIndexEntry` (src/index.ts:104-108) only ever SETS the new key — rename and delete must delete the OLD key and write once, or the stale key lingers in index.json forever.\\n   - `wmDir(\\\"\\\")` resolves to the LIBRARY ROOT (src/index.ts:55): require `raw === sanitizeName(raw) && raw !== \\\"\\\"` at the top of both tools, before any fs call.\\n   - `mpd_workmate_spawn` must decrement its in-process in-use counter in a `finally` (throw path included), else one failed spawn leaks a permanent in-use block.\\n   - `mpdWorkmate.delete` must be declared as an object-literal property (`delete: (…) => …`); a bare `delete(...)` member is a parse error.\\n\\n3) Contract §K records a captain decision so you do not re-litigate it: the sidebar tab-STRIP label stays hardcoded English \\\"Workmates\\\" in this change (the page body is zh/en; the strip label is resolved at tab-registration time where no localized `t` is in scope, and the sibling AgentTeams tab behaves the same). Documented deferral, not a finding.\\n\\nRebuild packages/mpd-workmate-plugin/dist after your source change — the repo runs dist. Do not end the turn with t3 claimed and no output.\", \"to\": \"Senior Engineer\"}"}}}}
