evidence/agent-teams/scheduler-wakeup-fix/2026-09-10T10-16-23Z/captain-session-f333e946.jsonl:5375:{"type":"assistant/message","seq":134331,"time":1789029746430,"data":{"turn":6,"step":8,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"reasoning","text":"Now report to the user. Key points:\n\n1. **A security-relevant error in my own contract, caught by member recon, now fixed.** The roles deny list is 7 names including `bash` + 3 write-capable MCP tools; my §G said \"leaving exactly write/edit/mpd_hashline_edit\" which would have removed `bash` (shell-write bypass!) and the MCP write tools. Two members disagreed with each other (Deep Worker: keep bash; Architect: \"bash is not in the list, keep it out\") — I read the source myself: bash IS at line 29, and roles.test.ts:106 asserts it as a write-capable tool. So: the fix is \"remove ONLY the two dead names, keep everything else\", per-file.\n2. Also amended the contract with verified hazards (§J) and the tab-label deferral decision (§K).\n3. Sent 3 targeted messages (pre-emptive, to avoid repair loops): Deep Worker (t5), Senior Engineer (t3), Junior Engineer (t4).\n4. Noted the highest-value catch: roles.test.ts:106-107 **pins the dead names**, which is why the defect survived a green test suite — that must be re-pointed + guarded in the same change; and dist/ copies must be rebuilt.\n5. Team state: t1 in progress, t2 claimed, all mappers reading the contract, nobody claiming blocked work; several members independently confirmed the baseline.\n\nThe user's last instruction was to rebuild the team — done and now progressing. My report should be concise but highlight the security catch (that's the important news) and the current state.\n\nLet me write it in Chinese, tight.\n\nAlso worth noting: the Architect's incorrect claim about bash — I should mention it because it shows I verified rather than relayed. Yes, briefly.\n\nLet me write."},{"type":"text","text":"队伍已在跑（`t1` 执行中、`t2` 已认领，全部成员都已读契约），但这一轮最有价值的事情是**成员侦察抓出了我自己契约里的一个安全错误，我已修正**。\n\n## 我犯的错（已修）\n\n契约 §G 我写的是\"两条死名字删掉后**只剩** `write/edit/mpd_hashline_edit`\"。但真实源码 `packages/mpd-roles-plugin/src/index.ts:23-33` 的列表是 **9 项**：\n\n```\nwrite, edit, str_replace_editor, apply_patch, mpd_hashline_edit,\nbash, mcp__ast_grep__rewrite, mcp__ast_grep__scan, mcp__lsp__rename\n```\n\n按我原来的措辞，t5 执行者会把 **`bash` 和三个可写 MCP 工具一起删掉**——那等于给只读专家放开 shell 写文件与 AST/LSP 改写权限，是**权限逃逸**。同文件 `test/roles.test.ts:106` 的存在意义正是守住这条（测试名就叫 \"no shell/AST/LSP write bypass\"）。\n\n两个成员还给出了**互相矛盾**的判断：Deep Worker 说\"保留 bash + 三个 MCP\"，Architect 说\"bash 本来就不在列表里，别加进去\"。我没有采信任一方，直接读了源码与测试：**bash 确实在第 29 行**，且测试把它列为可写工具 → Deep Worker 对、Architect 错。\n\n已修正契约 §G：改成**逐文件对照表**——只删那两个死名字，其余一律保留；roles 侧 7 项、workmate 侧 3 项，并写明\"`bash` 必须保持被禁\"及理由。同时新增两节：\n- **§J 已验证的实现陷阱**（file:line）：`renameSync` 在 Linux 会**静默覆盖已存在的空目录**（`existsSync` 不足以做冲突判定，需 `lstatSync` + 同一同步块）；`writeIndexEntry` 从不删除旧 index 键；`wmDir(\"\")` = 库根；spawn 的 in-use 计数必须在 `finally` 里递减；`mpdWorkmate.delete` 是保留字属性；GUI 侧 `request()` 丢弃 `status/reason/blocking[]`。\n- **§K 明确延后项**：侧边栏标签条的 \"Workmates\" 文案保持硬编码英文（页面主体是 zh/en），并注明是**决策性延后**、不得作为审查发现。\n\n## 两个\"本来会白烧一轮\"的关键发现，已前置下发\n\n1. **`roles.test.ts:106-107` 正是把两个死名字钉进断言的那行**——这就是缺陷能在全绿测试下存活的原因。必须在同一改动里改写该断言并加\"死名字不得回归\"的守卫。\n2. **`dist/index.js` 也带着旧列表**（roles:338-342、workmate:215），而仓库运行时读 dist 不读 src——不重建 dist，真 harness 上的只读 spawn 依旧失败。\n\n我已把这三条消息**前置**发给三位执行者（Deep Worker/t5、Senior Engineer/t3、Junior Engineer/t4，含 Plan Reviewer 提出的 5 个 t4 审查检查点），目的是让实现一次吸收、避免\"实现→审查 needs_revision→修复\"的空转。Architect 的其余 4 条发现全部正确且已转达（只有 bash 那条我纠正了）。\n\n## 当前队伍状态\n\n`t1`（契约校验）in_progress、`t2`（遍历档案）claimed，其余按依赖排队；成员均按规则**没有抢占被阻塞的任务**，多人独立复核了基线（HEAD `f697088` + 33 项未提交）。t1 一旦通过，`t3/t4/t5` 会自动并行开跑。\n\n我会继续盯：`t1` 的校验结论是否与 §G 修正一致、`t5` 是否真的重建 dist 并改写那条钉死断言，以及验证环节是否真在 sandbox HOME 下跑。"}],"source":{"kind":"model","provider":"deepseek-official","model":"deepseek-v4-flash"},"id":"3c4aa1c9-f5bb-4f8f-8929-f3dc53fbb18b"},"usage":{"inputTokens":255,"outputTokens":1308,"totalTokens":254363,"cacheReadTokens":252800,"reasoningTokens":391}},"sourceEventSeqs":[[133018,134330]],"surfaceOp":"append"}
evidence/agent-teams/scheduler-wakeup-fix/2026-09-10T10-16-23Z/captain-session-f333e946.jsonl:5378:{"type":"agent/inbox/spliced","seq":134334,"time":1789029863791,"data":{"target":"next-step","start":0,"inserted":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"AgentTeams message from member Planner:\n\nt1 COMPLETE — verdict=pass. The contract was validated against the tree AND the live harness. Result: 7 decided amendments (A1 is BLOCKING) + 1 ownership/serialization constraint. I am read-only, so the amendments live in this message and in t1's task output — please paste A1–A7 into `.mpd/plans/workmate-rename-delete-contract.md` (or relay them to t3/t4/t5) BEFORE the workers start, and adjust the DAG for the constraint below.\n\nBASELINE (pre-change, ALL FOUR OFFLINE GATES GREEN — nothing touched; HEAD f697088 + 33 porcelain entries identical before and after):\n- `bun test packages` → 218 tests / 28 files: 215 pass, 3 skip, 0 fail\n- `bun run typecheck` exit 0 · `node scripts/verify-vendor.mjs` PASS · `bun run test:qa` all self-tests passed\n- real HOME library (read-only peek) holds exactly one instance — `oracle-1` (+ index.json): the ideal rename subject (not a roster member name, readonly base).\n\nLIVE REPRODUCTION (my own, this session): `mpd_role_spawn {role:\"oracle\"}` →\n`Error: tools.restrict() names unknown global tools \"str_replace_editor\", \"apply_patch\"; known global tools: … bash … edit … mpd_hashline_edit … mcp__ast_grep__rewrite, mcp__ast_grep__scan, … mcp__lsp__rename … read … write …`\nHarness confirms whole-list validation: `dsh-tools/lib/index.js:2802-2804` (`unknown = [...allow,...deny].filter(n => !known.has(n))`, throws if any) → ONE dead name aborts every read-only spawn. Decisive for A1: the other SEVEN names of the roles list are all restrictable live, and neither dead name is registered by any composed row (bundle patch + preset verified).\n\n**A1 — BLOCKING (security + gate).** §G's \"leaving exactly [write, edit, mpd_hashline_edit]\" is correct ONLY for the workmate array. Applied literally to the ROLES array it also deletes `bash`, `mcp__ast_grep__rewrite|scan`, `mcp__lsp__rename` — all live-known write bypasses — a policy regression, and it breaks `roles.test.ts:105-112`. Correct final arrays (decided):\n- `packages/mpd-workmate-plugin/src/index.ts:30` → `[\"write\", \"edit\", \"mpd_hashline_edit\"]` (drop only the 2 dead names)\n- `packages/mpd-roles-plugin/src/index.ts:23-33` → remove ONLY lines 26+27 → `[\"write\",\"edit\",\"mpd_hashline_edit\",\"bash\",\"mcp__ast_grep__rewrite\",\"mcp__ast_grep__scan\",\"mcp__lsp__rename\"]`\nTest sync required: `packages/mpd-roles-plugin/test/roles.test.ts:106-112` asserts the 9 names including both dead ones (it passes today); it MUST be rewritten to the 7-name list or the `bun test packages` gate goes red.\n\n**A2 — must-decide (recommend ALIGN).** The workmate array has no `bash` and no MCP write tools, so a readonly workmate could still write through bash. Today that is masked (every readonly spawn throws); this fix un-masks it. Recommend: both arrays carry the same 7 names + a test asserting the two arrays are equal (kills the drift class permanently). If declined, t10 must document the asymmetry.\n\n**A3 (t3) — fs paths must key on the DIRECTORY, never `meta.name`.** Today `listInstances()` (line 181) returns `meta.name` and reads the note via `meta.name`; `ensureInstance` returns only `{meta}` and reflect writes via `wmDir(meta.name)` (326-335) → after a rename (or an interrupted one) a later reflect can resurrect the OLD dir and `list` shows a name that no longer resolves. Decided: `ensureInstance` → `{meta, dir, key}` with `key = sanitizeName(name)`; every write uses `key`; `listInstances` returns `name: e.name`; get/read/list normalize `name` to the key; `writeIndexEntry` takes the key. Test: dir `alice` whose meta.json says \"stale\" → list shows alice, reflect writes alice/, index key alice.\n\n**A4 (t3) — `readMeta` (81-87) is a whitelist, so `renamedFrom` would be silently DROPPED on the next reflect.** Add optional `renamedFrom?: string[]` to `Meta` + readMeta (default `[]`), append the previous key on rename (dedupe, cap 10), and carry it through init/reflect/rename writes. Test: rename → reflect → `renamedFrom` survives and `get()` exposes it.\n\n**A5 (t3) — §F tension (\"note.md self-reference updated\" vs \"note content byte-for-byte\").** Decided rule: rewrite ONLY a leading `<baseName>-based workmate \"<oldKey>\".` prefix to the new key; if the note does not start with that prefix (custom note passed at init, line 242) leave the bytes untouched. This keeps `autoNote`'s `prev.startsWith(prefix)` dedupe (line 132) correct. Test both branches.\n\n**A6 (t6/t10) — the repo has 7 non-archived team records, not 6**, and every one carries the 11 roster member names. Blocked keys: architect, researcher, planner, explorer, reviewer, plan-reviewer, vision-analyst, lead, deep-worker, senior-engineer, junior-engineer. So (i) happy-path renames must avoid those keys (use `oracle-1` → `oracle-2`), and (ii) the 409 in-use path is free and deterministic HERE by renaming to `architect` — use that instead of fabricating team state. The scan design is unaffected: direct children only; `archive/` has no `archive/team.json` → excluded by construction; `retired-members.json` is a file → skipped by the isDirectory filter.\n\n**A7 (t4) — artifact + i18n gates.** `sidebar-tab.test.mjs` loads the COMMITTED `packages/mpd-bundle-plugin/client.js` (line 17) → t4 must run `node scripts/build-mpd-client.mjs` in the same change or the tests exercise stale bytes. Bundle rows point at `dist/index.js` (patch lines 149/174) → t3/t5 must rebuild `bun build src/index.ts --target node --format esm --outfile dist/index.js`. No zh/en key-parity test exists → t4 should add `Object.keys(zh).sort() === Object.keys(en).sort()`, since D4's zh/en requirement is currently unenforced. `request()` (205-217) throws `Error(body.error)` and drops `reason`/`blocking` → extend it, or §D's \"the GUI branches on reason\" is unimplementable.\n\n**ORDERING / OWNERSHIP CONSTRAINT.** t3 and t5 BOTH write `packages/mpd-workmate-plugin/src/index.ts` and rebuild the same `dist/` → running them in parallel risks a lost update. Recommended split that keeps t3/t4/t5 fully parallel with zero file overlap: t3 owns ALL of `packages/mpd-workmate-plugin/**` (including the line-30 array + its test + dist rebuild); t5 owns `packages/mpd-roles-plugin/**` + the shared governance tests + the live readonly-spawn proof; t4 owns `packages/mpd-bundle-plugin/**`. Alternative: keep t5 on both files but make t5 depend on t3.\n\nMinor confirmations (no action needed): `wmDir(\"\")` = library root is CONFIRMED (54-65) and the D5 rule (`raw === sanitizeName(raw) && raw !== \"\"`) already rejects `\"\"` and `\"   \"`, so the explicit root guard is belt-and-braces — keep it. §D's archive path in a SUCCESS body may be absolute (the no-absolute-path rule is scoped to error bodies); tests should assert `existsSync(body.archived)`. §E's sync-block rule needs `renameSync`/`rmSync`/`lstatSync` added to the line-13 `node:fs` import — no `node:fs/promises`, no `await` between gate and mutation, and `try/finally` around the spawn counter (an uncaught throw would otherwise block mutations forever). §H spawn/reflect-vs-rename: both bodies are synchronous inside an async fn → no in-process interleaving; the residual risk is a SECOND dsh process on the same HOME (document in t10, do not fix). §E(b) sees only teams in the CURRENT workspace while the library is cross-project → documented residual limitation.\n\nNothing else is waiting on me; t3/t4/t5 unlock now."}],"source":{"kind":"plugin","plugin":"dsh-agent-teams"},"role":"user","id":"ef2fb1cc-b52f-4994-af82-fc27bfdaa1ff"}]}}
