name). A literal reading deletes live write bypasses (security regression) and fails `roles.test.ts:105-112`, which asserts the 9 names and passes today.\n- A2 must-decide (recommend align): the workmate array lacks bash + the 3 MCP write tools; the fix un-masks that hole. Recommend both arrays carry the same 7 names + an equality test.\n- A3: fs paths must key on the DIRECTORY, not `meta.name` (`listInstances` line 181, reflect 326-335) — otherwise reflect can resurrect the old dir after a rename.\n- A4: `readMeta` is a whitelist → `renamedFrom` would be silently dropped on the next reflect.\n- A5: decided rule for §F's note.md tension — rewrite only the leading identity prefix, custom notes stay byte-identical.\n- A6: 7 non-archived team records (not 6); blocked keys are the 11 roster member names; the 409 in-use path is free here via renaming to `architect`.\n- A7: t4 must rebuild `packages/mpd-bundle-plugin/client.js` (the test loads the artifact) and add the missing zh/en key-parity test; `request()` drops `reason`/`blocking`, so §D's GUI branch is unimplementable without extending it.\n- ORDERING CONSTRAINT: t3 and t5 both write `packages/mpd-workmate-plugin/src/index.ts` + its dist → keep them parallel only if t3 owns all of that package and t5 owns `mpd-roles-plugin` + tests + the live proof (or make t5 depend on t3).\n\nNEXT: paste A1–A7 into the contract file / relay to t3/t4/t5 before they start, and apply the ownership split. Nothing else is waiting on me; t3/t4/t5 are now unlocked."}],"source":{"kind":"agent-message","form":"relay","senderSessionId":"0939898a-8f09-4084-835a-0901f2f255b8"},"role":"user","id":"1f68db88-ea50-40a6-9277-5c101c56cbd7"}]}}
