_DENY`) so the roles-side test can assert both arrays are equal — t5 owns that guard, you own the export.\\n\\nA3 (fs paths key on the DIRECTORY, never `meta.name`): `ensureInstance` returns `{meta, dir, key}` with `key = sanitizeName(name)`; every write uses `key`; `listInstances` returns the DIRECTORY name; list/get/read normalize to the key; `writeIndexEntry` takes the key. Without this, a later reflect resurrects the OLD dir after a rename and `list` can show a name that no longer resolves. Test: dir `alice` with `meta.json` saying `stale` → list shows alice, reflect writes alice/, index key alice.\\n\\nA4 (`renamedFrom` must enter `readMeta`'s whitelist, `src/index.ts:81-87`): otherwise it is silently dropped on the next reflect. Add `renamedFrom?: string[]` to Meta + readMeta (default []), append the previous key on rename (dedupe, cap 10), carry it through the init/reflect/rename writes. Test: rename → reflect → renamedFrom survives and get() exposes it.\\n\\nA5 (resolves the §F tension): rewrite ONLY a LEADING `<baseName>-based workmate \\\"<oldKey>\\\".` prefix in note.md. If the note does not start with that prefix (custom note from init), leave the bytes untouched — this keeps autoNote's prev.startsWith(prefix) dedupe correct. Test both branches.\\n\\nA6 (use these keys in tests): there are SEVEN non-archived team records, each carrying all 11 roster names, so the blocked keys are architect, researcher, planner, explorer, reviewer, plan-reviewer, vision-analyst, lead, deep-worker, senior-engineer, junior-engineer. Your happy-path test must NOT use them — use `oracle-1` → `oracle-2`. The 409 in-use case is deterministic by renaming to `architect`.\\n\\nA7: rebuild packages/mpd-workmate-plugin/dist after the source change (bundle rows point at dist). Also note the harness validates the whole filter list (dsh-tools/lib/index.js:2802-2804), so a partial deny-list edit changes nothing on the real harness.\\n\\nOwnership is decided and needs no extra dependency: t3 owns ALL of packages/mpd-workmate-plugin/** (including line 30, its tests, the dist rebuild); t5 owns packages/mpd-roles-plugin/** and will not touch your package. Do not end the turn with t3 claimed and no output.\", \"to\": \"Senior Engineer\"}"},{"type":"tool-call","id":"call_01_4w5MqbVCiUyQNRP5AeAy9530","name":"agent_teams_send_message","arguments":"{\"content\": \"Captain → Deep Worker (t5). The t1 validator independently reproduced the defect live and confirmed your reading. Two additions to your scope, both from contract section L (re-read §G and §L before coding):\\n\\nA1 (as you pinned it, now binding): packages/mpd-roles-plugin/src/index.ts:23-33 keeps seven names — write, edit, mpd_hashline_edit, bash, mcp__ast_grep__rewrite, mcp__ast_grep__scan, mcp__lsp__rename — and ONLY str_replace_editor + apply_patch leave. `bash` stays denied on purpose (a shell can write; roles.test.ts:106 exists to keep the \\\"no shell/AST/LSP write bypass\\\" property); an independent member argued the opposite and was wrong.\\n\\nA2 (NEW, captain decision ALIGN — a second file in your scope): the workmate-side array in packages/mpd-workmate-plugin/src/index.ts:30 is being brought up to the SAME seven names by t3, which EXPORTS it. Your job on the roles side adds the parity guard: assert in packages/mpd-roles-plugin/test/roles.test.ts that the roles array and the exported workmate array are EQUAL. That kills the drift class that let this defect hide. Do NOT edit anything under packages/mpd-workmate-plugin/** — only import from it.\\n\\nAlso required, as before: rewrite the assertion at roles.test.ts:105-112 (it currently pins the two dead names, which is why a green suite hid the defect) and add a guard that the dead names cannot come back; rebuild packages/mpd-roles-plugin/dist/index.js:338-342 (the repo runs dist, not src).\\n\\nNew evidence available to you: the harness validates the WHOLE restriction list at dsh-tools/lib/index.js:2802-2804 and throws before any child is created — so the live proof you owe is that a read-only mpd_role_spawn now STARTS a child. Your out-of-scope call on the `exec.name === \\\"str_replace_editor\\\"` guards in mpd-tools/hashline/comment-checker plugins remains approved: leave them. Do not end the turn with t5 claimed and no output.\", \"to\": \"Deep Worker\"}"}],"source":{"kind":"model","provider":"deepseek-official","model":"deepseek-v4-flash"},"id":"20c42a39-49e5-4a1c-a835-d1314ac1c3d8"},"usage":{"inputTokens":180,"outputTokens":1547,"totalTokens":264127,"cacheReadTokens":262400,"reasoningTokens":185}},"sourceEventSeqs":[[138821,140308]],"surfaceOp":"append"}
