evidence/agent-teams/scheduler-wakeup-fix/2026-09-10T10-16-23Z/captain-session-f333e946.jsonl:5670:{"type":"assistant/message","seq":142271,"time":1789029933846,"data":{"turn":7,"step":5,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"reasoning","text":"Now report to the user. Keep it concise but cover:\n\n1. t1 passed (verdict=pass) with a live reproduction and a green baseline (215 pass/0 fail, typecheck 0, verify-vendor PASS, test:qa pass) — and the tree unchanged by the read-only member.\n2. The t1 validator independently found A1 = exactly my §G correction (good: two independent confirmations).\n3. The decision I made (A2 ALIGN): I decided to align both deny lists to 7 names, closing a real hole (readonly workmate could write via bash; masked until now because the spawn was broken). Plus the parity test to prevent drift.\n4. A3/A4/A5 implementation corrections adopted into the contract (dir-key not meta.name; renamedFrom whitelist; note-prefix rule).\n5. A6: seven stale teams (not six) → free deterministic 409 test; happy path uses oracle-1→oracle-2.\n6. A7: client.js is loaded by the test (rebuild required); dist rebuild; missing zh/en parity test.\n7. Ownership: t3 owns the whole workmate package; t5 owns roles; zero overlap → fully parallel (no extra dependency).\n8. Messages sent to t3/t5/t6 owners; contract updated (§G, §L).\n9. Status: t2 still running (dossier), t3/t4/t5 unlocked and will start.\n\nNote: I should double check — is the user waiting for me to do something specific? Their last message was about re-pulling the team. I did. Now I'm reporting progress. Good.\n\nKeep it in Chinese, compact, with the decision highlighted.\n\nI should also mention: the AMENDMENTS were possible because the contract is a FILE (not plan text) — that's why the team can still be steered while running. Nice detail.\n\nLet me write it."},{"type":"text","text":"`t1` 通过（verdict=pass），校验者**独立复现了缺陷并逐条核对了契约**——其中包括与我此前修正完全一致的 A1（deny 列表逐文件对照），两条独立证据链吻合。它同时带来 7 条修订和 1 条只有队长能拍板的决策，我已全部处理完。\n\n## 我做的决策：A2 — 两个 deny 列表**对齐**（ALIGN）\n\n问题：roles 侧列表有 7 项（含 `bash` + 3 个可写 MCP），workmate 侧只有 3 项。这意味着**只读 workmate 仍可通过 bash 写文件**——这个洞今天被\"只读 spawn 全线失败\"掩盖着，而恰恰是这次修复会把它**暴露出来**。\n\n我的裁决：两处统一为同一组 7 个名字（`write, edit, mpd_hashline_edit, bash, mcp__ast_grep__rewrite, mcp__ast_grep__scan, mcp__lsp__rename`），并要求 workmate 侧**导出**该数组、roles 侧测试**断言两者相等**——一次性消除这个漂移类缺陷（正是它让死名字躲过了全绿测试）。\n\n## 已并入契约的其余修订（§L 新增，§G 修订）\n\n| 项 | 内容 | 归属 |\n|---|---|---|\n| A3 | **文件系统路径必须以目录名为准，绝不用 `meta.name`**；否则改名后一次 reflect 会把**旧目录复活**、`list` 显示已失效的名字 | t3 |\n| A4 | `readMeta` 是白名单，`renamedFrom` 会被静默丢弃 → 需加入白名单并贯穿各写入路径 | t3 |\n| A5 | §F 矛盾的裁决：只改写 note.md **开头那一段身份前缀**，自定义 note 保持字节不变（同时保住 `autoNote` 的去重逻辑） | t3 |\n| A6 | 历史团队记录是 **7 个**不是 6 个，阻塞键位=全部 11 个角色名 → 改名测试走 `oracle-1 → oracle-2`；**409 in-use 用例可直接用改名为 `architect` 免费拿到**，无需伪造团队状态 | t3/t6 |\n| A7 | `sidebar-tab.test.mjs:17` 加载的是**已提交的 client.js**（不重建就是测旧字节）；bundle 行指向 `dist/index.js`；zh/en 键一致性此前**无测试**，需补 | t4/t3/t5 |\n\n另外确定**所有权切分**（消除并行写同一文件的丢更新风险）：t3 独占 `packages/mpd-workmate-plugin/**`（含第 30 行、测试、dist 重建），t5 独占 `packages/mpd-roles-plugin/**`（含 parity 守卫），t4 独占 `packages/mpd-bundle-plugin/**` —— **零文件重叠，三者真并行**，不需要额外依赖。\n\n## 下发情况\n\n三条针对性指令已投递：t3（A2/A3/A4/A5/A6/A7 全部落点）、t5（A1 确认 + parity 守卫 + 不得改动 workmate 包）、t6（验证配方：happy path 用 `oracle-1→oracle-2`、in-use 用 `architect`、archive 路径断言 `existsSync(body.archived)`，并要求验证\"只读 workmate 的 deny 里含 bash\"与\"renamedFrom 经 reflect 后仍存在\"）。\n\n值得一提：**契约放在文件里而不是计划文本里，是这次能在队伍运行时继续纠偏的关键**——计划一旦 running 就锁死，但 `.mpd/plans/workmate-rename-delete-contract.md` 可随时修订，且每条任务都要求成员先读它。\n\n`t2`（遍历档案）仍在跑；`t3/t4/t5` 已解锁，应立即开跑。我会盯 t5 是否真重建 dist 并改写那条钉死断言、以及 t3 是否落实 A3（目录键）——这两条是最容易\"看起来做完实际没做\"的地方。"}],"source":{"kind":"model","provider":"deepseek-official","model":"deepseek-v4-flash"},"id":"9c488481-4bbd-4ebb-91ff-17d725b6cb1b"},"usage":{"inputTokens":201,"outputTokens":1326,"totalTokens":266231,"cacheReadTokens":264704,"reasoningTokens":401}},"sourceEventSeqs":[[140940,142270]],"surfaceOp":"append"}
evidence/agent-teams/scheduler-wakeup-fix/2026-09-10T10-16-23Z/captain-session-f333e946.jsonl:5673:{"type":"agent/inbox/spliced","seq":142274,"time":1789029999262,"data":{"target":"next-step","start":0,"inserted":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"AgentTeams message from member Researcher:\n\nt2 COMPLETED (Researcher, read-only dossier). Full text is in the t2 task output; the items that change what t3/t4/t5/t6 must do:\n\n1) DENY DEFECT — independent live reproduction at BOTH call sites (mpd_role_spawn{librarian} and mpd_workmate_spawn{oracle-1}): identical `tools.restrict() names unknown global tools \"str_replace_editor\", \"apply_patch\"`, thrown before any child is created. I captured the FULL live registry (104 names): write/edit/mpd_hashline_edit/bash/mcp__ast_grep__rewrite/mcp__ast_grep__scan/mcp__lsp__rename are ALL present, both dead names absent ⇒ §L A2's 7-name list is spawn-safe by name. Validation source: dsh-tools/lib/index.js:2802-2804, set = view(scope).restrictableNames (lib/index.js:2863-2881; excludes scope-local names).\n\n2) IN-USE GATE — seven non-archived teams confirmed, blocked keys exactly A6's 11. IMPORTANT: QA boots HOME=<sandbox> but cwd=repo, so the gate reads the REAL .mpd/team → sandbox cases must also avoid roster keys; the in-use case is free via rename→architect (oracle-1 exists in the real home, not in a sandbox). `mpd_config_get team.stateDir` → null here ⇒ hardcode `<cwd>/.mpd/team`; do not attempt a config lookup.\n\n3) FILESYSTEM (measured): renameSync onto an EXISTING EMPTY dir SUCCEEDS silently (data-integrity hazard, §J confirmed); non-empty → ENOTEMPTY; file target → ENOTDIR; a DANGLING symlink target is invisible to existsSync(false) but visible to lstatSync, and rename then throws ENOTDIR. ⇒ collision guard must lstat the target and map ANY hit to 409 collision so no raw fs error escapes as a non-§D body.\n\n4) t4 HARNESS BLOCKERS: client-harness.mjs fetchImpl (L327-332) can only return 200-body or 404 {error} — 409 in-use/collision and 400 confirm-required are NOT expressible without extending the stub; and ctx.locale.register (L294) discards the {zh,en} dicts, so A7's key-parity assertion needs the 2nd arg captured or the dicts exported.\n\n5) CONTRACT GAPS (recommendations, 5 live in the dossier §5): (a) §H \"readonly instance as mutation target\" still has NO decided outcome — recommend ALLOW; (b) same-key rename has no §D reason code — recommend 400 invalid-name; (c) dir without meta.json — recommend 404 unknown, no fs mutation; (d) a child spawned before a rename cannot reflect afterwards (prompt hardcodes the key) — decide whether renamedFrom resolves legacy keys; (e) lstat guard as in (3).\n\n6) Do NOT edit the stale copies that greps hit: .qa-reloc/**, dist/mpd-package/**, and TRACKED evidence/scan/t3-20260829/build/mpd-workmate-plugin.js. Live files are only src/index.ts + dist/index.js and src/web-client.js + client.js. VENDOR_LOCK locks only upstream assets (skills, agent-teams _deps, 4 MCP dist files) → rebuilds do not affect verify-vendor.\n\n7) NOTE: the contract file grew 146→248 lines while I worked (mtime 08:41Z); my dossier is aligned with the latest §A–§L revision, including A2 deny parity, A3 directory-key, A4 renamedFrom, A6 seven teams, A7 artifact/i18n. Baseline: HEAD f697088 + 33 porcelain entries; my targeted test run = 21 pass / 0 fail."}],"source":{"kind":"plugin","plugin":"dsh-agent-teams"},"role":"user","id":"08aded73-105c-475f-90fc-4ee0a0b1ccba"}]}}
