evidence/agent-teams/scheduler-wakeup-fix/2026-09-10T10-16-23Z/captain-session-f333e946.jsonl:5834:{"type":"assistant/chunk","seq":147213,"time":1789030044781,"data":{"turn":8,"step":2,"chunk":{"type":"block-end","index":1,"block":{"type":"tool-call","id":"call_00_SafZoPtj5fMaNAm93rSg9943","name":"agent_teams_send_message","arguments":"{\"content\": \"Captain → Senior Engineer (t3). The t2 dossier landed and I have decided all five gaps it surfaced; they are now binding contract section M. Read §G, §L and §M before you code — §M is short and every item lands in your file.\\n\\nM1 — readonly instances ARE valid mutation targets: ALLOW. Rename/delete are library administration by the calling agent, not the workmate editing itself. No extra block, no extra reason code.\\n\\nM2 — same-key rename: 400 + reason \\\"invalid-name\\\", error text says the new name equals the current key. No fs side effect.\\n\\nM3 — a directory without meta.json (orphan): 404 + reason \\\"unknown\\\", zero fs mutation. Never touch a directory the library cannot address.\\n\\nM4 — a reflect arriving with a LEGACY key must NOT resolve through renamedFrom: fail with \\\"no workmate named X\\\" and zero side effects, never resurrect a directory. renamedFrom stays informational (surfaced by list/get/read). This is a deliberate captain decision — do not add legacy-key resolution.\\n\\nM5 — collision guard = lstat the target and map ANY hit to 409 collision. Measured facts to defend against (t2 ran the probes): renameSync onto an EXISTING EMPTY directory succeeds SILENTLY, non-empty gives ENOTEMPTY, a file target gives ENOTDIR, and a DANGLING symlink is invisible to existsSync but visible to lstatSync (after which rename throws ENOTDIR). No raw fs error may escape as a non-§D body.\\n\\nM6 — read team state from `<cwd>/.mpd/team`, hardcoded: mpd_config_get team.stateDir returns null in this deployment, so do not add a config lookup. Note QA boots HOME=<sandbox> but cwd=repo, so the gate still sees the REAL team records — your tests must avoid roster keys for the same reason production does.\\n\\nM7 — never edit the stale mirrors your greps will hit: .qa-reloc/**, dist/mpd-package/**, and the tracked evidence/scan/** copy. Live files are only packages/mpd-workmate-plugin/{src,dist} — plus A7's dist rebuild, which does NOT affect verify-vendor (VENDOR_LOCK covers upstream assets only).\\n\\nStill binding from §L: A2 export the workmate READONLY_DENY and raise it to the same seven names as the roles list; A3 key all fs paths on the directory, never meta.name; A4 add renamedFrom to the readMeta whitelist; A5 rewrite only the leading identity prefix in note.md.\\n\\nDo not end the turn with t3 claimed and no output.\", \"to\": \"Senior Engineer\"}"}}}}
