me reason production does.\\n\\nM7 — never edit the stale mirrors your greps will hit: .qa-reloc/**, dist/mpd-package/**, and the tracked evidence/scan/** copy. Live files are only packages/mpd-workmate-plugin/{src,dist} — plus A7's dist rebuild, which does NOT affect verify-vendor (VENDOR_LOCK covers upstream assets only).\\n\\nStill binding from §L: A2 export the workmate READONLY_DENY and raise it to the same seven names as the roles list; A3 key all fs paths on the directory, never meta.name; A4 add renamedFrom to the readMeta whitelist; A5 rewrite only the leading identity prefix in note.md.\\n\\nDo not end the turn with t3 claimed and no output.\", \"to\": \"Senior Engineer\"}"}}
evidence/agent-teams/scheduler-wakeup-fix/2026-09-10T10-16-23Z/captain-session-f333e946.jsonl:5857:{"type":"tool/result","seq":147267,"time":1789030049137,"data":{"turn":8,"step":3,"message":{"source":{"kind":"tool","callId":"call_00_boawDJZUOBefgCiFcOWN5077"},"content":[{"type":"tool-result","toolCallId":"call_00_boawDJZUOBefgCiFcOWN5077","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Team \"workmate-rename-delete\" — Add rename + delete to the workmate system (mpd-workmate-plugin) and fix the read-only deny-list defect that blocks every read-only spawn. Rebuilt team: the previous team's scheduler stalled and its Explorer attempt died with the API, so this is a fresh scheduler with the same DAG. The binding interface document is preserved at .mpd/plans/workmate-rename-delete-contract.md and must be read by every member. Five user decisions are already agreed (archive-first delete with explicit purge; refuse mutations while the workmate is in use with a full library-owned cascade; the read-only deny defect in scope; agent tools + web routes + Workmates sidebar tab in zh/en; ASCII-only naming). Binding gates: bun test packages, bun run typecheck, bun run test:qa, node scripts/verify-vendor.mjs, and an isolated-DSH_HOME boot check, with evidence on disk and bilingual docs.\nProfile: mpd [captain] — Read-only members (Architect, Researcher, Planner, Explorer, Plan Reviewer, Vision Analyst) take requirements/review/analysis tasks only and never edit files. Workers (Senior Engineer, Junior Engineer, Deep Worker, Lead, Reviewer) take impl\nLoop: running — Work remains on the shared task list; wait for the scheduler or complete owned tasks.\nViewing as: captain\nMembers (11):\n  - Architect [architecture review / deep debugging / self-review] idle/ready · deepseek-official/deepseek-v4-flash · reasoning max\n  - Researcher [code / open-source evidence search] idle/ready · deepseek-official/deepseek-v4-flash · reasoning max\n  - Planner [planning / task decomposition] idle/ready · deepseek-official/deepseek-v4-flash · reasoning max\n  - Explorer [read-only codebase exploration] idle/ready · deepseek-official/deepseek-v4-flash · reasoning max\n  - Reviewer [correctness / risk review] idle/ready · deepseek-official/deepseek-v4-flash · reasoning max\n  - Plan Reviewer [work-plan QA review / UI-UX critique] idle/ready · deepseek-official/deepseek-v4-flash · reasoning max\n  - Vision Analyst [image / diagram analysis] idle/ready · deepseek-official/deepseek-v4-flash-vision-exp · reasoning high\n  - Lead [orchestration / integration] idle/ready · deepseek-official/deepseek-v4-flash · reasoning max\n  - Deep Worker [autonomous goal-driven implementation] idle/ready · deepseek-official/deepseek-v4-flash · reasoning max\n  - Senior Engineer [primary implementation] idle/ready · deepseek-official/deepseek-v4-flash · reasoning max\n  - Junior Engineer [small mechanical changes] idle/ready · deepseek-official/deepseek-v4-flash · reasoning max\nTasks (11):\n  - t1 [completed] requirements r1 verdict pass attempt 1 Validate the preserved rename/delete contract against the real code and live harness → Planner\n  - t2 [completed] work attempt 1 Project traversal dossier: the workmate system in full bundle context → Researcher\n      output: # t2 DOSSIER — the workmate system in full bundle context (Researcher, read-only)\n\nBaseline: HEAD f697088, `git status --porcelain` = 33 entries (unchanged by me; I edited nothing).\nContract revision read: `.mpd/plans/workmate-rename-delete-contract.md` grew 146→248 lines WHILE this task ran\n(mtime \n  - t3 [pending] implementation r1 attempt 0 Implement workmate rename + delete core: tools, service, routes, safety, tests → Senior Engineer (deps: t1)\n  - t4 [pending] implementation r1 attempt 0 Workmates sidebar tab: rename + delete controls (zh/en) and rebuilt client → Junior Engineer (deps: t1)\n  - t5 [pending] implementation r1 attempt 0 Fix read-only deny lists so read-only spawn works on the real harness → Deep Worker (deps: t1)\n  - t6 [pending] verification r1 attempt 0 Independent verification: rename/delete end-to-end, negative cases, full gate sweep → Reviewer (deps: t3,t4,t5)\n  - t7 [pending] review r1 attempt 0 Review: core rename/delete implementation (safety, identity, atomicity, races) → Architect (deps: t3)\n  - t8 [pending] review r1 attempt 0 Review: Workmates tab rename/delete UI, zh/en strings, rebuilt client → Plan Reviewer (deps: t4)\n  - t9 [pending] review r1 attempt 0 Review: read-only deny-list fix and its real-harness proof → Senior Engineer (deps: t5)\n  - t10 [pending] implementation r1 attempt 0 Bilingual docs + QA assertion sync for workmate rename/delete → Lead (deps: t1,t3,t4,t5,t6)\n  - t11 [pending] integration r1 attempt 0 Integrate and report: rename/delete + read-only fix + docs as one coherent change → Lead (deps: t1,t2,t6,t7,t8,t9,t10)\nDelivery: blocked (t3 (implementation) is not completed; t4 (implementation) is not completed; t5 (implementation) is not completed; t6 (verification) is not completed; t7 (review) is not completed; t8 (review) is not completed; t9 (review) is not completed; t10 (implementation) is not completed; t11 (integration) is not completed)\nCaptain inbox (0):\nMember inbox Reviewer (1): latest — Captain → Reviewer (t6). Your pre-finding was correct and is now folded into the binding contract as section L (plus an \nMember inbox Vision Analyst (1): latest — Captain → Vision Analyst. Standing answer, so you do not need to ask again: there is NO image/screenshot task for you in\nMember inbox Deep Worker (2): latest — Captain → Deep Worker (t5). The t1 validator independently reproduced the defect live and confirmed your reading. Two ad\nMember inbox Senior Engineer (3): latest — Captain → Senior Engineer (t3). The t2 dossier landed and I have decided all five gaps it surfaced; they are now binding\nMember inbox Junior Engineer (2): latest — Captain → Junior Engineer (t4). The t2 dossier found two hard blockers in your test path; both are now binding contract "}],"isError":false}],"role":"user","id":"dc44d9af-22c9-412a-918b-a98d5d50e3ea"}},"sourceEventSeqs":[147266],"surfaceOp":"append"}
