evidence/wave2/t8-verification/20260911T061046Z/attempt2/check3-t13-captain.raw.json:96:        "evidence": "Reproduced pre-fix: the covering pattern stayed in outOfScope, so classifyChangedPath('AGENTS.md') = out_of_scope while the repair's acceptance required that edit. Post-fix, replayed through the REAL archived inputs (team mpd-default-7332aba4, t7 inScope/outOfScope + t10 findings F1-cocotb-lane-venv-root and F3-agents-md-state-root-stale): generated inScope = [t7 inScope…, 'packages/mpd-verif-plugin/src/venv.ts', 'AGENTS.md'] and generated outOfScope = ['presets/**','packages/mpd-bundle/cordis.patch.yml','VENDOR_LOCK.json','README.md','README.zh-CN.md'] — AGENTS.md dropped from the prohibitions. classifyChangedPath('AGENTS.md')=in_scope and classifyChangedPath('packages/mpd-verif-plugin/src/venv.ts')=in_scope, while the prohibitions no finding requires still hold (VENDOR_LOCK.json and presets/mpd/agent.cordis.yml = out_of_scope), and contractContradiction(generated) = none. Raw log: evidence/wave2/adopted-tooling-repair/f1/real-inputs-replay.log. Falsifiable test from the same inputs: 'DEFECT 2 fix, REAL wave-1 inputs (team mpd-default-7332aba4 t7 + t10): the required edit is in scope' (30 pass / 0 fail, f2/self-fix-suite.log)."
evidence/wave2/t8-verification/20260911T061046Z/attempt2/check3-t13-captain.raw.json:104:        "criterion": "F2 CLOSED: every behaviour-changing line t4 introduced in `lib/quality-gates.js` sits inside a registered `mpd-delta` region — specifically the three groups the verifier named as unmarked (`inScopeOverlap` ~252-255, `normalizeScopePattern` ~263-267, the create-time contradiction gate ~405-412), and `lib/mpd-deltas.js` is regenerated so the guard can detect and restore ALL of them. t4 acceptance 4 must pass when re-judged",
evidence/wave2/t8-verification/20260911T061046Z/attempt2/check3-t13-captain.raw.json:106:        "evidence": "The three named groups are now inside registered regions: mpd-delta scope-overlap (inScopeOverlap rewrite), mpd-delta scope-overlap-normalize (normalizeScopePattern), mpd-delta create-contract-gate (the create-time contradiction gate in validateCreateTask); all 9 regions and their spans are listed in f2/region-inventory.log. The whole pathMatchesScope function now lives inside mpd-delta scope-glob (so a re-materialize cannot leave a stray upstream copy behind), and lib/mpd-deltas.js was regenerated to 9 regions (guard: 'already applied: 9 mpd delta region(s) across 2 adopted file(s)'). The new F2 test performs a real LCS line diff between the pre-delta revision (git HEAD) and the working tree and asserts that EVERY added line is inside a region, a marker line, or prose — zero executable lines outside a region (plus explicit assertions that the three named groups are inside). Raw log: f2/self-fix-suite.log. Two guard-side root causes found while closing F2 and fixed in the same pass: writeRegistry could pick an anchor living INSIDE another region (the old scope-glob anchor was pathMatchesScopeNormalized, declared by the neighbouring scope-glob-core region), so a dropped region took its own anchor with it and healed nothing — anchors are now selected outside every region span; and --write-registry no longer runs a same-process verification that could only ever see the pre-write registry."
evidence/wave2/t8-verification/20260911T061046Z/attempt2/check3-t13-captain.raw.json:109:        "criterion": "F3 CLOSED: the healing path in `scripts/vendor-agent-teams.mjs` (~line 122, which always runs with write:true) must REFUSE — or post-validate — when inserting a region would redefine a declaration the file still carries. Reproduce the verifier's exact scenario (the hand re-materialize the guard exists for): the old path produced two `export function pathMatchesScope` and the file FAILED TO IMPORT with `Identifier 'pathMatchesScope' has already been declared` while `--write` and the next `--check` both exited 0. After the fix, that scenario must fail loudly with a named cause, and a clean re-materialize must still succeed",
evidence/wave2/t8-verification/20260911T061046Z/attempt2/check3-t13-captain.raw.json:111:        "evidence": "Verifier scenario reproduced in a sandbox (upstream quality-gates.js from git HEAD + our tools.js/mpd-deltas.js, then the heal path) and captured in f3/hand-rematerialize.log: post-fix --write exits 1 with '[patch-agent-teams-fixes] FAIL: refusing to heal delta \"mpd-delta scope-glob\" … it declares \"pathMatchesScope\" but that declaration still exists OUTSIDE any region at line 102 — the file was re-materialized with the OLD body; remove the old declaration (or restore the marked file) before healing, otherwise the healed module fails to import'; --check also exits 1 (verify-only, region MISSING); the refused file is byte-identical to the input with exactly 1 declaration (no half-heal, no double declaration). vendor-agent-teams.mjs turns the refusal into a failed run (process.exit(1)) instead of a green 'applied'. A clean re-materialize still succeeds: 'F3: a clean (region-carrying) tree still heals successfully' re-inserts 7 regions and the next pass verifies byte-identical (f2/self-fix-suite.log). Implementation note: the collision check is restricted to MODULE-scope declarations — an earlier draft also matched a nested loop local (const key) and wrongly refused a valid heal, a bug the test caught."
evidence/wave2/t8-verification/20260911T061046Z/attempt2/check3-t13-captain.raw.json:114:        "criterion": "The three fixes are proven together by re-running the verifier's own driver where possible (evidence/wave2/t8-verification/20260911T061046Z/) rather than inventing a parallel harness",
evidence/wave2/t8-verification/20260911T061046Z/attempt2/check3-t13-captain.raw.json:116:        "evidence": "Re-ran the t8 drivers in place: check5-mount.sh (gates/mount-driver-rerun.raw.json — 14/14 tools, task_contract REGISTERED, 0 apply-crash signatures, probe DONE; gates/mount-driver-rerun also refreshed check5-plugin-suite.log) and check4-guard-failure.sh (gates/guard-driver-rerun.log — all failure modes exit 1 with a named cause, live tree untouched, sha256 equal before/after). The F1 confirmation re-reads the archived inputs from .mpd/team/archive/mpd-default-7332aba4/team.json exactly as the verifier did, and the F3 confirmation reproduces the verifier's hand re-materialize (HEAD file + our registry) rather than a synthetic surrogate. Two driver expectations are stale against this repair and are stated rather than worked around: the driver hard-codes `7 regions` (now 9) and mutates the merged-away scope-glob-core region, so S5 skips its mutation and S1 prints 9. The in-region drift case that S5 intends is verified directly: mutating one line inside the scope-glob region makes --check exit 1 naming the exact line ('lines 102-195 … first difference at line 118') while the pristine tree exits 0."
evidence/wave2/t8-verification/20260911T061046Z/attempt2/check3-t13-captain.raw.json:121:        "evidence": "bun test packages/mpd-agent-teams-plugin = 87 pass / 0 fail (gates/plugin-suite.log); self-fix suite = 30 pass / 0 fail (f2/self-fix-suite.log); bun test packages = 340 pass / 0 fail across 38 files (gates/full-suite.log); bun run typecheck exit 0 (gates/typecheck.log). Isolated mounted boot: AGENT_TEAMS_TOOLS_PRESENT=14/14, T4_TOOL_agent_teams_task_contract=REGISTERED, apply_crash_signatures=0 (gates/mount-driver-rerun.raw.json) — no --dump-config result is cited as load evidence. The mount driver's own passed=false is its workspace-isolation counter: the flagged .mpd/team/mpd-default-587132ea was created by captain session session-8954c880-eee (a concurrent teammate), not by this boot, whose leak counters are 0 (real_workspace_session_keys_in_sandbox=0); that item belongs to t7/t9. Untouched: skills/**, VENDOR_LOCK.json, AGENTS.md, packages/mpd-verif-plugin/**, packages/mpd-bundle/cordis.patch.yml; the live tree's packages/mpd-agent-teams-plugin/_deps/ shows 0 changes (the vendor script was exercised only through the guard path in sandboxes)."
