evidence/wave2/t8-verification/20260911T061046Z/check3-t6-captain.raw.json:156:  "rendered": "Task t6 [in_progress] implementation — B8: make the ast-grep/codegraph MCP binaries resolvable in both install layouts\nAssignee: Deep Worker (attempt 2, attempt_id 4a4f14d4-afe8-473d-8088-76b1405d0a3f)\nDependencies: t1\nContract:\n  Objective: Make the ast-grep (and, if t1 scopes it here, codegraph) binaries resolvable in both install layouts, so the MCP tools work instead of returning BINARY_NOT_FOUND.\n  In scope: packages/mpd-bundle/cordis.patch.yml, packages/mpd-bootstrap-plugin/src, packages/mpd-bootstrap-plugin/dist/index.js, packages/mpd-codegraph-plugin/src, packages/mpd-codegraph-plugin/dist/index.js, docs, evidence/wave2/b8-binary-resolution\n  Out of scope: skills/**, VENDOR_LOCK.json, packages/mpd-agent-teams-plugin/**, packages/mpd-verif-plugin/src/regress.ts\n  Acceptance: The resolution mechanism decided in t1 is implemented exactly; any deviation is reported as a finding rather than taken silently, `__ast_grep` tools work end-to-end: a real `mcp__ast_grep__search` (or the equivalent MCP call path) returns a real result instead of BINARY_NOT_FOUND, demonstrated in a boot whose process cwd differs from the session workspace, The codegraph path is fixed to the same standard if t1 scoped it here: the boot log no longer reports `[mpd-codegraph] init status=no-binary`, and a real codegraph call or probe succeeds, Both install layouts are addressed as t1 required: state explicitly whether the mechanism works for a packed install, and if it cannot be tested here, say so rather than implying it was, The change is proven by a MOUNTING boot (isolated DSH_HOME + sandbox HOME) with 0 apply-crash signatures, plus the preset-conformance case still reporting ok:true with its negative control — a patch/preset row change cannot be validated by `--dump-config` alone, `node scripts/verify-vendor.mjs` still exits 0 and no file under skills/** was modified by this task\n  Verif