lts and commandsRun per criterion), and in the output declare the authorized DECLARED-BUT-UNMATCHED paths (the two launchers, the shared resolver + its test, `scripts/pack-mpd.mjs`, and the three README pairs) plus the two cross-referenced findings you already reported: the `devPatch()` `baseUrl + \"/node_modules/\"` operand defect in `preset-register.mjs`, and the bundle-lifecycle sandbox's `init status=fail binary=<resolved>` observation. Do not start new work — t12 (R1-F1) is separately queued for you and I will leave it in place.\nCompletion payload so far:\n  acceptanceResults: [{\"criterion\":\"The resolution mechanism decided in t1 is implemented exactly; any deviation is reported as a finding rather than taken silently\",\"status\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"RESULT.json .mechanism: the patch names NO binary path (grep for the two env keys in cordis.patch.yml is empty); each MCP row launches <pkg>/launch.mjs, which resolves through packages/mpd-mcp-shared/bin-resolve.mjs with t1 §3.2 precedence (caller env pin -> $MPD_AST_GREP_BIN_DIR -> createRequire of the optionalDependency -> <bundle>/.toolchain/node_modules/.bin/{ast-grep,sg}|codegraph -> env left unset) and the mandatory acceptance probe (existsSync + --version containing 'ast-grep', ast-grep before sg at every tier). The codegraph require tier reads the package's own `bin` entry (1.5.0 ships `bin: {codegraph: npm-shim.js}`) — recorded. Deviations recorded as findings: (F-devflavor-mcp-rewrite) the dev-flavor rewrite must drop the baseUrl operand, and (F-codegraph-init-fail-in-sandbox) an unrelated sandbox init failure.\"},{\"criterion\":\"`__ast_grep` tools work end-to-end: a real `mcp__ast_grep__search` (or the equivalent MCP call path) returns a real result instead of BINARY_NOT_FOUND, demonstrated in a boot whose process cwd differs from the session workspace\",\"status\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"mcp-gate.result.json (5/5, exit 0): the SHIPPED packages/mpd-mcp-astgrep/launch.mjs is driven as a real 