evidence/wave3/registry-redesign/t1-decision-record.txt:8:Verification (in-memory simulation of the rule on the real files, all three strip scenarios): strip BOTH -> quality-gates.js 1070/1070 and tools.js 2386/2386 byte-identical; strip quality-gates.js only -> both identical; strip tools.js only -> both identical. Measured windows: task-contract after[k=2]=["    ctx.tools.register(defineTool({","        name: 'agent_teams_status',"], before[k=4]=["                delivered,","            };","        },","    }));"]; every other region needs k<=3.
evidence/wave3/registry-redesign/t1-decision-record.txt:11:ACCEPTANCE BAR for t2 (state both numbers): check4f tools.js strip-heal goes from 60 diff lines / task-contract at 1970 vs canonical 1733 to 0 diff lines / byte-identical; check4e quality-gates.js stays 0 diff lines / byte-identical. Re-run the two recorded drivers UNCHANGED — evidence/wave2/t8-verification/20260911T061046Z/attempt3/drivers/check4e-heal-fidelity.sh and check4f-tools-heal-fidelity.sh — and add the combined strip-both scenario (my simulation shows 0 for both files). Keep the F3/F4 refusal tests and the 90/0 plugin suite green.
evidence/wave3/registry-redesign/t1-decision-record.txt:14:Use `line.trim() === beginLine(id)` / `=== endLine(id)` for the begin search, the end search AND validateHealedFile's occurrence count — the exact spelling writeRegistry already uses for the end line, so reader and emitter become one rule. Exhaustively verified colliding pairs (exactly 3, no others): scope-overlap ⊂ scope-overlap-normalize (quality-gates.js:244/263), repair-scope ⊂ repair-scope-fields (:714/:730), task-contract ⊂ task-contract-render (tools.js:1733/2259). Today the loose `.includes` search resolves correctly only by file order (each outer's own end precedes its child's); two hazards follow: (i) outer begin marker missing -> the guard prints a MISDIAGNOSIS `half-open marker pair (begin@-1, end@N)` and refuses to heal a merely-missing region (measured in-memory by dropping each outer begin line: identical result for all three pairs); (ii) outer's own end line removed -> the end search resolves to the CHILD's end line, producing a bogus span and a false "delta ... no longer matches the registered block". Required behavior: begin absent + end present = a partially stripped/MISSING region — in --check FAIL naming the line, in --write heal from context and drop the single orphan end-marker line, then re-validate; the `half-open` wording is reserved for a genuinely inverted pair (both markers present, end < begin). Fixtures: ONE per colliding pair, each with (1) child's end line before the parent's own end, (2) parent's begin marker removed (dangling end), (3) intact control asserting the resolved span equals the grep line numbers.
evidence/wave3/registry-redesign/t1-decision-record.txt:22:Do NOT patch dist/mpd-mcp-codegraph/dist/serve.js. Fix in packages/mpd-mcp-codegraph/launch.mjs: try runCodegraphServe(); on throw, write the error to STDERR (never stdout), set process.env.MPD_CODEGRAPH_BIN to a path-looking sentinel that does not exist, and call runCodegraphServe() once more. The adopted code then takes `source:"env"` in resolveCodegraphCommand, and provisionMissingCodegraph returns null at its FIRST guard (source === "env") -> runUnavailableMcp(CODEGRAPH_SKIP_HINT) -> the child stays alive, answers initialize/tools/list with zero tools and tools/call with the skip reason, exit 0. Source-verified: runCodegraphServe reads `options.env ?? processEnv` per call (the second call sees the sentinel); the throw is inside acquireLock's `mkdir(join(lockPath,".."))` reached from ensureCodegraphProvisioned, whose try/catch starts AFTER acquireLock, so it escapes to the launcher; the throw precedes all stdout/stdin wiring, so the retry cannot double-write.
evidence/wave3/registry-redesign/t1-decision-record.txt:23:Justification against the marker+re-apply rule: serve.js is a SHA-pinned PREBUILT (VENDOR_LOCK.assets["packages/mpd-mcp-codegraph/dist/serve.js"].sha256, enforced as a BLOCKING gate by scripts/verify-vendor.mjs:96-99). A marked delta inside it would either fail that gate or force a re-pin to our own bytes — turning a provenance gate into a self-attestation — and would require wiring a third file into the delta registry (a re-apply path into a regenerated bundle whose anchors cannot survive). The marker rule exists for adopted MAIN CODE (lib/**, not sha-pinned); the launcher is already the B8-introduced adaptation point for this package and already owns the "never throw, never write to stdout" contract. It also avoids duplicating the MCP-unavailable stub, which is NOT exported (serve.js exports only resolveServeProcessInvocation, runCodegraphServe, runCodegraphServeCli). t4 acceptance: with HOME read-only and no resolvable codegraph, the launcher answers initialize/tools/list and exits 0, stderr carries the original error + skip hint, and the mcp-call log shows 0 uncaught-ENOENT signatures; a writable-HOME control still resolves/provisions normally.
evidence/wave3/registry-redesign/t1-decision-record.txt:27:VENDOR_LOCK.assets.skills is ONE asset (fileCount 366 + treeSha 5b13e92091e38ed8a001c08b11cd8fc73f650041260ad7fc519c782ab6a6ef45) and scripts/verify-vendor.mjs recomputes that whole-tree fingerprint as a blocking gate (:100-108). All four group-C sites are under skills/** (skills/dsh-qa/scripts/preset-register.mjs devPatch + its mcpEnv pins at :43-45, skills/dsh-qa/scripts/rtl-verif.mjs duplicate devPatch, skills/dsh-qa/scripts/codegraph-smoke.mjs:36 doc gap) plus the SKILL.md case-table row — so any one edit invalidates the same treeSha and they must ride in ONE task (t3) with ONE re-pin in the same commit. Reuse the wave-2 re-pin pattern (evidence/wave2/t11-integration/20260911T072333Z/repin-skills.mjs).
evidence/wave3/registry-redesign/t7-review-output.txt:3:VERIFIED CORRECT: (1) DECISIVE registry exactness — I stripped ALL 12 regions from BOTH adopted files in one state; one --write healed both byte-identically, --check exit 0; t5's 3-round driver agrees → the wave-2 failure class is closed. (2) F3 durability OBSERVED — my re-materialize fixture refuses with exit 1 naming delta + symbol + line 977 and an unchanged file sha; t5's vendor leg agrees with a green control. (3) update_task diagnostics — omitted attempt_id → `attempt_id is required … agent_teams_claim_task` (never stale/stop), present-but-mismatched keeps stale wording, omitted status rejected as required; the oversized-drop boundary is evidenced (byte-identical provider stream, key-lossless parse, installed-harness 16,241-byte assembly + max-token drop). (4) Rules & hygiene clean: one VENDOR_LOCK skills re-pin, English-only agent text, EN+zh-CN pairs together, no chdir / no row-set DSH_WORKSPACE_ROOT, no secrets in evidence. Every t2 acceptance criterion traced to a named raw artifact.
