evidence/workmate/rename-delete-integration/2026-09-10T14-40-00Z/team-task-records.json:4:  "description": "Add rename + delete to the workmate system (mpd-workmate-plugin) and fix the read-only deny-list defect that blocks every read-only spawn. Rebuilt team: the previous team's scheduler stalled and its Explorer attempt died with the API, so this is a fresh scheduler with the same DAG. The binding interface document is preserved at .mpd/plans/workmate-rename-delete-contract.md and must be read by every member. Five user decisions are already agreed (archive-first delete with explicit purge; refuse mutations while the workmate is in use with a full library-owned cascade; the read-only deny defect in scope; agent tools + web routes + Workmates sidebar tab in zh/en; ASCII-only naming). Binding gates: bun test packages, bun run typecheck, bun run test:qa, node scripts/verify-vendor.mjs, and an isolated-DSH_HOME boot check, with evidence on disk and bilingual docs.",
evidence/workmate/rename-delete-integration/2026-09-10T14-40-00Z/team-task-records.json:8:    "protocol": "Read-only members (Architect, Researcher, Planner, Explorer, Plan Reviewer, Vision Analyst) take requirements/review/analysis tasks only and never edit files. Workers (Senior Engineer, Junior Engineer, Deep Worker, Lead, Reviewer) take implementation/verification/integration. The captain leads, designs the DAG, and integrates results. Workmate reuse: before delegating a role task, consult mpd_workmate_list / mpd_workmate_match(task); if a workmate note matches well, delegate to that workmate (member name = workmate name, so its persona/memory are injected), otherwise initialize a fresh workmate with mpd_workmate_init — never force a weak note match.",
