evidence/workmate/rename-delete-integration/2026-09-10T14-40-00Z/team-task-records.json:300:      "description": "The user asked for a genuine traversal of this project (\"遍历工程，了解工程详细信息\"), so this task delivers the whole-project picture with the workmate system located inside it. A previous attempt at this task died with ZERO output; that failure mode is the single most important thing to avoid here.\n\nHARD DELIVERY RULES:\n- Target roughly 150-200 lines of dense structured text in your task output. No pasted source, no per-package essays.\n- If you cannot finish everything, STOP and deliver what you have with an explicit trailing line \"PARTIAL — not covered: <sections>\". A labelled partial is strictly better than a silent death.\n- Never end your turn with this task claimed and no output. Complete it, or fail it with the concrete blocker.\n\nDO NOT re-derive the workmate internals in depth — .mpd/plans/workmate-rename-delete-contract.md already pins sanitizeName, the wmDir(\"\") hazard, the index.json writer-with-no-reader, the tool/route surface, the in-use gate and the deny-list correction. Reference it; your value is breadth and coupling.\n\nDeliver five sections:\n1. Whole-repo map: every package under packages/ with what it ACTUALLY does (from its src/index.ts + README, not its name), plus presets/, skills/, scripts/, tests/, evidence/ and the .mpd state roots. One line each.\n2. Where the workmate system sits: the package, library root, state files and caps, tools, routes, GUI tab — and then every OTHER surface referencing workmate (bundle patch rows, presets, the agent-teams member binding, QA scripts asserting its route literals, every doc mentioning it), each with file:line.\n3. Coupling + stale-surface map: where a workmate NAME is load-bearing (directory key, index.json key, team-member binding by name equality, note self-reference), which cross-plugin assumptions must stay byte-identical (sanitizeName vs members.js#workmateKey), and exactly which surfaces go stale on rename or delete.\n4. Execution + gates: how the bundle installs, how QA isolates DSH_HOME/HOME, what each AGENTS.md §4 gate really runs, and the evidence-on-disk convention.\n5. Contradictions: anywhere the docs and the real code disagree.\n\nAlready verified by the captain so you need not re-check: HEAD is f697088 and the tree is dirty by design (33 uncommitted entries from a previous session — do not report them as this team's changes, and never revert them); the real workmate library holds exactly one instance, \"oracle-1\"; .mpd/team/ holds six stale non-archived team records plus an archive/ dir.",
evidence/workmate/rename-delete-integration/2026-09-10T14-40-00Z/team-task-records.json:323:      "output": "# t2 DOSSIER — the workmate system in full bundle context (Researcher, read-only)\n\nBaseline: HEAD f697088, `git status --porcelain` = 33 entries (unchanged by me; I edited nothing).\nContract revision read: `.mpd/plans/workmate-rename-delete-contract.md` grew 146→248 lines WHILE this task ran\n(mtime 08:41Z); everything below is consistent with the LATEST revision (§A–§L, incl. A2 deny parity, A3\ndirectory-key, A4 renamedFrom, A6 seven teams, A7 artifact/i18n).\nBaseline tests (measured): `bun test packages/mpd-workmate-plugin packages/mpd-roles-plugin\npackages/mpd-bundle-plugin/test/sidebar-tab.test.mjs` → 21 pass / 0 fail.\n\n## 1. LIVE-HARNESS EVIDENCE (measured in this session, not inferred)\n1.1 Defect reproduced INDEPENDENTLY at BOTH call sites, same error:\n  - `mpd_role_spawn {role:\"librarian\"}` → `tools.restrict() names unknown global tools\n    \"str_replace_editor\", \"apply_patch\"; known global tools: …`\n  - `mpd_workmate_spawn {name:\"oracle-1\"}` → byte-identical error (workmate plugin, live real-HOME instance).\n  Both abort BEFORE a child is created (no token cost), so §G is confirmed and the failure is total.\n1.2 Harness source of truth: `/root/.nvm/.../@deepseek-ai/dsh/node_modules/@deepseek-ai/dsh-tools/lib/index.js:2802-2804`\n  (`restrict()` throws when any name is not in `this.view(scope).restrictableNames`);\n  `restrictableNames` is built at lib/index.js:2863-2881 = globals + INHERITED parent layers, and it\n  EXCLUDES scope-local (own-scope) tools — so a scope-registered tool name would also throw. Same file mirrored in\n  `packages/mpd-agent-teams-plugin/_deps/dsh-tools/lib/index.js:2792`.\n1.3 Full live registry captured (104 names). Every name in §L A2 is present:\n  `write`✓ `edit`✓ `mpd_hashline_edit`✓ `bash`✓ `mcp__ast_grep__rewrite`✓ `mcp__ast_grep__scan`✓ `mcp__lsp__rename`✓;\n  `str_replace_editor`/`apply_patch` absent. ⇒ the 7-name list is spawn-safe by NAME in this profile.\n1.4 Extra write-capable tools in the live registry, NOT covered by any static list: `mcp__nowledge_mem__mem_fs`\n  (has write/rm), `mcp__nowledge_mem__memory_add|memory_update|memory_evolves_revise|resolve_timeline_review|\n  trigger_memory_catchup|report_skill_outcome`, `mcp__lsp__install_decision`; plus indirect writers\n  `subagent|subagent_fork|workflow|ssh_exec|ssh_upload|mpd_memory_write|mpd_boulder_*`. These come from the user\n  HOME config (not the bundle), so they are profile-optional and CANNOT be added statically without breaking\n  profiles that lack them — residual risk, document, do not \"fix\" (§G's forbidden-fix rule already covers the shape).\n  Consequence for tests: assert the DENY LIST CONTENT, never that the registry equals a fixed set (a QA sandbox\n  will NOT have the `nowledge_mem` rows).\n1.5 Library state now: `mpd_workmate_list` → exactly 1 instance `oracle-1 [Architect readonly] uses=0`; on disk\n  `~/.mpd/workmate/{index.json, oracle-1/{meta.json,persona.md,memory.md,note.md}}`. Per key uniqueness, the live\n  happy path for tests is `oracle-1` → `oracle-2` (A6(i)) since `oracle-1` already exists only in the REAL home —\n  a sandbox HOME starts empty, so each case must `mpd_workmate_init` first.\n1.6 Team state now = SEVEN non-archived records (A6 confirmed): `agent-teams-sidebar-migration`, `mpd-default`,\n  `mpd-default-53380813`, `mpd-default-84e50f06`, `mpd-default-c146a414`, `mpd-default-c2be0a8a`,\n  `workmate-rename-delete` — each with all 11 roster names. `.mpd/team/archive/` holds 5 archived teams (a\n  `<id>/team.json` ONE LEVEL DOWN → the direct-children scan skips them); `.mpd/team/retired-members.json` is a\n  FILE → also skipped. Blocked keys are therefore exactly the 11 in A6.\n  CRITICAL for t6: QA boots with `HOME=<sandbox>` but cwd = the repo, so the gate reads the REAL `.mpd/team` →\n  sandbox cases must ALSO avoid roster member names, and the in-use case is free via rename→`architect`.\n1.7 `mpd_config_get team.stateDir` → **null** in this workspace (no `.mpd/mpd.jsonc`). ⇒ the gate must use the\n  literal `<cwd>/.mpd/team`, not a config lookup. Source of truth for that path: bundle patch\n  `packages/mpd-bundle/cordis.patch.yml` (`agent-teams.config.stateDir: .mdp/team` → line ~202) and\n  `packages/mpd-agent-teams-plugin/lib/index.js:261-262, 336-337` (`join(captain.session.header.cwd ?? process.cwd(), stateDir)`).\n1.8 Filesystem semantics MEASURED on this host (probe in a temp dir, removed after):\n  - `renameSync(dir → existing EMPTY dir)` **SUCCEEDS silently** (source dir gone, target now holds the source\n    content) — §J's hazard, confirmed;\n  - non-empty dir target → `ENOTEMPTY`; regular-file target → `ENOTDIR`;\n  - `existsSync(danglingSymlink)` = **false** while `lstatSync` sees it present (rename then throws `ENOTDIR`).\n  ⇒ the collision guard must `lstatSync` the target and treat ANY hit (dir / empty dir / file / symlink /\n  dangling symlink) as the contract's 409 `collision`, so no raw fs error escapes as a non-standard error body.\n\n## 2. CODE MAP (live files only — see §Re stale copies)\n`packages/mpd-workmate-plugin/src/index.ts` (439 lines; the whole feature):\n  caps L25-28 `PERSONA_CAP/MEMORY_CAP/NOTE_CAP/MATCH_THRESHOLD`; `READONLY_DENY` **L30** (the workmate array t3 owns);\n  `homeDir` L52, `workmateRoot` L54, `wmDir` **L55** (`wmDir(\"\")` → LIBRARY ROOT — guard at the tool head);\n  `sanitizeName` L58-65; `capText` L68-73; `Meta` L75-79; `readMeta` **L81-87** (fixed-shape whitelist — drops\n  `renamedFrom` today, A4); `writeJson` L89-92; `indexPath` L94; `readIndex` L96-102; `writeIndexEntry` **L104-108**\n  (only SETS the key — must drop the old key); `readNote` L110-112; `readMemory` L114-120; `readPersona` L122-124;\n  `autoNote` **L129-136** (writes `<baseName>-based workmate \"<name>\".`; `prev.startsWith(prefix)` dedupe — A5);\n  `appendMemory` L139-156; `mergePersona` L159-165; `ensureInstance` **L167-172** (A3: must also return `key`);\n  `listInstances` **L174-184** (returns `meta.name`, not the dir name; filters on `<dir>/meta.json` — so a\n  half-created dir and `.archive/` are invisible); `scoreMatch` L186-202; `apply` L204; `rolesService` L211-213\n  (lazy `ctx.get(\"mpdRoles\")`); `resolveBase` L215-225; `initWorkmate` L227-246 (writes meta/persona/memory/note\n  then index L238-244); `workmateLibrary` **L248-259** + `ctx.provide(\"mpdWorkmate\")` L260; tools: list L262-271,\n  init L273-279, spawn L281-314 (`dsh.spawnAgent` L300-310, readonly `toolFilter` **L309**), reflect L316-338\n  (writes wmDir(meta.name) L326-334), match L340-357; web surface L359-438 (`webRegistered` L363,\n  `registerWebSurface` L364-432 with list L369-377, roster L380-396, get L398-412, init L413-431; called L433;\n  `ctx.on(\"internal/service\", …)` L434-438).\n  Path-through-`meta.name` sites beyond ensureInstance (all in A3 scope): L181, L251, L256, L290-292, L326-334, L349.\n`packages/mpd-workmate-plugin/dist/index.js` — the file the PATCH LOADS (patch row 174); rebuild in the same change\n  (`bun build src/index.ts --target node --format esm --outfile dist/index.js`); dist currently mirrors src (L215 deny).\n`packages/mpd-bundle-plugin/src/web-client.js` (421 lines; t4 owns): routes L123-126; locale ns L127;\n  `SIDEBAR_TAB_ID=\"mpd-workmate\"` L131 + title L135 (K deferral); zh L139-166 / en L167-194 (24 keys each, no parity\n  test exists); `interpolate/translateFor` L196-203; **`request()` L205-217** (collapses non-OK to `Error(body.error)`\n  — drops status/reason/blocking); styles L224-230; `WorkmateLibraryView` L233-359 (state L235-244, `refresh` L246-254\n  — list+roster, `openDetail` L256-262, `submit` L263-272, filter L274-278, detail branch L280-309, list L311-338,\n  init form L339-357); `registerWorkmateSidebarTab` L368-384 (order 90, `single: true`, component L377);\n  `loadTeamPage` L390-401; `apply` L403-414; `module.exports` L419 (exports `inject, apply, WorkmateLibraryView,\n  SIDEBAR_TAB_ID` — zh/en are NOT exported, see 3.2).\n`packages/mpd-bundle-plugin/client.js` — COMMITTED combined artifact (built by `scripts/build-mpd-client.mjs`;\n  browser + offline harness both load THIS file). Must be regenerated.\n`packages/mpd-agent-teams-plugin/lib/members.js` — **DO NOT EDIT** (adopted main code, refreshable by\n  `scripts/vendor-agent-teams.mjs`): `workmateKey` L45-50 (byte-identical twin of `sanitizeName` — keep in sync),\n  `homeDir` L56-58, `workmateBacking` L64-82, caps L26-27, injection L372-408, reflect instruction L84-86.\n`packages/mpd-roles-plugin/src/index.ts` — `READONLY_DENY` L23-33, used L123 (t5 owns; `dist/index.js` rebuild too).\nBundle rows (`packages/mpd-bundle/cordis.patch.yml`): mpd-roles 148-149, **mpd-workmate 173-174**, mpd-web-compat 128,\n  agent-teams 200+ (`stateDir: .mdp/team`, sessionTeamPolicy, `profiles.mpd` with the 11 names).\nPreset guidance the docs mirror: `presets/mpd/agent.cordis.yml` L99-110 (WORKMATE LIBRARY block).\n\n## 3. TEST / BUILD / QA WIRING\n3.1 `packages/mpd-workmate-plugin/test/workmate.test.ts` (167 lines, sandbox HOME via `process.env.HOME=tmpdir`);\n  readonly assertion L155 `expect(spawned[1].toolFilter).toEqual({deny: expect.arrayContaining([\"write\",\"edit\"])})`\n  survives a 7-name list. `packages/mpd-roles-plugin/test/roles.test.ts:105-112` PINS the 9 old names (rewrite per A1/A2).\n3.2 Offline client harness `packages/mpd-bundle-plugin/test/client-harness.mjs`: `loadBundleClient` L10-22 reads the\n  COMMITTED `client.js`; `ctx` stub L274-295; **`fetchImpl` L327-332 returns `{ok:true,status:200,body}` for a URL\n  present in `responses`, else 404 `{error:\"not found\"}`** → there is NO way to express 409/400-with-reason today,\n  so t4's negative-path tests need the stub extended (e.g. accept `{status, body}` descriptors); and\n  `ctx.locale.register: (ns) => …` L294 DISCARDS the `{zh,en}` dicts, so the A7 key-parity assertion needs the 2nd\n  argument captured (or the dicts exported from web-client.js).\n3.3 QA (`test:qa` = every `skills/dsh-qa/scripts/*.mjs --self-test`): `workmate-library.mjs` self-test L30-66 asserts\n  the patch row, `memberPersona` injection, the host `roster`/`get` route STRINGS, `SIDEBAR_TAB_ID`, `ctx.inject`\n  awaiting and the no-floater rule (L60-63) — new routes/TODO must not break those literals; real flow L94-117.\n  `web-client-adapt.mjs:77` asserts `path: \"/plugins/mpd-workmate/list\"`+`init`+`internal/service`, real fetches\n  :104/:182; `bundle-lifecycle.mjs:127` fetches `/plugins/mpd-workmate/list` on a real boot; SKILL.md case table\n  rows 46-48. Evidence convention `evidence/<domain>/<slug>/<timestamp>/{result.json,output.log}` (SKILL.md §3);\n  existing workmate evidence `evidence/plan-f/workmate-library/2026-08-28T09-33-38.409Z/`.\n3.4 `VENDOR_LOCK.json` locks ONLY upstream assets (`skills`, `packages/mpd-agent-teams-plugin/_deps`,\n  `mpd-mcp-{astgrep,gitbash,lsp,codegraph}/dist/*`) — `client.js`/`dist/index.js` are NOT fingerprinted, so\n  `verify-vendor` is unaffected by the rebuilds (but the four MCP dist files must not be touched).\n3.5 `scripts/pack-mpd.mjs` PLUGIN_PKGS L21-28 includes mpd-workmate-plugin (+ mpd-bundle-plugin) and FAILS without a\n  dist; `dist/mpd-package/` is gitignored (release step only).\n3.6 **Stale copies — never edit:** `.qa-reloc/**` and `dist/mpd-package/**` (both gitignored) and the TRACKED\n  `evidence/scan/t3-20260829/build/mpd-workmate-plugin.js` (an old esbuild bundle; `ctx.provide(\"mpdWorkmate\")` at\n  :236). Greps for workmate symbols hit them; live code is `src/index.ts` + `dist/index.js` and `web-client.js` +\n  `client.js` only.\n\n## 4. DOC SURFACES t10 MUST TOUCH (each with its `*.zh-CN.md` twin + language-switch link)\n`packages/mpd-workmate-plugin/README.md` (layout L22-30, tools table L38-44, service L46) + zh;\n`docs/architecture.md` L107 (row), L122-139 (roster→workmate→team), L243-256 (sidebar + routes) + zh;\n`docs/user-guide.md` L104-124 (tools table), L147-151, L172-182 (sidebar tab + route list), L204 + zh;\n`docs/development.md` L68, L88-90 (QA case table) + zh; `docs/feature-audit.md` L16 + zh;\n`README.md` L74-90 + `README.zh-CN.md` L65-76; `packages/mpd-bundle-plugin/README.md` + zh;\n`AGENTS.md` (English-only) L127-130, L220-221, L343/L346/L350 troubleshooting, L369-373 glossary;\n`docs/index.md` L16 only mentions the hub row (likely unchanged).\n\n## 5. CONTRACT GAPS I COULD NOT CLOSE (recommendations, not findings to raise as review blockers)\n(a) §H \"readonly instance as the target of a mutation\" has NO decided outcome in §A–§L. Recommend ALLOW (readonly\n    governs the spawned child's tools; the library is user data) and pin it in a test; keep the readonly badge in\n    the GUI confirm step.\n(b) Same-key rename (`alice`→`alice`): §B says \"rejected, no side effect\" but §D has no reason code for it\n    (case-only rename already lands on 400 `invalid-name` via the raw===sanitize predicate). Pick one\n    (recommend 400 `invalid-name`) and test it.\n(c) Half-created dir without `meta.json`: invisible to `list` (L178) and `get/read`→null (L250-258). Decide\n    rename/delete behaviour — recommend 404 `unknown` with NO filesystem mutation.\n(d) Spawned child's reflect after a rename: the spawn prompt hardcodes the key (L293-299) and reflect resolves by\n    name (L322) → the child's reflect fails \"no workmate named X\". §F's `renamedFrom` could resolve legacy keys;\n    decide (recommend: keep the deterministic failure, document it) since the §E gate only covers in-process races.\n(e) Collision guard must be lstat-based (see 1.8) — a raw `ENOTDIR`/`ENOTEMPTY` escaping as a non-§D body would be\n    a contract violation; a dangling-symlink target is invisible to `existsSync`.\n(f) `~/.mpd/workmate/.archive` is currently invisible to `listInstances` (no `meta.json` at that level) so archiving\n    cannot pollute `list`/`match` — keep the archived instance's `meta.json` one level deeper, never at the root.\n    `.archive` as a NAME is already rejected by the D5 predicate (`sanitizeName(\".archive\")=\"archive\"`), while a\n    workmate literally named `archive` is creatable and does NOT collide with `.archive` on a case-sensitive fs.\n(g) §E(b) residual: the scan sees only THIS workspace's teams while the library is cross-project, and a second dsh\n    process on the same HOME is invisible to the in-process map — already listed in §L's residuals; the refusal\n    message should therefore name the team+member (A6) so a user can act.\n\nMethod: `read` on every live file cited, targeted greps, one live reproduction per call site, one filesystem probe in\na temp dir (removed). No file in the repo was created, modified or deleted by this task."
