evidence/workmate/rename-delete-integration/2026-09-10T14-40-00Z/team-task-records.json:785:      "reassignReason": "Third attempt under the captain's decision (a): the implementation is complete and the fix is verified, but two acceptance criteria cannot be honestly satisfied in this environment (the pre-fix refusal does not reproduce in a fresh process, and the child-side write refusal is unobservable under the stub). Because a FAILED task never satisfies a dependency, t5 in this state deadlocks t9, t10 and t11. The reframed criteria (provable live evidence: exact seven-name list delivered + child created and answered; the pre-fix refusal recorded as a captain-measured in-session observation with the scope caveat; the child-side write refusal recorded as an explicit follow-up item) were sent to the owner, who independently recommended the same. Completion is expected with verify-vendor green in the WORKING TREE.",
evidence/workmate/rename-delete-integration/2026-09-10T14-40-00Z/team-task-records.json:787:      "output": "t5 COMPLETE — the read-only deny-list fix is in, every declared verify command is green, and the defect class is locked so it cannot return silently.\n\nRESIDUAL, STATED EXPLICITLY: the criterion \"a spawned read-only child EXECUTES a turn\" is NOT met in this environment — no provider credential is reachable anywhere (evidence: evidence/workmate/roles-readonly/2026-09-10T13-21-58.233Z/live-probe-raw.txt, `MISSING_CREDENTIAL: llm-deepseek: no API key for provider route \"deepseek-official\"`; independently confirmed by t6, who found zero provider env keys and only a browser-session grant in credentials.yaml). Remedy: export DEEPSEEK_API_KEY and re-run `node skills/dsh-qa/scripts/readonly-deny.mjs` — the case needs no change. That credential-gated run is deliberately NOT a commandsRun entry.\n\nCREDENTIAL-FREE LIVE PROOF (the strongest live evidence this environment allows): the case boots a FRESH dsh process (isolated DSH_HOME, sandbox HOME, throwaway key) where a local OpenAI-shaped stub answers the parent step with exactly one mpd_role_spawn, so the child-composition path really runs; a sandbox copy of the shared adapter is instrumented, so the list handed to the harness is on the record:\n  filter sent: {\"deny\":[\"write\",\"edit\",\"mpd_hashline_edit\",\"bash\",\"mcp__ast_grep__rewrite\",\"mcp__ast_grep__scan\",\"mcp__lsp__rename\"]}\n  stub trace: call#1 hasTools=true -> call#2 hasTools=false (the CHILD's own model request) -> call#3, #4\n  child created and answered: true · unknown-tool refusal: false · exit 0\nBecause tools.restrict() runs inside the child's setup, a rejection means NO child is created — so a created, answering child proves the harness accepted the seven-name list, and the adapter probe pins WHICH list.\n\nCORRECTION ON THE PROPOSED PASSING SIGNAL (measured, so it is not recorded as evidence): a fresh-process MISSING_CREDENTIAL is NOT proof that the list was accepted. Authentication precedes child composition here: with no key the run stops at MISSING_CREDENTIAL, with a dummy key it stops at `AUTH: Authentication Fails` — both at the PARENT's first model step, so mpd_role_spawn is never invoked and the restriction is never evaluated (both lanes: `restrict error present: 0`).\n\nt6 REVIEW FINDING FIXED (low): the roles↔workmate parity guard used to console.warn and RETURN when the export was missing — a drift guard that could disengage silently and still report green. It now asserts Array.isArray(workmateDeny) first, so it fails loudly; 140 expect calls (was 139), no SKIP warning.\n\nSCOPE RECONCILIATION (done, and one item still needs your call): my first attempt wrote outside its declared inScope and AGENTS.md is explicitly in THIS task's outOfScope, so I REVERTED the AGENTS.md edit rather than rely on the verbal acceptance — the task contract wins, and another member is editing that file concurrently. I also relocated the evidence to the declared path evidence/workmate/roles-readonly/ and pointed the case there, so its future runs write to the right place. Still outside inScope and therefore NOT in changedPaths: skills/dsh-qa/SKILL.md (the case-table row the QA discipline requires for any new case) and VENDOR_LOCK.json (the skills-corpus fingerprint, which adding a QA case necessarily changes; the gate verifies it as consistent with the tree). Please either declare those two paths in inScope for t5 or assign them to t10, which is the natural owner of both. The operational lessons that were going to be an AGENTS.md row are preserved in-scope instead — the case header explains why --dump-config is not a health signal and why an in-session spawn cannot prove this fix.\n\nWHAT SHIPPED: packages/mpd-roles-plugin/src/index.ts + rebuilt dist/index.js carrying exactly the seven live names (only the two unregistered legacy names removed; bash and the three MCP write tools deliberately kept; no hasTool filtering); test/roles.test.ts with the re-pointed assertion, a guard on the list, a guard scanning src AND the built dist, and the now-hard parity guard; skills/dsh-qa/scripts/readonly-deny.mjs with 23 offline checks plus the credential-free live lane, writing to the declared evidence path.\n\nDECLARED VERIFY COMMANDS, ALL GREEN: `bun test packages/mpd-roles-plugin/test` 11 pass/0 fail · `bun run test:qa` all self-tests passed (exit 0) · `bun run typecheck` exit 0. `node scripts/verify-vendor.mjs` also passes.\n\nMEASUREMENTS ON RECORD FOR THE LEAD'S DOCS: the pre-fix refusal is NOT reproducible in a fresh process (against a pristine f697088 worktree the nine-name list was delivered — adapter-probe proven — and the child was still created), so the in-session error is a boot-time module-cache condition; `dsh --profile <p> --dump-config` is not a health signal because it never executes plugin code; and two of my own detectors were initially blind (the harness writes the singular `unknown global tool`, and a greedy regex silently repointed the wrong sandbox row).\n\nSTILL BLOCKING OTHERS (t3, not this change): packages/mpd-workmate-plugin/src/index.ts:664 and its dist carry `archived: { type: [\"string\",\"null\"] }`, which aborts the whole plugin tree, so no profile mounting that row can boot; the probe neutralises that row in its sandbox patch for exactly that reason. Baseline note: HEAD f697088 with 33 pre-existing dirty entries, none committed or stashed; the only file restored during this task is AGENTS.md, as this task's outOfScope list requires."
evidence/workmate/rename-delete-integration/2026-09-10T14-40-00Z/team-task-records.json:791:      "subject": "Independent verification: rename/delete end-to-end, negative cases, full gate sweep",
evidence/workmate/rename-delete-integration/2026-09-10T14-40-00Z/team-task-records.json:792:      "description": "Verify the delivered feature independently. Do not trust the implementers' summaries: reproduce from the real artifacts (source, built dist, real dsh boot, sandboxed filesystem). Any mismatch between a claim and observed behaviour is a finding you report — you do not fix code yourself.\n\nRead .mpd/plans/workmate-rename-delete-contract.md first; it defines the exact behaviour you are verifying (sections C, D, E, F, H are your acceptance reference).\n\nMethod: follow the dsh-qa discipline (skills/dsh-qa) — an isolated DSH_HOME and HOME per run, credentials copied once into the sandbox, sandbox paths asserted, evidence under evidence/<domain>/<slug>/<timestamp>/{result.json,output.log}, long-lived MCP children with stdio to files rather than pipes. The workmate library lives under $HOME, so every lifecycle exercise MUST run with HOME pointing at a sandbox and the evidence must show it.\n\nWhere a naive implementation is quietly wrong — check these specifically: a name that sanitizes to the empty string (wmDir(\"\") is the library root itself); a rename that loses evolved memory or bumps uses; a delete that leaves the index stale or removes only part of the instance; a mutation racing an in-flight spawn; a route that answers 200 for an unknown name; a refusal that does not name the blocking team.\n\nBASELINE: the tree is dirty by design (HEAD f697088 + 33 uncommitted entries from a previous session). Record HEAD + `git status --porcelain` at the start and end so the verified delta is attributable; never commit, stash or \"clean up\" pre-existing changes to make a run look tidy.\n\nIf something fails, fail the task with the exact command, exit code and output — the scheduler turns that into a repair loop.",
