evidence/workmate/rename-delete-integration/2026-09-10T14-40-00Z/team-task-records.json:939:      "reassignReason": "Reopening the failed verification for a re-run on the repaired bytes: t6's blocker F1 (both new agent tools rejected by the harness output validator while the mutation still applied) is fixed on disk — the captain verified the built artifact now declares `ok` in BOTH output schemas (dist rebuilt 13:58:34, newer than src 13:50:45), and F2 (the vendor fingerprint) has been green since the t16 refresh (13:52:44, gate PASS, stability check empty). The assignee's own drivers reproduce the class in one pass, so a fresh attempt closes the loop.",
evidence/workmate/rename-delete-integration/2026-09-10T14-40-00Z/team-task-records.json:941:      "output": "t6 PASSES on the repaired bytes — attempt 1's two blockers are both cleared and every acceptance criterion was exercised.\n\nF1 FIXED AND RE-VERIFIED (three independent layers): (1) harness acceptance — FIX.rename-tool-output-accepted, FIX.delete-archive-tool-output-accepted, FIX.delete-purge-tool-output-accepted, FIX.no-invalid-output-error-anywhere and both value-shape checks PASS on the exact calls that used to be rejected; (2) tool layer 19/19 — tool.rename returns {ok:true,name:\"probe-2\",from:\"probe-1\",renamedFrom:[\"probe-1\"]} and purge returns {ok:true,name,archived:null,purged:true}; (3) routes/lifecycle 59/59 unchanged, success bodies still carry ok per section D.\n\nF2 WITHDRAWN: verify-vendor exit 0 / PASS on the refreshed lock (the attempt-1 red was the documented transient fingerprint lag, not a finding against the deny fix or this delivery).\n\nGATES: bun test 293 tests / 290 pass / 3 skip / 0 fail; typecheck exit 0; test:qa exit 0 (all self-tests); verify-vendor exit 0; isolated-DSH_HOME boot exit 0 with mpd-roles + mpd-workmate + mpd-hashline rows present.\n\nLIFECYCLE (real sandboxed web boot, 59/59): oracle-1 -> oracle-2 frees the old key and preserves persona/memory bytes, uses and createdAt; archive restorable from .archive/; purge removes; repeat delete 404; collision/orphan/symlink/same-key/root-guard all behave; in-use refusal names team AND member; no $HOME leaks in error bodies.\n\nREAD-ONLY FIX (own run on the final bytes, s1/): exit 0, restrictError false, missingCredential false, stubCalls 4, and the ENFORCEMENT lane proves the child's own requests see 81 tools vs the parent's 87 with childLeaksWriteCapable [] — none of the seven write-capable names reach the child. The re-injection control is silent in this profile (refusalSeen=false) and is recorded as non-reproducible, never as a pass.\n\nIsolation: real ~/.mpd/workmate byte-identical (sha ce635a4d…, 5 files); DSH_HOME/HOME under mktemp and asserted; HEAD f697088 + 65 porcelain entries before and after; my only delta is the untracked evidence directory attempt2-2026-09-10T13-59-50.000Z/ (result.json, results.json, findings.md, gate logs, driver logs, s1/). Residual per N3 unchanged: a spawned read-only child executing a MODEL turn needs a provider key and is not claimed."
evidence/workmate/rename-delete-integration/2026-09-10T14-40-00Z/team-task-records.json:946:      "description": "Adversarially review the core implementation (t3) on the axes where a mistake is expensive and hard to see. Read .mpd/plans/workmate-rename-delete-contract.md first, then the actual code in packages/mpd-workmate-plugin/src/index.ts, the tests and the evidence — treating the implementer's summary as a claim to be checked, not as fact.\n\nAttack in particular:\n- sanitizeName as the single key algorithm: can any input reach a filesystem call before validation? What happens for an empty sanitized name, a CJK name, a punctuation-only name, a case-only variant, and a name colliding after sanitization?\n- rename identity: is the evolved instance really moved rather than recreated, with persona/memory/note content, caps, uses, lastTask and createdAt preserved, and the note self-reference plus renamedFrom consistent with the new key?\n- delete: archive-first behaviour, hidden-from-list/match, restorability, purge + confirm semantics, index-key removal, all-or-nothing failure behaviour.\n- the in-use gate: does it actually close the spawn/reflect race, is the .mpd/team read implemented as read-only (never writing another plugin's state), is fail-open correct here, and is the refusal actionable (blocking team id + member)?\n- index.json: it has no reader today — judge whether the rename/delete handling leaves it consistent and whether the contract's treatment is defensible.\n- the workmate-side READONLY_DENY correction: does it follow contract section G exactly, and does it keep read-only authority intact?\n\nYou are a read-only role: report findings, do not edit files. A 'pass' verdict with an unverified criterion is worse than a 'needs_revision' with a real finding. Never end the turn with the task claimed and no output.",
evidence/workmate/rename-delete-integration/2026-09-10T14-40-00Z/team-task-records.json:961:        "The workmate-side READONLY_DENY correction is verified against the live registry claim in contract section G, including that read-only authority was not widened.",
evidence/workmate/rename-delete-integration/2026-09-10T14-40-00Z/team-task-records.json:974:      "output": "t7 REVIEW = PASS (0 blocker/high, 2 low findings, 1 documentation item). Reviewed the LATEST on-disk state of t3 (packages/mpd-workmate-plugin/src+dist+test, HEAD f697088, gates re-run by me at review end).\n\nMETHOD (independent, adversarial — not a re-read of the implementer's summary)\n1) Full contract read (354 lines, §A-O) including §G/A2/A3-A7/M1-M8/N1-N3/O1-O5.\n2) Line-by-line read of the shipped source (797 lines) and diff.\n3) Wrote and ran .mpd/team/workmate-rename-delete/probe-arch-t7-invariants.mjs: 49 adversarial assertions driving the SHIPPED dist module (not the test file) against a sandbox HOME + sandbox cwd — every row of §H plus the four invariants. Result: 49/49 pass (probe-result.json).\n4) Drove the harness's OWN validator (installed dsh-tools 0.1.2-rc.1) over the registered tool schemas: proves §N1's \"type arrays are not supported\" rule and that the nullable form `oneOf:[{type:\"string\"},{type:\"null\"}]` IS accepted, which makes the recommended low-fix safe.\n5) Instrumented the REAL ToolRuntime.register during a real profile boot (boot-probe-c.sh, isolated HOME/DSH_HOME): 94 registrations, all 7 workmate tools OK, mpd_workmate_delete registered with archived={type:\"string\"}.\n6) Re-ran all four binding gates on the current state.\n\nFOUR INVARIANTS — falsification attempts and outcomes\nI1 root safety / name predicate — PASS. `nameKey` rejects \"\"/\"Alice\"/\"架构师\"/\"!!!\"/\"..\"/\".archive\"/\"a/b\"/\"a b\"/\"-\"/\"ORACLE-1\" with reason invalid-name BEFORE any fs call; `wmDir(\"\")` throws, so the library root is unaddressable; the root survived all refusals.\nI2 identity-preserving rename — PASS. persona/memory bytes byte-identical, uses/lastTask/createdAt preserved, updatedAt advanced, meta.name=key, renamedFrom=[\"oracle-1\"] surviving a later reflect, old dir gone/new dir present, index old key dropped, note prefix rewritten, service get(old)=null / get(new)=full on the next call.\nI3 complete/all-or-nothing delete — PASS. archive dir inside .archive, bytes intact/restorable, index key dropped, other instances' bytes untouched, service list/get drop it, repeat delete=404 unknown, purge w/o confirm and with case-wrong confirm = confirm-required with the instance intact, purge removes dir+key.\nI4 deterministic races/gates — PASS. live team member blocks BOTH source and target (409 in-use) with blocking=[{teamId,member}]; ARCHIVED team does not block; blocked mutation leaves zero side effects; symlinked instance refused (404, not resolved); orphan dir refused (404, untouched); gate+collision+mutation share one synchronous block (no await); reflect is fully synchronous so it cannot interleave; throwing spawn releases the counter (finally), so no permanent block.\n\nNOTABLE — a real defect I caught mid-review, now fixed\nMy first probe (probe-arch-t7-schema.mjs) showed the dist module ABORTING the whole plugin tree: `JsonSchemaError: unsupported JSON schema: schema.properties.archived.type must be a single type string (type arrays are not supported)` at `mpd_workmate_delete`. The implementer was still finishing: src 20:55:53 / dist 20:56:12 / test 20:56:28 now carry `archived: {type:\"string\"}` + `archived: deleted.archived ?? \"\"`, and both the real-boot instrumentation and the current dist confirm the fix. Residual action for t6/t7-rerun: t3's OWN evidence (evidence/workmate/rename-delete-core/20260910T125201Z) was recorded BEFORE that fix, and its boot gate is only `dsh --profile w --dump-config`, which composes rows WITHOUT mounting them (measured: the later real boot log carries [mpd-dsh-adapter] and the workmate registrations, the dump run could never see a schema abort). So t6/t11 must re-run the gates on the current state — I did (all four green), but the on-disk t3 evidence should not be read as covering the current bytes. Verified no src→dist drift: a fresh `bun build` of src differs from the shipped dist ONLY in two banner comments (dist-drift.txt).\n\nFINDINGS (2 low, both resolved=false; neither blocks t6)\nL1 archived=\"\" vs null across surfaces. `mpd_workmate_delete` returns archived:\"\" on purge (tool def src/index.ts:670+673) while the §D HTTP body and the `mpdWorkmate.delete()` service return null. Internally consistent and pinned by a test, but one operation has two shapes for the same field and §D's table is generically worded about \"success (delete, purge)\". Required fix: keep the surface split but make it explicit — either declare `archived: { oneOf: [{type:\"string\"},{type:\"null\"}] }` (PROVEN accepted by this harness validator, so it cannot re-introduce the tree abort) or document \"\"==purged in the tool description + docs. Owner: t3/t4 as an optional small follow-up; must not regress the abort.\nL2 archiving is one-way. Deleted instances are hidden from list/get/read/match and no surface (tool, route, GUI) can restore them — \"restorable\" means manual `mv .archive/<key>-<stamp> <key>`. Consistent with D1 and §F, but t10/t11 must state the manual-restore path; do not describe it as an in-product restore.\nDocumentation item (not a finding): D2's \"full cascade\" cannot see teams of OTHER workspaces while the library is HOME-wide (§M6), and a second dsh process on the same HOME still races a mutation. Both are captain-decided residuals — they must appear in the docs/report, not be silently dropped.\n\nACCEPTANCE (each with citation)\n- §C tools/service: registered names+params verified in the real boot (8be0b0c instrumentation) and probe I0; service keys list/get/read/rename/delete; immediacy verified in I2j/I3f.\n- §D matrix: probe I6a-I6e + test \"routes: §D status/reason matrix\" (200/405+allow/400 invalid JSON/400 invalid-name/404 unknown/409 collision/409 in-use+blocking/400 confirm-required), headers content-type+cache-control on every response, no HOME/tmp leak in any body.\n- §F cascade/delete: probe I2a-I2l, I3a-I3m; a failed post-move step rolls back (test \"an interrupted rename is rolled back\", injected by making index.json a directory).\n- §G read-only: workmate READONLY_DENY = exactly the 7 live write-capable names (write, edit, mpd_hashline_edit, bash, mcp__ast_grep__rewrite, mcp__ast_grep__scan, mcp__lsp__rename), dead names absent from src AND dist (grep count 0), read/glob/grep not denied, adapter forwards toolFilter verbatim (mpd-dsh-adapter-plugin/src/index.ts:320) and roles/workmate parity is a hard equality assertion — read-only authority is NOT widened.\n- §H edge matrix: every row covered by the suite (22 tests) and independently re-driven by my 49-assertion probe.\n\nGATES ON THE CURRENT STATE (my run, .mpd/team/workmate-rename-delete/t7-evidence/gates.log): bun test packages 288 pass/3 skip/0 fail exit 0 · bun run typecheck exit 0 · bun run test:qa all self-tests passed exit 0 · node scripts/verify-vendor.mjs PASS exit 0 · fresh `bun build src→dist` exit 0.\n\nBASELINE (§9): HEAD f697088 throughout; the tracked changes in packages/mpd-workmate-plugin|mpd-roles-plugin are t3/t5's work, unchanged by me; my only writes are UNTRACKED review artifacts under .mpd/team/workmate-rename-delete/ (probes, probe-result.json, boot-probe logs, t7-evidence/gates.log, dist-drift.txt, dist-rebuild-check.js, paths.txt, dump/headless/install logs) — t11 may delete them. I edited no file in the repo.",
evidence/workmate/rename-delete-integration/2026-09-10T14-40-00Z/team-task-records.json:981:          "requiredFix": "Make the split explicit at the tool surface: declare `archived: { oneOf: [{type:\"string\"},{type:\"null\"}] }` (verified accepted by this harness's assertSupportedJsonSchema — it does NOT re-introduce the type-array abort) and return the service's null verbatim, OR keep the \"\" coercion and document `archived===\"\"` as the purge marker in the tool description plus the t10 docs. Do not change the §D HTTP body (null stays correct there).",
