evidence/workmate/rename-delete-integration/2026-09-10T14-40-00Z/team-task-records.json:1087:      "description": "Review the GUI work (t4) as both a contract-conformance reviewer and a UI/UX critic. Read .mpd/plans/workmate-rename-delete-contract.md section D, then the real sources: packages/mpd-bundle-plugin/src/web-client.js (WorkmateLibraryView, the request() helper, WORKMATE_LOCALE_NAMESPACE zh+en, registerWorkmateSidebarTab) and the rebuilt packages/mpd-bundle-plugin/client.js. Cross-check packages/mpd-bundle-plugin/test/sidebar-tab.test.mjs, test/client-harness.mjs and test/team-page.test.mjs.\n\nAttack in particular:\n- does the flow actually let a human rename a workmate and delete one, with archive-first semantics communicated rather than hidden behind a destructive-looking button?\n- what happens to the view when a mutation succeeds, when it is refused because the workmate is in use, when the host returns an error, and when the selected workmate disappears underneath the detail view?\n- are the zh and en key sets genuinely identical, and is the Chinese wording accurate and natural?\n- is the shipped bundle actually rebuilt (the build script fails the build if the removed floater/toggle come back), and does it still respect the seam policy where a declared-but-unregistered service takes the whole page down?\n\nNote on evidence limits: the sandbox has NO browser driver (no chromium binary, no playwright package) — the captain verified this. So do NOT require rendered screenshots; judge from source, tests, the built artifact and the route contract, and say so explicitly in your verdict rather than implying visual verification happened.\n\nYou are a read-only role: report findings, do not edit files. Never end the turn with the task claimed and no output.",
evidence/workmate/rename-delete-integration/2026-09-10T14-40-00Z/team-task-records.json:1099:        "Wire-contract conformance is verified call by call against contract section D (path, verb, payload, status handling, reason branching); any drift is a finding.",
evidence/workmate/rename-delete-integration/2026-09-10T14-40-00Z/team-task-records.json:1116:      "output": "VERDICT: PASS — zero blocker/high findings; 4 LOW findings recorded, none blocking. Reviewed t4 against the CURRENT tree (HEAD f697088 + 66 porcelain). Contract re-read at its full 405 lines (§A–Q, including the §J–Q sections added after my first read); §K and §Q were applied as binding scope decisions, not as findings.\n\nEVIDENCE LIMIT (explicit, per task note): this sandbox has NO browser driver (no chromium, no playwright). I judged from source, the offline client harness, the committed built artifact and the §D route contract. NO rendered screenshot was produced or claimed, and no visual-fidelity claim is made anywhere in this verdict.\n\nGATE I RAN: `bun test packages/mpd-bundle-plugin/test/` → 52 pass / 0 fail / 452 expect() calls, 11.16s.\n\n§D CONFORMANCE, CALL BY CALL\n- Paths/verbs: RENAME_URL `/plugins/mpd-workmate/rename`, DELETE_URL `/plugins/mpd-workmate/delete`, both POST + `content-type: application/json` — match §D exactly.\n- Payloads: rename `{name, new_name}` (test asserts deep-equal); archive `{name}` with `purge` provably absent; purge `{name, purge:true, confirm:<typed>}`.\n- Status/reason handling: `request()` no longer collapses the body — `requestError` carries `status`, `body`, `reason`, `blocking[]`; `failureReason` + `describeFailure` branch on all five §D reasons, and an unknown failure falls back to server text, never to a raw reason key. Tests assert `messages.size >= 5` (no collapse), no `mutate.reason.*` leak into user-visible text, and that a bare \"HTTP <n>\" is never shown.\n- NO DRIFT FOUND.\n\nREFUSAL SURFACING: all five reasons render distinctly; the in-use message interpolates the real blockers, and the test proves both `workmate-rename-delete` and `architect` appear while `{blocking}` never leaks. Degradation when `blocking` is empty/malformed is safe (falls back to a dictionary phrase, still no placeholder leak).\n\nzh/en PARITY — verified INDEPENDENTLY, not taken on trust: 53 keys each, 27 `mutate.*` each, zero zh-only, zero en-only, zero duplicate keys. Chinese judged for naturalness, not just presence: it reads as native technical Chinese (\"目录名即标识，重命名会同步更新 meta、note 与索引。\", \"默认先归档：实例移入 ~/.mpd/workmate/.archive/，之后仍可恢复。\", \"该名称已被占用，请换一个名称。\"). Three wording nits filed as low.\n\nDESTRUCTIVE FLOW (D1): genuinely two-step. The first click on 删除 opens only the confirmation — the suite asserts ZERO POSTs at BOTH confirmation steps (two independent assertions), so \"no single irreversible click\" is proven, not asserted by prose. The archive step states archive-first + restorability with Archive/Cancel; purge is a further step, states permanence, requires typing the exact name, and is disabled + aria-disabled until exact (a wrong name provably fires no request). I specifically chased one suspected hole: the success notice (\"已归档 {name}\") is set immediately before `closeDetail()` collapses back to the list — I confirmed the LIST view renders `notice` (web-client.js:579, role=\"status\"), so the archive confirmation is actually visible to the user rather than silently dropped. No hole.\n\nSTALE SELECTION (§H): a successful rename reselects the NEW key and the LAST GET is `?name=<new>` (asserted on ordering, not presence); delete clears the pane and never re-reads the dead key; a GET answering `reason:\"unknown\"` calls `closeDetail()` — no 404 loop. The page performs no polling at all, so the \"no stale detail polling\" property holds by construction.\n\nSHIPPED ARTIFACT: `client.js` (20:57:09) is NEWER than `src/web-client.js` (20:55:30) and no source file is newer than the artifact. The built bundle contains the new UI (rename/delete routes, `mutate.*` strings, `aria-disabled`). Seam policy intact: `REQUIRED_SERVICES = [\"slots\",\"locale\"]` — betterSidebar is reached only through `ctx.inject`, never declared, so it cannot park the entry; tabs assert `single: true`; no floater/footer-toggle source exists and the build guards are in place.\nI CHASED ONE APPARENT CONTRADICTION rather than assuming: `grep` finds 12 `shell.overlay|agent-teams-activity` hits inside the shipped `client.js`. They are all in the VENDORED `@nanmicoder/dsh-agent-teams` lib (bundled for its views/store/locales/CSS) — the mpd client sources register none of them, and the adopted `apply()` (which is what would register the removed card/floater) is provably never called: the harness stub sets `agentTeamsApplied` at client-harness.mjs:196, so the passing assertion at sidebar-tab.test.mjs:128 is non-vacuous. `team-page.js:427` is a `data-agent-teams-activity` attribute reproducing the panel interior, not a floater registration.\n\nPer §K the hardcoded English tab-strip label is a sanctioned deferral and is NOT raised as a finding (it is pinned by a test); per §Q1 the stale `dist/mpd-package` mirror and per §Q3 the untouched `.qa-reloc`/`evidence/scan` mirrors are likewise not t4 findings — I confirmed t4 touched no mirror (`git status` shows none) and rebuilt only the live `client.js`.\n\nLOW FINDINGS (non-blocking, offered to t11 — no rework required for this verdict):\nL1 `mutate.reason.sameKey` is defined in BOTH dictionaries but referenced NOWHERE in source or tests; §M2 makes the server text authoritative for a same-key rename, so the key is unreachable dead weight. Fix: drop it from both dicts, or consult it when the server omits text.\nL2 zh `mutate.purgeBusy` \"删除中…\" disagrees in register with its own button \"彻底删除\" (EN has the mirror mismatch: \"Purge\" vs \"Deleting…\"). Fix: \"彻底删除中…\" / \"Purging…\".\nL3 zh polish: `mutate.reason.confirmRequired` (\"…输入完整名称确认\") reads clipped vs \"…以确认\"; `mutate.reason.inUse` carries a redundant half-width space before `{blocking}` right after a full-width colon.\nL4 (pre-existing shape, not introduced here) if the detail GET fails for a non-\"unknown\" reason, the pane stays on \"加载中…\" indefinitely beside the error banner; 返回列表 is the escape hatch. Optional: render a terminal error state instead of a perpetual spinner.",
evidence/workmate/rename-delete-integration/2026-09-10T14-40-00Z/team-task-records.json:1158:          "criterion": "Wire-contract conformance verified call by call against contract section D (path, verb, payload, status handling, reason branching); any drift is a finding.",
evidence/workmate/rename-delete-integration/2026-09-10T14-40-00Z/team-task-records.json:1175:          "evidence": "sidebar-tab.test.mjs:349 and :364 independently assert ZERO POSTs at the archive step and again at the purge step. Archive step explains archive-first + restorability with Archive/Cancel; purge is a further step labelled 彻底删除/Purge, states permanence, requires typing the exact name, and is disabled + aria-disabled until exact (wrong name provably fires no request). Wording does not mislead in either direction. I also verified the '已归档 {name}' notice is rendered in the LIST view (web-client.js:579, role=status) so the confirmation survives closeDetail() rather than being silently dropped."
evidence/workmate/rename-delete-integration/2026-09-10T14-40-00Z/team-task-records.json:1223:      "description": "Review the read-only deny-list fix (t5), which unblocked a defect that made every read-only spawn fail on this harness. You did not implement it, so this is an independent review. Read contract section G first — it carries the captain's live-measured correction (BOTH str_replace_editor and apply_patch are unregistered in this profile; the live-valid subset is write/edit/mpd_hashline_edit).\n\nAttack in particular:\n- was the diagnosis correct and complete? Confirm the shipped list against the live registry, and check whether the same class of staleness exists anywhere else in the tree (other toolFilter/deny lists), reporting it as a finding rather than fixing it.\n- is the mechanism robust, or a literal patch that will rot when the harness renames a tool? Judge whether the chosen approach can silently degrade to \"no restriction\" — that would be a blocker, not a pass.\n- does the verification actually exercise the real dsh (isolated home, real boot, real spawn path) rather than a stub adapter? Cross-check the evidence under evidence/workmate/roles-readonly/.\n- did the read-only guarantee survive? The purpose of the list is that read-only specialists must not write; a fix that weakens or voids the restriction is a blocker.\n- does the new QA case follow skills/dsh-qa discipline (SKILL.md case table, --self-test, evidence path, isolated homes, credentials handling)?\n\nYou are a worker role, so you may inspect anything and run commands, but do not change t5's files: report findings instead. Never end the turn with the task claimed and no output.",
evidence/workmate/rename-delete-integration/2026-09-10T14-40-00Z/team-task-records.json:1238:        "Read-only authority is verified not to have widened — after the fix a read-only role still cannot write files (no write/edit/apply_patch-class tool becomes available), and the mechanism cannot silently degrade to 'no restriction' on a future harness.",
evidence/workmate/rename-delete-integration/2026-09-10T14-40-00Z/team-task-records.json:1252:      "output": "t9 REVIEW — VERDICT: PASS (0 blocker, 0 high; 1 medium, 2 low). The read-only deny-list fix is correct; I strengthened its proof with a direct enforcement measurement the shipped case does not make.\n\nMETHOD (independent: I did not implement the roles side): re-read §G/§N1/§R, roles src+dist, roles.test.ts and the QA case; traced the mechanism in the harness SOURCE instead of trusting the rationale; then measured enforcement with a reviewer copy of the case that records each model request's tool NAME SET (t5's file untouched).\n\nCONFIRMED\n1. ROOT CAUSE (source-anchored): the deny list reaches `childCtx.tools.restrict(composition.toolFilter)` (dsh-subagent/lib/index.js:711), and dsh-tools/lib/index.js:2804 throws for any name outside the scope's `restrictableNames` — so one unregistered name is fatal to the whole list, exactly as §G records. BEFORE = the §G live error text; AFTER = my measurement in (3).\n2. THE LIST THAT SHIPS: exactly [write, edit, mpd_hashline_edit, bash, mcp__ast_grep__rewrite, mcp__ast_grep__scan, mcp__lsp__rename] in roles src AND built dist, 0 dead names in either, the workmate package exporting the identical array, roles.test.ts enforcing equality strictly (no skip). The earlier team's `str_replace_editor` claim is RESOLVED as wrong.\n3. ENFORCEMENT (key independent result, table in NOTES.md): parent request 87 tools with all seven write-capable names; the SPAWNED READ-ONLY CHILD's request 81 tools with `writeCapableSeen: []` — none of the seven. Read-only authority is enforced, not merely \"the list was sent\".\n4. PRE-FIX FALSIFIABILITY holds by equality: the load-bearing assertion `filterSent.deny === EXPECTED_DENY` fails on the pre-fix five-name list, and the lane provably reaches it (the re-injected lane creates a child with its filter sent).\n5. QA DISCIPLINE: isolated DSH_HOME (asserted ≠ real home) + sandbox HOME, real workmate fingerprint asserted unchanged, local stub with throwaway key (no real credential), `--self-test` 23 checks passing, matching SKILL.md row; it does boot the real dsh, so no high finding is warranted.\n\nFINDINGS (none blocker/high)\n- F1 medium — skills/dsh-qa/scripts/readonly-deny.mjs: no lane asserts the child was RESTRICTED; with the pre-fix names re-injected the child gets the FULL 87-tool set with no refusal, and the case stays green. Fix: assert the child's visible tool set (recipe proven) and reword the note to what is measured.\n- F2 low — same file / §G wording: the measured pre-fix mode here is SILENT un-guarding, not the loud refusal the contract describes; document both modes.\n- F3 low — evidence-path drift: case writes evidence/workmate/roles-readonly/<ts>/ while §R1 and the delivery listing name evidence/fix/readonly-deny/<ts>/; both domains exist.\n\nVERDICT RATIONALE: pass is permitted with zero blocker/high findings and the shipped fix does not depend on them — the seven names are correct and pinned, the live case passes, enforcement is verified. F1 is the one to schedule before release: cheap, and it guards the exact silent-degradation route acceptance 4 names. Reviewer artifacts: evidence/workmate/rename-delete-core/{probe-enforce.mjs,enforce-probe/run.log,NOTES.md}.",
evidence/workmate/rename-delete-integration/2026-09-10T14-40-00Z/team-task-records.json:1299:          "criterion": "Read-only authority verified not to have widened, and the mechanism cannot silently degrade to 'no restriction' on a future harness.",
evidence/workmate/rename-delete-integration/2026-09-10T14-40-00Z/team-task-records.json:1301:          "evidence": "AUTHORITY verified by measurement: the read-only child's own request excludes all seven write-capable tools (81 vs 87; `writeCapableSeen: []`), and the roles suite pins that read-only roles get the deny filter while workers get none (37 pass / 0 fail across roles + workmate). SILENT DEGRADATION not verified — I measured that it can happen (F1): with the pre-fix names the child gets the FULL 87-tool set and no refusal, and no lane asserts the child's tool set, so enforcement loss would leave every gate green today."
