evidence/workmate/rename-delete-integration/2026-09-10T14-40-00Z/team-task-records.json:1444:          "evidence": "Both files rewritten in one pass (+112/-4 EN, +91/-4 zh). EN now carries: the tool table with mpd_workmate_rename {name,new_name} and mpd_workmate_delete {name,purge?,confirm?}; a `## Rename and delete` section (full cascade: directory key + meta.name + index.json key + note self-reference + renamedFrom deduped/capped-at-10, persona/memory bytes + caps + uses + lastTask + createdAt preserved byte-for-byte, only updatedAt changes, note.md rewritten ONLY for the LEADING `autoNote` prefix); the archive-first delete with `.archive/<name>-<compactUtcStamp>/`, the result shapes ({ok,name,archived:\"<path>\",purged:false} vs {ok,name,archived:null,purged:true}), the ONE-WAY note with the manual `mv` recovery; a `### Refused while in use` subsection (409 in-use + blocking[{teamId,member}], the two triggers, how to clear, and the documented consequence that renaming TO a roster key in use is refused); `## Naming rule (ASCII-only)` (accept iff already sanitized and non-empty, rejected before any fs call, Unicode deferred); the full 10-row HTTP status/reason table + shared headers + lazy registration + no-$HOME-leak; a `## GUI (Workmates sidebar tab)` section incl. the §K tab-strip-label deferral. The zh file is the same content in 简体中文, not a summary. Both keep the switch link on line 3 under the title (verified by an automated 16-file link check in this turn)."
evidence/workmate/rename-delete-integration/2026-09-10T14-40-00Z/team-task-records.json:1459:          "evidence": "AGENTS.md §13 roster entry now documents the read-only discipline as the exported deny list — exactly seven names, identical in mpd-roles-plugin and mpd-workmate-plugin, asserted equal by roles.test.ts — and adds an explicit 'Do NOT re-add `str_replace_editor` or `apply_patch`' paragraph giving the reason (not registered in this profile; the harness validates the WHOLE list at spawn time so one dead entry breaks every read-only spawn; an installed dsh-tool-str-replace-editor package or a dsh-base patch row is NOT proof of runtime registration; `--dump-config` composes rows without mounting them) and the second trap (do not filter with dsh.hasTool — it reads the global view where write/edit/bash answer false, so filtering would silently drop the guarantee). Reason verified true as phrased: packages/mpd-roles-plugin/test/roles.test.ts contains a guard asserting the two dead names appear in neither src nor dist, and both packages carry the same seven live names — checked in this turn. The defect-class troubleshooting row was deliberately NOT added (contract §T3 accepted that revert); the knowledge lives in §13 + the QA case header as §T3 directs."
