evidence/workmate/rename-delete-integration/2026-09-10T14-40-00Z/team-task-records.json:1560:      "description": "P1 — the plugin tree cannot boot, and this is the single unblocker for ALL of the independent verification (t6), in both halves (the rename/delete lifecycle and the fresh-boot deny-list probe).\n\nMEASURED BY THE CAPTAIN twice, after t3 reported complete:\n- `packages/mpd-workmate-plugin/src/index.ts:664` still reads `archived: { type: [\"string\", \"null\"] }` in the `mpd_workmate_delete` output schema; the built copy still carries it too (Reviewer locates it at dist/index.js:822).\n- A FRESH process running `bun skills/dsh-qa/scripts/readonly-deny.mjs` crashes during plugin apply with a stack through `Object.registerTool (packages/mpd-dsh-adapter-plugin/dist/index.js:74:20)` and `new apply (…mpd-workmate…)`.\n- The Reviewer pinned the harness validator: `dsh-tools/lib/index.js:236` — `Array.isArray(type) ? \"<path>.type must be a single type string (type arrays are not supported)\"`.\n- Per contract §N1 this class takes the WHOLE plugin tree down, and `cordis.patch.yml:149/:174` mounts both rows unconditionally, so EVERY profile composing the bundle (headless included) dies on it. Headless is NOT a workaround.\n- t3's earlier \"isolated boot + --dump-config\" evidence did not catch this because `--dump-config` composes rows without applying them. Do not repeat that check as proof.\n\nWHAT TO DO:\n1. Replace the type array with a SINGLE type string, choosing a representation that keeps contract §D honest — e.g. make `archived` optional (drop it from `required`, omit it on purge) or use an explicit non-null sentinel string. Do NOT rely on a `nullable:` keyword without proving it by booting (§N1 measured this harness strict).\n2. Rebuild the dist.\n3. PROVE IT BY ACTUALLY BOOTING a fresh dsh process in an isolated DSH_HOME and showing the workmate row APPLIES (reaching a downstream credential error is acceptable and expected; a JsonSchemaError is not). Then re-run the readonly-deny probe and show the failure signature changed away from the apply crash.\n4. Confirm no type arrays remain in this package's src or dist.\n\nBASELINE: dirty by design (HEAD f697088 plus pre-existing uncommitted work, including VENDOR_LOCK.json) — never commit/stash/revert; report only your own delta.",
evidence/workmate/rename-delete-integration/2026-09-10T14-40-00Z/team-task-records.json:1596:      "verify": [
evidence/workmate/rename-delete-integration/2026-09-10T14-40-00Z/team-task-records.json:1608:      "output": "t12 COMPLETE (attempt 1). P1 unblocked: the plugin tree APPLIES again, proven by a fresh process that mounts it, and the accepted §R1 live probe now PASSES with a real answering child.\n\nTIMELINE (important for the record): the schema fix, the dist rebuild and a first apply proof were already landed before t12 was created — they were my response to the same blocker Deep Worker reported, and your verification at that point was taken from a pre-repair read. So t12 added the two missing proofs on the final bytes (fresh-process APPLY, §R1 live probe) rather than a new fix; nothing was re-fixed, reverted or widened.\n\nWHAT IS IN PLACE\n- src: `archived` declared with a SINGLE type string (`{ type: \"string\" }`, still required); 0 type arrays in src and dist.\n- §D preserved: the HTTP route still emits the contract's literal `archived: null, purged: true` on purge and `archived: \"<path>\", purged: false` on archive, because the core still returns null; only the harness-facing tool surface maps null to the explicit sentinel `\"\"`, which is the captain-sanctioned option. `purged` is the unambiguous discriminator, so the GUI (which consumes the routes) cannot confuse the two.\n- dist rebuilt from the fixed source (verified newer than src, 0 type arrays).\n- A regression test pins the class: no registered output schema may contain a `type` array, plus both the tool and wire shapes.\n- I deliberately did NOT adopt §N1's `oneOf` form during a P1 repair (it is recorded there as a low-severity item for t10/t11): the single-type form is the one measured to apply here, and normalizing on null was not worth re-opening the boot.\n\nPROOF 1 — FRESH-PROCESS APPLY (acceptance 3), evidence/workmate/rename-delete-core/20260910T131805Z-t12/apply-boot.log: isolated DSH_HOME + sandbox HOME, full `mpd` profile installed with `dsh plugin --profile mpd add --store-dir <tmp> <repo>`, then a real boot. 0 occurrences of `unsupported JSON schema` / `JsonSchemaError` / `plugin tree failed to load` / `failed to apply loader entry`, and the rows' own apply-time lines appear (`[mpd-dsh-adapter] mpdDsh provided`, `[mpd-bootstrap] skill corpus served …`, `[mpd-codegraph] init status=no-binary`). Since a failed apply ABORTS the boot, the missing abort is the mount signal. No --dump-config result is cited as load evidence; for the record I also measured that dump-config cannot close this class (with the union back in dist only, the full-profile dump stayed exit 0 + row present while the real boot exited 1 with the JsonSchemaError).\n\nPROOF 2 — LIVE PROBE (acceptance 4), evidence/.../readonly-deny.log: `bun skills/dsh-qa/scripts/readonly-deny.mjs` no longer shows the apply crash — it PASSES (exit 0) with 0 apply-crash signatures and 0 registerTool/new-apply frames: `spawnDriven: true`, `stubCalls: 4`, `positiveOk: \"the seven-name list reached tools.restrict() and the harness accepted it: the child was created and answered, with no unknown-tool refusal\"`, `isolation.realWorkmateUntouched: true`. A broken tree cannot create a child, so this independently confirms the repair. One observation for t5/t9 (not a t12 criterion): the probe's own `reinjectionDiagnostic` reports `refusalSeen=false` when the dead names are re-injected, i.e. the refusal itself is not reproducible in this profile — the positive lane carries the proof, as the probe states.\n\nVERIFY: all three contract commands exit 0 (`bun test packages/mpd-workmate-plugin/test` 26 pass/0 fail; `bun run typecheck`; `bun skills/dsh-qa/scripts/readonly-deny.mjs` PASS). Acceptance list and commandsRun are attached; NOTES.md was updated with the apply proof and the probe outcome.\n\nRESIDUALS / NOT MINE: (a) §R3's `verify-vendor` `skills` treeSha refresh is still outstanding and I stay out of it — `skills/**` and VENDOR_LOCK.json are outside t12's inScope; (b) per §N3 the sandbox holds no usable provider key, so no completed model turn is claimed anywhere in my evidence — my criteria are apply/mount and child-answered, not \"the model replied\"; (c) t5 remains `pending` on the board, which still gates my t9.",
