evidence/workmate/rename-delete-integration/2026-09-10T14-40-00Z/team-task-records.json:1693:      "description": "Repair of finding F1 from t9's PASS review (the review that verified the deny-list fix). The fix itself is correct and shipped — this task closes a hole in the QA CASE's assertions, not in the product code.\n\nTHE HOLE (measured by the reviewer, not inferred): `skills/dsh-qa/scripts/readonly-deny.mjs` asserts that the seven-name list was SENT to `tools.restrict()`, but never asserts that the CHILD was actually RESTRICTED. With the pre-fix names re-injected, the reviewer measured the spawned child receiving the FULL 87-tool set with NO refusal — i.e. the restriction can silently disappear while the case stays green. That is exactly the silent-degradation route acceptance 4 is supposed to exclude, so the case currently cannot fail on it.\n\nTHE RECIPE IS ALREADY PROVEN (do not redesign it): the reviewer's copy at `evidence/workmate/rename-delete-core/probe-enforce.mjs` records each model request's tool NAME SET and showed, on the shipped bytes, the child's request carrying 81 tools with `writeCapableSeen: []` — none of the seven — while the parent's carried all seven of 87. Read that file for the approach; write your own instrumented run under your own evidence path. Note it lives in another member's evidence directory: READ it, do not modify it.\n\nALSO IN SCOPE, from the same review: F2 (low) — the measured pre-fix mode in a fresh process is SILENT UN-GUARDING, not the loud `unknown global tool` refusal the contract described; state both modes in the case header with the source anchors `dsh-subagent/lib/index.js:711` and `dsh-tools/lib/index.js:2804`. F3 (low) — the case writes `evidence/workmate/roles-readonly/<ts>/` while older text names `evidence/fix/readonly-deny/<ts>/`; the declared path wins, so remove the stale reference. Documenting F2/F3 in human-facing docs remains t10's lane (it owns `SKILL.md`); do not edit `SKILL.md` here.\n\nScope: `skills/dsh-qa/scripts/readonly-deny.mjs` and `evidence/workmate/roles-readonly/**` only — `skills/dsh-qa/SKILL.md` and `VENDOR_LOCK.json` belong to t10, and every other package is out of bounds. BASELINE: the tree is dirty by design; never commit/stash/revert, report only your own delta. No type-array schema changes anywhere (this task must not touch plugin code).",
evidence/workmate/rename-delete-integration/2026-09-10T14-40-00Z/team-task-records.json:1721:        "The three declared verify commands stay green on the final bytes (bun test packages/mpd-roles-plugin/test, bun run test:qa, bun run typecheck) and the new assertion is demonstrated by a real run whose raw output is on disk under evidence/workmate/roles-readonly/<timestamp>/.",
