evidence/workmate/rename-delete-integration/2026-09-10T14-40-00Z/team-task-records.json:1743:      "output": "t13 COMPLETE — the case now asserts the child is RESTRICTED, and the assertion is falsifiable. F1, F2 and F3 all landed.\n\nF1, THE REAL FIX: the case recorded what the adapter SENT but never what the child COULD SEE. It now captures every request's tool-name set and asserts enforcement. Measured on the final bytes:\n  POSITIVE lane — parent call#1: 87 tools, all seven write-capable visible. Child call#3: **81 tools, write-capable visible: NONE**, with `structured_output` present (the role's report schema). Raw: `enforcement {ok:true, childRequests:1, childToolCounts:[81], parentToolCount:87, childLeaksWriteCapable:[], childHasStructuredOutput:true, parentHasAllSeven:true}`.\n  CONTROL lane — with the pre-fix names re-injected the restriction SILENTLY stops applying: the child gets the FULL 87-tool set and no refusal, so zero requests match the restricted-child signature. Raw: `reinjectionControl {ok:true, childRequestsUnderRestriction:0, parentToolCount:87, parentSeesWriteCapable:[all seven], refusalSeen:false}`.\n  Why that makes the positive assertion real rather than decorative: a restricted child is recognisable *because* it lacks the denied tools; remove the restriction and the signature disappears. The case also requires `childRequests > 0` and that the parent really shows the seven, so a run that never reaches a child — or one where the parent itself is unguarded — fails instead of passing vacuously. The two lanes cannot both drift green: loosening the signature makes the control lane find a match and fail.\n  HOW I FOUND THE RIGHT CLASSIFIER, because my first two attempts were wrong and the data said so: `deployment:persona` markers do not appear in the child's request (its prompt carries the persona TEXT, not the section name), and the child is NOT a strict subset of the parent — it is the parent's set MINUS the six denied tool names PLUS `structured_output`. I determined that by dumping raw request bodies instead of guessing, which also revealed that call#2 is a session-title side request with 0 tools, not the child.\n\nF2: the case header now states the measured fresh-process mode is SILENT UN-GUARDING rather than a loud refusal, with both anchors — `@deepseek-ai/dsh-subagent` applies the filter only when `composition.toolFilter` is defined (lib/index.js:711) and `@deepseek-ai/dsh-tools` throws only for names outside `view(scope).restrictableNames` (lib/index.js:2804), so a stale-but-known name overlaps and the restriction becomes partly inert with no error. That answers the open question previously recorded as §W3.\n\nF3: every reference to the superseded `evidence/fix/readonly-deny/` is gone from the case and its header (grep count 0); it writes to and cites the declared `evidence/workmate/roles-readonly/<ts>/`.\n\nDECLARED VERIFY COMMANDS, ALL GREEN ON THE FINAL BYTES: `bun test packages/mpd-roles-plugin/test` 11 pass / 0 fail / 140 expect calls · `bun run test:qa` all self-tests passed (exit 0) · `bun run typecheck` exit 0. The real run also PASSes end to end (exit 0) with the payloads above.\nEVIDENCE: evidence/workmate/roles-readonly/2026-09-10T13-44-26.599Z/{enforcement.md,case-result.json,result.json,output.log}.\n\nONE OUT-OF-SCOPE CONSEQUENCE, DECLARED FOR t10 (§Y2 owner): editing the case necessarily changes the vendored `skills` corpus, so `node scripts/verify-vendor.mjs` is RED until VENDOR_LOCK.json is refreshed — and that file is explicitly in t13's outOfScope, so I did not touch it. The value t10 needs, computed with the gate's OWN helpers as the last action (never hand-derived):\n    fileCount: 364   treeSha: 2c11c7a9233182c9f22e74e013aef2a66b31fe1650852ac45f6c8c19c5fef280\nThis SUPERSEDES every earlier figure cited in this delivery, including `ca9dfa77…` and the stale `e51fb02a…` recorded in §Y2 — the lock must carry this value or be recomputed again if any further `skills/` edit lands first.\n\nASSUMPTION WORTH FLAGGING: the child signature depends on `structured_output` being added for the read-only specialist's report schema. If a future harness drops that marker, the case will FAIL (childRequests 0) rather than pass silently, which is the correct direction — but it means the signature must be re-derived from a raw dump rather than patched defensively.",
evidence/workmate/rename-delete-integration/2026-09-10T14-40-00Z/team-task-records.json:1773:          "criterion": "5. The three declared verify commands stay green on the final bytes and the new assertion is demonstrated by a real run whose raw output is on disk.",
evidence/workmate/rename-delete-integration/2026-09-10T14-40-00Z/team-task-records.json:1780:          "evidence": "Submitted with changedPaths (case script + evidence), commandsRun (the three declared commands) and these acceptanceResults. One out-of-scope consequence is declared in the output: the case edit changes the vendored skills corpus, so verify-vendor needs the lock refresh t10 owns; the correct value is supplied."
evidence/workmate/rename-delete-integration/2026-09-10T14-40-00Z/team-task-records.json:1813:      "description": "Independent verification of the F1 repair (t13), offered by the reviewer who filed the finding and who owns the probe that measures it. This is the \"do not approve your own implementation\" step for t13: the assertion's author is Deep Worker, so its falsifiability must be proven by someone else.\n\nMETHOD (already proven to work): `evidence/workmate/rename-delete-core/probe-enforce.mjs` records each model request's tool NAME SET. On the shipped seven-name list the child's own request carried 81 tools with ZERO write-capable names while the parent's carried all seven of 87; with the pre-fix names re-injected the child's request carried 87 with ALL SEVEN and no refusal. Re-run that instrumentation after t13 lands and confirm the SHIPPED case now asserts the same property — i.e. the shipped assertion must pass on the shipped list and must fail in the re-injection lane.\n\nSequencing constraints (binding): this runs AFTER t13; t13's last action is the `VENDOR_LOCK.json` recompute, so measure on those frozen bytes; if `verify-vendor` is red at the moment you measure, that is the known transient fingerprint lag — re-run it rather than filing it as a finding. Do not edit `skills/**` or `VENDOR_LOCK.json` yourself: read-only verification, your own evidence path only.\n\nReport to the captain with the raw per-request readings so the delivery can state that the guard is independently falsifiable, not merely asserted by its author.",
