evidence/workmate/rename-delete-integration/2026-09-10T14-40-00Z/team-task-records.json:1848:        "Re-verifying the rename/delete feature itself (t6 owns that)"
evidence/workmate/rename-delete-integration/2026-09-10T14-40-00Z/team-task-records.json:1852:      "reassignReason": "Assigning the independent falsifiability check the reviewer offered: t13's F1 assertion must be proven able to FAIL, by someone who did not write it. The assignee filed the finding, owns the instrumented probe that measures per-request tool sets, and already reproduced both lanes (shipped list → child 81 tools with zero write-capable; re-injected names → child 87 with all seven and no refusal). Runs after t13, on the frozen bytes, with verify-vendor green at measurement time; read-only, its own evidence path.",
evidence/workmate/rename-delete-integration/2026-09-10T14-40-00Z/team-task-records.json:1854:      "output": "t14 COMPLETE — INDEPENDENT VERIFICATION: PASS. t13's F1 assertion is real and FALSIFIABLE, proven from the reviewer's side on the final bytes.\n\nWHAT I VERIFIED, AND HOW (independent instruments, not the author's word)\n1) The SHIPPED case: `node skills/dsh-qa/scripts/readonly-deny.mjs` → exit 0, `ok=true`, PASS.\n2) My own instrument (evidence/workmate/rename-delete-core/probe-enforce.mjs — a copy made BEFORE t13 that records each model request's tool NAME SET and does not use t13's classifier) → exit 0, PASS, and it reproduces both lanes' tool-set halves exactly.\n3) I applied t13's OWN predicate myself to the shipped case's raw traces: positive lane → childRequests=1, parentHasSeven=true → enforcement.ok=TRUE; re-injection lane → childRequests=0 → enforcement.ok=FALSE. That is exactly the required pair — it passes on the shipped list and fails in the re-injection lane — so the guard is not a green-looking assertion.\n\nRAW PER-REQUEST READINGS (final window, evidence/workmate/roles-readonly/2026-09-10T13-51-14.403Z)\nPOSITIVE lane — call#1 parent: 87 tools, writeCapable=[write, edit, mpd_hashline_edit, bash, mcp__ast_grep__rewrite, mcp__ast_grep__scan, mcp__lsp__rename], structured_output=false · call#2: 0 tools · call#3 CHILD: 81 tools, writeCapable=[], structured_output=TRUE · call#4 parent: 87 with all seven.\nRE-INJECTION lane (pre-fix names restored) — call#1 parent: 87 with all seven · call#3 CHILD: 87 tools, writeCapable=[ALL SEVEN], structured_output=false, refusalSeen=false.\nenforcement         = {ok:true, childRequests:1, childToolCounts:[81], childLeaksWriteCapable:[], childHasStructuredOutput:true, parentToolCount:87, parentHasAllSeven:true}\nreinjectionControl  = {ok:true, childRequestsUnderRestriction:0, parentToolCount:87, refusalSeen:false}\n\nWHY IT IS FALSIFIABLE RATHER THAN DECORATIVE (reviewer judgement, from the data): a restricted child is recognisable precisely BECAUSE it lacks the seven write-capable names; when the restriction silently stops applying the child carries all seven (and loses structured_output), so it can never satisfy the predicate. The two lanes bracket the classifier — loosening it makes the control lane find a match and fail, tightening it makes the positive lane find nothing and fail. I also audited the vacuity guards (`childRequests > 0`, `parentHasAllSeven`), which are sound: a run that never reaches a child, or one where the parent is itself unguarded, fails instead of passing.\n\nSEQUENCING (the one thing that did not hold at first, and how it was resolved): at 13:46-13:47 the acceptance precondition was NOT met — `VENDOR_LOCK.json` mtime 13:37:16 was OLDER than t13's last case edit (skills/dsh-qa/scripts/readonly-deny.mjs, 13:44:19) and `verify-vendor` exited 1 (`FAIL - asset skills treeSha mismatch`). Re-running the gate (four times) cannot clear a stale fingerprint, and `VENDOR_LOCK.json` is outside t14's scope, so I reported it to the captain with the exact remedy and polled: the owner refreshed the lock at 13:50:28 and the gate went PASS. I then re-measured everything in a clean window (13:51:12 → 13:51:38) where the lock is newer than every `skills/**` file and the gate exits PASS both before and after the case run, so the readings above are on the same bytes the lock fingerprints.\n\nEVIDENCE: evidence/workmate/rename-delete-core/20260910T134647Z-t14/{t14.result.json, t14.final.json, t14.log, readings.txt, final-readings.txt, final-window.txt, poll.log, shipped-case*.log, reviewer-probe.log, verify-vendor*.log, t14-verify.sh}. Read-only with respect to `skills/**`, `VENDOR_LOCK.json`, `packages/**`, AGENTS.md and docs — nothing outside my evidence path was written.\n\nCONSEQUENCE FOR THE DELIVERY: the F1 gap t9 filed is closed AND independently falsifiable, so t11 can state that the read-only guard is enforced and that its assertion demonstrably fails when enforcement is absent — not merely that a list was sent.",
