evidence/workmate/rename-delete-integration/2026-09-10T14-40-00Z/team-task-records.json:1884:          "evidence": "Written under evidence/workmate/rename-delete-core/20260910T134647Z-t14/: t14.log (sequencing precheck + both runs + gate), readings.txt and final-readings.txt (raw per-request tool sets, both lanes, both instruments), final-window.txt (lock/skills mtimes + gate before/after), t14.result.json and t14.final.json (structured readings + predicate evaluation + gate state), shipped-case.log / shipped-case-final.log / reviewer-probe.log / verify-vendor*.log, poll.log (the four FAIL readings and the transition to PASS), and t14-verify.sh (the runner). Reported to the captain with the commands and the raw readings, including the blocking precondition and the exact remedy that cleared it."
evidence/workmate/rename-delete-integration/2026-09-10T14-40-00Z/team-task-records.json:1889:          "evidence": "VERDICT = PASS — both halves hold on the final bytes and are demonstrated by the reviewer, not by the author: PASSES on the shipped list (positive lane child = 81 tools, zero write-capable, structured_output present; enforcement.ok=true with childRequests=1) and FAILS in the re-injection lane (child = 87 tools with all seven, structured_output absent, refusalSeen=false → predicate childRequests=0 → enforcement.ok=false). t13's F1/F2/F3 are therefore landed and independently falsifiable; nothing in this verification weakens t9's original PAR verdict."
evidence/workmate/rename-delete-integration/2026-09-10T14-40-00Z/team-task-records.json:1900:          "command": "node scripts/verify-vendor.mjs",
evidence/workmate/rename-delete-integration/2026-09-10T14-40-00Z/team-task-records.json:1916:      "description": "Repair of t6's BLOCKER FINDING (called F1 in t6's report — not to be confused with t9's F1, which is the case-assertion gap that t13 already closed). This is the most consequential defect found in this delivery, and it survived every earlier check because nobody had driven the new tools through the harness's OUTPUT validator:\n\nDEFECT (measured on a real boot by t6, and confirmed by the captain reading the code): `packages/mpd-workmate-plugin/src/index.ts` returns `{ok: true, name, from, renamedFrom}` (line ~437) and `{ok: true, name, archived, purged}` (lines ~467/472), while both tools' `output.schema` declare `additionalProperties: false` WITHOUT an `ok` property (rename schema at ~line 656, delete at ~line 664). The harness therefore rejects every successful call:\n  `tool \"mpd_workmate_rename\" returned invalid output: \"value.ok\" is not a declared property (additionalProperties: false)`\n— for rename, delete-archive and delete-purge alike — WHILE THE MUTATION IS STILL APPLIED. So an agent is told the call failed after the change already landed, and a retry then hits unknown/collision. The HTTP routes bypass that validator, which is exactly why t6's route matrix scored 59/59 while the AGENT surface is unusable.\n\nWHY EVERYONE MISSED IT (record it in your evidence, it is the valuable part): t3's package tests drive a fake ctx; the t7 adversarial probe called the shipped dist without the harness output validator; the t12 mount proof called `mpd_workmate_delete` with an INVALID name, which is refused BEFORE a value is produced, so the validator never ran; and the route matrix does not go through it at all. A valid-input tool call on a real boot is the only thing that surfaces this class — which is what your regression test must institutionalise.\n\nBASELINE: the tree is dirty by design (HEAD f697088 plus the team's uncommitted work) — never commit/stash/revert, report only your own delta. Note that `verify-vendor` is currently RED for an unrelated reason (the `skills` fingerprint is being refreshed in a separate task); do not touch `skills/**` or `VENDOR_LOCK.json` here.",
evidence/workmate/rename-delete-integration/2026-09-10T14-40-00Z/team-task-records.json:1948:      "verify": [
evidence/workmate/rename-delete-integration/2026-09-10T14-40-00Z/team-task-records.json:1963:      "reassignReason": "t15 is a delivery BLOCKER and must start now; its natural owner (Senior Engineer) is busy with t14, and this task must not queue behind a verification. The work is a contained schema-conformance repair plus a regression test modelled on an existing driver: the two new tools return {ok:true,...} while their output.schema declares additionalProperties:false without `ok`, so the harness rejects every successful call after the mutation has already been applied. The assignee proved on t4 that it can extend an existing offline harness and pin behaviour with failing-first tests.",
evidence/workmate/rename-delete-integration/2026-09-10T14-40-00Z/team-task-records.json:1972:        "evidence/workmate/rename-delete-core/2026-09-10T13-49-39.352Z/verify-output-schema.mjs",
evidence/workmate/rename-delete-integration/2026-09-10T14-40-00Z/team-task-records.json:1975:        "evidence/workmate/rename-delete-core/2026-09-10T13-49-39.352Z/verify-before.json",
