evidence/workmate/rename-delete-integration/2026-09-10T14-40-00Z/team-task-records.json:1978:        "evidence/workmate/rename-delete-core/2026-09-10T13-49-39.352Z/verify-after.console.log",
evidence/workmate/rename-delete-integration/2026-09-10T14-40-00Z/team-task-records.json:1992:          "evidence": "CHOSEN: DECLARE `ok` (keep it in the value). Both schemas now carry `ok: { type: \"boolean\" }` and list it in `required` (rename [ok,name,from]; delete [ok,name,archived,purged]). Why declare: (1) `ok` is already in the service results and the §D route bodies, so tool/service/wire keep ONE shape; (2) the package suite already asserts `out.ok === true`, so dropping the field would contradict the intended contract; (3) `required` stops the flag silently vanishing again (the exact drift that caused this); (4) no `render` reads `ok`, so model-visible text is unchanged. Real boot after the repair: verify-after.json 16/16 checks PASS — rename {\"ok\":true,\"name\":\"t15-probe-2\",\"from\":\"t15-probe\"}, archive {\"ok\":true,\"name\":\"t15-probe-2\",\"archived\":\"…/.archive/t15-probe-2-…Z\",\"purged\":false}, purge {\"ok\":true,\"name\":\"t15-purge\",\"archived\":null,\"purged\":true}, with NO invalid-output error on any of them. The same probe on the pre-repair dist produced the defect string for all three (verify-before.json)."
evidence/workmate/rename-delete-integration/2026-09-10T14-40-00Z/team-task-records.json:2012:          "evidence": "evidence/workmate/rename-delete-core/2026-09-10T13-49-39.352Z/ holds NOTES.md (defect, chosen fix + rationale, why every earlier check missed it), verify-before.json/.console.log + boot-before.log (pre-repair boot: all three calls rejected with the defect string while the mutations landed), verify-after.json/.console.log + boot-after.log (post-repair boot 16/16 PASS), failing-first.test.ts/.log (the lock failing on the old shape), gate-sweep.sh + gate-sweep-result.json (all_passed: true, 7/7 gates), dump-config.txt/.err, git-baseline-before.txt/.after.txt (HEAD f697088 both sides). The real ~/.mpd/workmate hash is identical before and after every boot (ce635a4d2d5b3f66…, 5 files)."
