evidence/workmate/rename-delete-integration/2026-09-10T14-40-00Z/team-task-records.json:2068:      "subject": "Refresh the vendored skills fingerprint after t13's case edit (verify-vendor is red)",
evidence/workmate/rename-delete-integration/2026-09-10T14-40-00Z/team-task-records.json:2069:      "description": "The vendored `skills` fingerprint must be refreshed because t13 changed the corpus (its edit to `skills/dsh-qa/scripts/readonly-deny.mjs`), and `VENDOR_LOCK.json` was explicitly outside t13's declared inScope, so its author correctly left it alone. Measured by the captain just now: `node scripts/verify-vendor.mjs` → exit 1, `FAIL - asset skills treeSha mismatch`, `skills` 364 files, lock mtime 21:37:16 (older than t13's case edit at ~21:44).\n\nThis is the §R3 obligation discharged as its own small unit because the owner of the fingerprint work holds the algorithm: recompute with the gate's own helpers, write the value, re-run the gate to green, and record the stability proof. t13's author reports the freshly computed value as `fileCount 364 / treeSha 2c11c7a9233182c9f22e74e013aef2a66b31fe1650852ac45f6c8c19c5fef280`, which SUPERSEDES every earlier figure in this delivery (`ca9dfa77…`, `e51fb02a…`, `81620614…`) — but treat it as a cross-check, not as an instruction: recompute independently with the gate's helpers and confirm the two authoritative checks, because the constant has already gone stale three times while this delivery ran.\n\nNOT in scope: any further edit under `skills/**` (the corpus is frozen until merge except for t10's own doc sync, which must do its own same-unit refresh), and any plugin code. BASELINE: dirty by design — never commit/stash/revert; report only your own delta.",
