evidence/workmate/rename-delete-integration/2026-09-10T14-40-00Z/team-task-records.json:2107:      "reassignReason": "t16 discharges the §R3 obligation left by t13: the case edit changed the vendored skills corpus, so verify-vendor is red (captain-measured: exit 1, skills treeSha mismatch, lock mtime 21:37:16 older than the case edit). VENDOR_LOCK.json was correctly outside t13's inScope. The assignee holds the working recompute method (the gate's own readBytes/listFiles — two hand-derived digests were already rejected) and must confirm with the gate exit code plus the empty stability check.",
evidence/workmate/rename-delete-integration/2026-09-10T14-40-00Z/team-task-records.json:2109:      "output": "t16 COMPLETE — the vendored `skills` fingerprint is refreshed, both authoritative checks pass, and the delivery's last red binding gate is cleared.\n\nWHAT WAS RED: t13's case edit (plus a follow-up comment-only header edit) changed the vendored `skills` corpus while the lock held the previous fingerprint, so `node scripts/verify-vendor.mjs` reported `FAIL - asset skills treeSha mismatch` with `skills 364 files`. That red was mine and expected: t13's declared inScope excluded VENDOR_LOCK.json, so I left it stale and reported the value rather than writing outside scope.\n\nMETHOD — the constant was treated as a cross-check, never an instruction, exactly as instructed. The gate's OWN `readBytes`/`listFiles` were extracted VERBATIM from `scripts/verify-vendor.mjs`, run as the LAST action, and the digest written straight into the lock; an independent re-run afterwards returns exactly the stored value, which is what proves the lock is current rather than pasted:\n    fileCount: 364   treeSha: 1499dc30b80c5a7a377613ea6476601b5092ff8a357eb047922c92e5b2949cac\n    cross-check: recomputed === locked, CONSISTENT: true\n\nAUTHORITATIVE CHECK 1 — `node scripts/verify-vendor.mjs`: commit OK, version OK, stats OK, `asset OK: skills 364 files`, all five other assets OK, `[verify-vendor] PASS`, exit 0. Re-run after the evidence file was written: still PASS, exit 0.\nAUTHORITATIVE CHECK 2 — `find skills -newer VENDOR_LOCK.json -type f`: prints NOTHING.\n\nLOCK IDENTITY: `VENDOR_LOCK.json` mtime 21:52:44, sha256 31388572f84aec6dc3bdb69a935924b0c532786c6baa153fd88815bf566c2688.\nEVIDENCE: evidence/workmate/roles-readonly/2026-09-10T13-56-00.000Z/vendor-lock-t16.md (full gate output, the cross-check, the lock identity, and the ordering rule t10 inherits).\n\nSCOPE: no `skills/**` file was modified for t16 — the change is confined to `VENDOR_LOCK.json` (now inside this task's declared inScope) plus the evidence record. The empty `find` is the operational proof that nothing under `skills/` moved after the refresh.\n\nORDERING RULE FOR t10, which owns the remaining stale text: `skills/dsh-qa/SKILL.md`'s `readonly-deny` row still describes the pre-t13 sentinel-based live method, and because ANY `skills/**` edit invalidates this fingerprint — including a comment — t10's own doc sync must carry its own last-action refresh, or the gate re-reds at the next sweep. I demonstrated that twice in this delivery: a comment-only edit forced a second recompute of what had been a green lock.\n\nNothing further from me; `skills/` is frozen from my side.",
evidence/workmate/rename-delete-integration/2026-09-10T14-40-00Z/team-task-records.json:2118:          "evidence": "The gate's own helpers were extracted VERBATIM from scripts/verify-vendor.mjs, run as the last action before the write, and their digest written straight into the lock. An independent re-run of the same helpers afterwards returns exactly the stored value (1499dc30b80c5a7a377613ea6476601b5092ff8a357eb047922c92e5b2949cac, 364 files, CONSISTENT: true), which is what distinguishes a current fingerprint from a pasted constant. The value did move twice in this delivery (a comment-only skills edit re-red the gate), so this matters."
