evidence/workmate/rename-delete-integration/2026-09-10T14-40-00Z/team-task-records.json:2159:      "description": "This closes the last verified documentation discrepancy of the delivery. Two independent members measured it: `skills/dsh-qa/SKILL.md` was edited at 14:23:38Z (AFTER t13 landed) and yet its `readonly-deny` case-table row still states the PRE-t13 pass condition verbatim — \"the pass condition is a created, answering CHILD plus the absence of the harness `names unknown global tool[s]` refusal\" — with no enforcement dimension (grep for childRequests/childToolCounts/mutationLoaded/EXCLUDES returns 0). So the QA table describes a case that proves the list was SENT, while the shipped case (case hash `ba6b4908…`) actually proves the child is RESTRICTED.\n\nWHY IT SURVIVED: the doc-sync task was explicitly told not to treat that row as stale (§U2), an instruction written before t13 changed the pass condition — so leaving it alone was the correct reading of a rule that had gone out of date. That is why this is a separate task rather than a repair of t10.\n\nTHE EXACT ASSERTION THE CASE MAKES (so the row is exact, not a paraphrase): positive lane — `ok: childSpy.length > 0 && parentShowsAllSeven && childSpy.every((c) => c.writeCapableVisible.length === 0)`; control lane — `ok: mutationLoaded && diagChild.length === 0 && parent sees all seven && refusalSeen === false`, with `mutationLoaded = DEAD_NAMES.every(n => filterSent.deny.includes(n))`. Measured on the shipped bytes: positive child = 81 tools with none of the seven (parent 87 with all seven, plus `structured_output`); re-injection child = 87 with all seven and `mutationLoaded: true`, `childRequestsUnderRestriction: 0`.\n\nALSO RECORD IN THE ROW (or its neighbourhood, if the table format cannot carry it): the pass condition must not be read from the file's mtime — this file carried a NEWER mtime than t13 while still describing the old condition, which is the same \"freshness signal misread as a content signal\" trap this delivery exists to kill.\n\nMECHANICAL RULE, demonstrated four times today: this edit invalidates the `skills` fingerprint, so the recompute is your LAST action and both authoritative checks must be re-run after it — `node scripts/verify-vendor.mjs` exiting PASS and `find skills -newer VENDOR_LOCK.json -type f` printing NOTHING. Current reference state: lock `c66efeef…`, 364 files, gate PASS, stable. `VENDOR_LOCK.json` is inside this task's declared inScope precisely so the refresh is a DECLARED change, unlike the earlier undeclared one.\n\nBASELINE: HEAD f697088, tree dirty by design — never commit/stash/revert; report only your own delta. Do NOT touch `AGENTS.md` (that is the integration task's file).",
evidence/workmate/rename-delete-integration/2026-09-10T14-40-00Z/team-task-records.json:2187:        "`VENDOR_LOCK.json`'s `skills` treeSha is recomputed with the gate's OWN `readBytes`/`listFiles` as the LAST action after the SKILL.md write (never a re-derived digest, never a value pasted from a message), and the evidence shows BOTH authoritative checks passing in that order: `node scripts/verify-vendor.mjs` exiting PASS and `find skills -newer VENDOR_LOCK.json -type f` printing NOTHING, with the new lock mtime.",
